es 6..18 (zstd1), 2..14 (magicless).\n- `ZSTD_getFrameHeader_advanced` L447-551 — every branch:\n  - `srcSize>0 && src==NULL → GENERIC` L456.\n  - `srcSize < minInputSize` L458-477: for `format != magicless` validates the first `MIN(4,srcSize)` bytes against zstd magic then skippable magic (`prefix_unknown` otherwise); returns `minInputSize` (needed size).\n  - skippable frame L480-492: if `srcSize < ZSTD_SKIPPABLEHEADERSIZE(8)` return 8; else `frameType=ZSTD_skippableFrame`, `dictID = magic - ZSTD_MAGIC_SKIPPABLE_START` (variant), `headerSize=8`, `frameContentSize = LE32(src+4)`, return 0.\n  - non-magic, non-skippable → `prefix_unknown` L493.\n  - `srcSize < fhsize` → return `fhsize` L497-499.\n  - FHD decode L502-549: `dictIDSizeCode = fhd&3`, `checksumFlag = (fhd>>2)&1`, reserved bit `fhd & 0x08` must be 0 (`frameParameter_unsupported`, L511), `singleSegment = (fhd>>5)&1`, `fcsID = fhd>>6`.\n  - `!singleSegment`: windowDescriptor byte → `windowLog = (wlByte>>3)+10`, reject `> ZSTD_WINDOWLOG_MAX` (`frameParameter_windowTooLarge`, L517), `windowSize = (1<<windowLog) + (windowSize>>3)*(wlByte&7)` L518-519.\n  - dictID: case 0 none; 1 → 1 byte; 2 → LE16; 3 → LE32 (L521-530).\n  - fcs: case 0 → `frameContentSize = ip[pos]` only if `singleSegment`, otherwise stays `ZSTD_CONTENTSIZE_UNKNOWN` (L536); 1 → `LE16 + 256`; 2 → LE32; 3 → LE64 (L537-539).\n  - `if (singleSegment) windowSize = frameContentSize` L541.\n  - outputs `blockSizeMax = MIN(windowSize, ZSTD_BLOCKSIZE_MAX)` L546.\n- `ZSTD_getFrameHeader` L559-562 (= `_advanced` with `ZSTD_f_zstd1`).\n- `ZSTD_getFrameContentSize` L569-585: legacy first; header error → `ZSTD_CONTENTSIZE_ERROR`; skippable → 0; else `zfh.frameContentSize` (may be `ZSTD_CONTENTSIZE_UNKNOWN`). `ZSTD_getDecompressedSize` L690-695 collapses ERROR/UNKNOWN to 0.\n- `readSkippableFrameSize` L587-601: `srcSize < 8 → srcSize_wrong`; overflow guard on `sizeU32 + 8`; `skippableSize > srcSize → srcSize_wrong`.\n- `ZSTD_readSkippableFrame` L614-636: ret