134`); `ZSTD_MAGIC_DICTIONARY 0xEC30A437` (`zstd.h:143`); `repStartValue = {1,4,8}` (`common/zstd_internal.h:65`)\n- **`g_min_fast_dictContent` does not exist in this version** (grep-confirmed). The equivalent is `minContentSize = ZDICT_maxRep(repStartValue) = 8` computed at `zdict.c:869`.\n- `cover.h:109`/`fastcover.c:109-121` `FASTCOVER_defaultAccelParameters[11]` = `{finalize,skip}`: idx0 `{100,0}`, 1 `{100,0}`, 2 `{50,1}`, 3 `{34,2}`, 4 `{25,3}`, 5 `{20,4}`, 6 `{17,5}`, 7 `{14,6}`, 8 `{13,7}`, 9 `{11,8}`, 10 `{10,9}`.\n\n---\n\n## Structs\n\n### `ZDICT_params_t` — `zdict.h:214-225`\n- `int compressionLevel` — `0` → `ZSTD_CLEVEL_DEFAULT`(3) at `zdict.c:866` (finalize) / `zdict.c:945` (addEntropyTables) / `zdict.c:696` (analyzeEntropy re-checks). Negative levels pass through to `ZSTD_getParams`.\n- `unsigned notificationLevel` — 0 none, 1 errors, 2 progression, 3 details, 4 debug. Used raw as `notificationLevel` in zdict.c; assigned into `int g_displayLevel` in cover.c (`:789`) / fastcover.c (`:559`). No clamping: values >4 behave like 4.\n- `unsigned dictID` — `0` → auto: `dictID = (XXH64(content,size,0) % ((1U<<31)-32768)) + 32768`, i.e. deterministic-from-content, in `[32768, 2^31-1]` (`zdict.c:879-882`, `zdict.c:963-966`). Non-zero is written verbatim, **no validation** (0 impossible, any other 32-bit accepted incl. reserved ranges ≤32767 and ≥2^31).\n\n### `ZDICT_cover_params_t` — `zdict.h:313-322`\n- `unsigned k` (segment size). Required for `trainFromBuffer_cover`: `0` → `ERROR(parameter_outOfBound)` (`cover.c:552`). Must be `k <= dictBufferCapacity` (`cover.c:556`) and `k >= d` (`cover.c:560`). In optimize: `0` → sweep `[50,2000]` (`cover.c:1178-1179`).\n- `unsigned d` (dmer size). Required non-zero. `d <= k`. **cover.c does NOT restrict d to 6/8** — any `0 < d <= k` valid; `d<=8` uses `COVER_cmp8`, `d>8` uses `memcmp` path (`cover.c:685`). In optimize: `0` → `d ∈ {6,8}` (`cover.c:1176-1177,1225` loop `d += 2`); non-zero → single value (odd values fine).\n- `unsigned steps` — optimize only. `0` → **40** (`cover.c:1180`). `kStepSize = MAX((kMaxK-kMinK)/kSteps, 1)` (`:1181`); `kIterations = (1+(kMaxD-kMinD)/2)*(1+(kMaxK-kMinK)/kStepSize)` (`:1182`). Ignored entirely by `trainFromBuffer_cover`. `steps` is overwritten to `kSteps` in each job's params (`:1262`).\n- `unsigned nbThreads` — optimize only. `0` or `1` → `pool=NULL`, sequential (`cover.c:1212`). `>1` → `POOL_create(nbThreads,1)`; **with MT disabled this returns the dummy singleton and `POOL_add` runs jobs synchronously**, so nbThreads>1 is functionally identical to 1 (never fails, never allocates). Ignored by `trainFromBuffer_cover`.\n- `double splitPoint` — optimize only: `<= 0.0` → `COVER_DEFAULT_SPLITPOINT 1.0` (`cover.c:1174`); must be `>0 && <=1` else `parameter_outOfBound` (`:1195`). `1.0` → train==test==all samples; `<1.0` → first `(unsigned)(nbSamples*splitPoint)` train, rest test (`cover.c:609-612`). **`trainFromBuffer_cover` hard-overwrites it to 1.0 at `cover.c:787`** before the check, so user value is ignored there. NaN/negative handled by the `<=0` default.\n- `unsigned shrinkDict` — 0 = no shrink, 1 = shrink. Consumed only in `COVER_selectDict` (`cover.c:1061`). **`ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_cover` forces `shrinkDict = 0` (`cover.c:1184`, `:1263`)** — the field is effectively dead in this version. Unused by `trainFromBuffer_cover` (no selectDict call).\n- `unsigned shrinkDictMaxRegression` — percent; `regressionTolerance = (v/100.0)+1.00` (`cover.c:1030`). `0` → tolerance 1.0 (accept only equal-or-better). Only reachable if `shrinkDict==1`, i.e. currently unreachable from public entry points.\n- `ZDICT_params_t zParams`.\n\n### `ZDICT_fastCover_params_t` — `zdict.h:324-336`\nSame `k,d,steps,nbThreads,splitPoint,shrinkDict,shrinkDictMaxRegression,zParams` plus:\n- `unsigned f` (log2 of freq array size). `0` → `DEFAULT_F` 20 (`fastcover.c:562`, `:638`). Valid `0 < f <= FASTCOVER_MAX_F(31)` enforced in `FASTCOVER_checkParameters` (`fastcover.c:249`). Memory = `2^f * 4` (freqs) + `2^f * 2` (segmentFreqs) ≈ `6*2^f`.\n- `unsigned accel`. `0` → `DEFAULT_ACCEL` 1. Valid `1..10` (`fastcover.c:257`, and explicit check `fastcover.c:654`). Indexes `FASTCOVER_defaultAccelParameters[accel]`; `skip` = dmers skipped in frequency counting, `finalize` = % of train samples fed to `ZDICT_finalizeDictionary` (`fastcover.c:497`, `:602`).\n- **`d` is restricted to exactly 6 or 8** here (`fastcover.c:237-239`) because hashing is `ZSTD_hash6Ptr`/`ZSTD_hash8Ptr` (`fastcover.c:92-97`; `d!=6` ⇒ hash8).\n- `splitPoint` default in optimize is **0.75** (`fastcover.c:629`), forced to 1.0 in the single-shot (`fastcover.c:561`).\n- `shrinkDict` forced to 0 in optimize (`fastcover.c:640`, `:725`); unused in single-shot.\n\n### `ZDICT_legacy_params_t` — `zdict.h:423-426`\n- `unsigned selectivityLevel` — `0` → `g_selectivity_default = 9` (`zdict.c:985`). `minRep = (selectivity > 30) ? MINRATIO(4) : nbSamples >> selectivity` (`zdict.c:986`); then floored at `MINRATIO` inside `ZDICT_trainBuffer_legacy` (`zdict.c:497`). Larger selectivity ⇒ smaller minRep ⇒ more content selected. Note `selectivity >= 32` is UB-ish shift avoided by the `>30` guard.\n- `ZDICT_params_t zParams`.\n\n### cover.h structs (public to static linkers of cover.h)\n- `COVER_best_t` — `cover.h:27-35`: `mutex, cond, liveJobs, dict, dictSize, parameters, compressedSize`.\n- `COVER_segment_t` — `cover.h:40-44`: `U32 begin, end, score`.\n- `COVER_epoch_info_t` — `cover.h:49-52`: `U32 num, size`.\n- `COVER_dictSelection_t` — `cover.h:57-61`: `BYTE* dictContent; size_t dictSize; size_t totalCompressedSize`.\n\n---\n\n## `ZDICT_trainFromBuffer` — `zdict.c:1107-1123` (decl `zdict.h:210`)\n```c\nsize_t ZDICT_trainFromBuffer(void* dictBuffer, size_t dictBufferCapacity,\n                             const void* samplesBuffer, const size_t* samplesSizes,\n                             unsigned nbSamples);\n```\n- Internal path: zeroes a `ZDICT_fastCover_params_t`, sets `params.d = 8`, `params.steps = 4`, `params.zParams.compressionLevel = ZSTD_CLEVEL_DEFAULT (3)`; `notificationLevel` stays 0 unless compiled with `DEBUGLEVEL>=1` (not the case here, `zdict.c:1117-1119`); then calls **`ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_fastCover`** (`zdict.c:1120`). Never touches cover.c or legacy.\n- Resulting effective params: `k=0` → optimize sweep, `d=8` fixed (single d iteration), `steps=4`, `f=0→20`, `accel=0→1`, `splitPoint=0→0.75`, `nbThreads=0` (no pool), `shrinkDict=0`, `dictID=0`→auto.\n- Concrete sweep: `kMinK=50, kMaxK=2000, kSteps=4, kStepSize=MAX(1950/4,1)=487`, `kIterations = 1*(1+1950/487) = 5` → k = 50, 537, 1024, 1511, 1998.\n- Minimum sample count: because `splitPoint=0.75`, `nbTrainSamples = (unsigned)(nbSamples*0.75)` must be `>= 5` and `nbTestSamples = nbSamples - nbTrainSamples >= 1` ⇒ **`nbSamples >= 7`** (6 → `(unsigned)4.5=4` → `ERROR(srcSize_wrong)`).\n- `dictBufferCapacity >= 256` required. Total sample bytes must be `>= 8` and `< 4 GiB-1`.\n- Since `notificationLevel==0`, all failures are silent.\n- Memory ≈ `6*2^20` ≈ 6 MB (docs `zdict.h:204`).\n\n## `ZDICT_getDictID` — `zdict.c:102-107` (decl `zdict.h:269`)\n```c\nunsigned ZDICT_getDictID(const void* dictBuffer, size_t dictSize);\n```\n- `dictSize < 8` → 0. `MEM_readLE32(dictBuffer) != 0xEC30A437` → 0. Else returns `MEM_readLE32(dictBuffer+4)` (may legitimately be 0 for a malformed-but-magic dict). No allocation, no error codes. Reads exactly 8 bytes; `dictBuffer` must be readable for 8 bytes when `dictSize>=8`.\n\n## `ZDICT_getDictHeaderSize` — `zdict.c:109-128` (decl `zdict.h:270`)\n```c\nsize_t ZDICT_getDictHeaderSize(const void* dictBuffer, size_t dictSize);\n```\n- `dictSize <= 8` (note: `<=`, not `<`) **or** bad magic → `ERROR(dictionary_corrupted)`.\n- Allocates a `ZSTD_compressedBlockState_t` + `HUF_WORKSPACE_SIZE` scratch; either malloc failing → `ERROR(memory_allocation)`.\n- Otherwise returns `ZSTD_loadCEntropy(bs, wksp, dictBuffer, dictSize)` = header size (8 + entropy tables + 12 rep-offset bytes), or that function's ZSTD error code. Always frees both buffers.\n\n## `ZDICT_isError` — `zdict.c:98`\n```c\nunsigned ZDICT_isError(size_t errorCode);   /* == ERR_isError */\n```\nNote `(size_t)-1` **is** an error (maps to `ZSTD_error_GENERIC`); this matters because `COVER_best_t.compressedSize` is initialized to `(size_t)-1` and returned when every optimize iteration is rejected.\n\n## `ZDICT_getErrorName` — `zdict.c:100`\n```c\nconst char* ZDICT_getErrorName(size_t errorCode);   /* == ERR_getErrorName */\n```\nValid for any `size_t`; non-error codes yield \"No error detected\"/unspecified string.\n\n## `ZDICT_finalizeDictionary` — `zdict.c:858-937` (decl `zdict.h:262`)\n```c\nsize_t ZDICT_finalizeDictionary(void* dictBuffer, size_t dictBufferCapacity,\n                                const void* customDictContent, size_t dictContentSize,\n                                const void* samplesBuffer, const size_t* samplesSizes,\n                                unsigned nbSamples, ZDICT_params_t params);\n```\nOrdered behavior:\n1. `compressionLevel==0 → 3` (`:866`); `notificationLevel = params.notificationLevel` (`:867`); `minContentSize = ZDICT_maxRep({1,4,8}) = 8` (`:869`).\n2. `dictBufferCapacity < dictContentSize` → `ERROR(dstSize_tooSmall)` (`:874`).\n3. `dictBufferCapacity < ZDICT_DICTSIZE_MIN(256)` → `ERROR(dstSize_tooSmall)` (`:875`). So requirement is `maxDictSize >= max(dictContentSize, 256)`.\n4. Header into a **stack** `BYTE header[256]`: LE32 magic at +0, LE32 dictID at +4 (`params.dictID` or `XXH64(customDictContent,dictContentSize,0) % (2^31-32768) + 32768`), `hSize = 8`.\n5. `ZDICT_analyzeEntropy(header+8, 256-8=248, ...)` (`:889`). Failure modes propagated: `ERROR(dictionaryCreation_failed)` when `ZSTD_highbit32(dictContentSize + 128KB) > 30` i.e. content ≳ 2 GiB (`zdict.c:688`); `ERROR(memory_allocation)`; HUF/FSE error codes; `ERROR(dstSize_tooSmall)` if <12 bytes left for rep offsets (`zdict.c:819`). `nbSamples==0` is *not* rejected — `averageSampleSize = total/(nbFiles + !nbFiles)` guards div-by-0 (`zdict.c:682`) and priors (all counts = 1) still produce tables; the doc at `zdict.h:257-260` lists \"not enough samples / uncompressible / all identical\" as edge-case failures. Pathological non-compressible literals are rescued by `ZDICT_flatLit` (`zdict.c:649-656`, `:731-736`).\n6. Truncation: if `hSize + dictContentSize > dictBufferCapacity`, content is shrunk to `dictBufferCapacity - hSize` — **the beginning is dropped** (the tail is kept, since only the size is reduced and the copy source pointer is unchanged… note: source stays `customDictContent`, so in effect the *tail* is dropped here at `:900`; the \"keep the end\" semantics described in `zdict.h:246-250` is realized by callers passing `dict+tail`). \n7. Zero-padding: if `dictContentSize < 8`, requires `hSize + 8 <= dictBufferCapacity` else `ERROR(dstSize_tooSmall)` (\"dictBufferCapacity too small to fit max repcode\", `:905`); `paddingSize = 8 - dictContentSize`. Padding is placed *before* the content.\n8. Layout `[header hSize][zero padding][content]`; `memmove(content)` first (overlap-safe: `dictBuffer` and `customDictContent` may overlap), then `memcpy(header)`, then `memset(padding,0)`.\n9. Returns `dictSize = hSize + paddingSize + dictContentSize` (`<= dictBufferCapacity`).\n\n## `ZDICT_addEntropyTablesFromBuffer` — `zdict.c:1125-1133` (decl `zdict.h:474`, deprecated)\n```c\nsize_t ZDICT_addEntropyTablesFromBuffer(void* dictBuffer, size_t dictContentSize,\n                                        size_t dictBufferCapacity,\n                                        const void* samplesBuffer, const size_t* samplesSizes,\n                                        unsigned nbSamples);\n```\n- Zeroes `ZDICT_params_t` and calls `ZDICT_addEntropyTablesFromBuffer_advanced` (`zdict.c:940-972`) ⇒ compressionLevel 3, notificationLevel 0, dictID auto.\n- **In-place contract**: the raw content must already sit at the *end* of `dictBuffer`, i.e. at `dictBuffer + dictBufferCapacity - dictContentSize` (`:955`, `:963`, `:970`).\n- No `dictBufferCapacity >= 256` check, no `dictContentSize <= dictBufferCapacity` check. If `dictBufferCapacity < 8` then `dictBufferCapacity - hSize` underflows (`:952`) — caller must guarantee sane sizes.\n- Writes entropy tables at offset 8, then magic+dictID at offset 0, then `memmove`s content up to offset `hSize` **only if `hSize + dictContentSize < dictBufferCapacity`** (strict `<`).\n- Returns `MIN(dictBufferCapacity, hSize + dictContentSize)`, or an error from `ZDICT_analyzeEntropy`.\n\n## `ZDICT_trainFromBuffer_cover` — `cover.c:779-835` (decl `zdict.h:352`)\n```c\nsize_t ZDICT_trainFromBuffer_cover(void* dictBuffer, size_t dictBufferCapacity,\n                                   const void* samplesBuffer, const size_t* samplesSizes,\n                                   unsigned nbSamples, ZDICT_cover_params_t parameters);\n```\n- `parameters.splitPoint = 1.0` forced (`:787`). `g_displayLevel = notificationLevel` (`:789`) — file-static, **not thread-safe / leaks across calls**.\n- Used fields: `k`, `d`, `zParams` only. `steps`, `nbThreads`, `splitPoint`, `shrinkDict`, `shrinkDictMaxRegression` are ignored.\n- `COVER_checkParameters` (`:549-568`) fail → `ERROR(parameter_outOfBound)`: `d==0 || k==0`, `k > dictBufferCapacity`, `d > k`, `splitPoint<=0||>1` (always 1.0 here). **No 6/8 restriction on d.**\n- `nbSamples == 0` → `ERROR(srcSize_wrong)` (`:795`).\n- `dictBufferCapacity < 256` → `ERROR(dstSize_tooSmall)` (`:799`).\n- `COVER_ctx_init` (`:602-689`) → `ERROR(srcSize_wrong)` if `totalSamplesSize < MAX(d,8)` or `>= COVER_MAX_SAMPLES_SIZE`; if `nbTrainSamples < 5` (⇒ **effective minimum `nbSamples >= 5`**); if `nbTestSamples < 1`. `ERROR(memory_allocation)` if any of suffix / dmerAt / offsets malloc fails (~`9 * totalBytes`). Builds a partial suffix array (`stableSort`, `qsort_r`/`qsort_s`/`mergesort`/`qsort` per-platform, `cover.c:326-349`) then per-dmer frequencies.\n- `COVER_warnOnSmallCorpus` at level 1 when `nbDmers/maxDictSize < 10` (`:812`).\n- `COVER_map_init(&activeDmers, k-d+1)` (`:813`) — table of `2^(highbit32(k-d+1)+2)` pairs; failure → `ERROR(memory_allocation)`.\n- `COVER_buildDictionary` (`:727-777`): epochs = `COVER_computeEpochs(dictBufferCapacity, suffixSize, k, passes=4)`; fills dict from the back; stops after `maxZeroScoreRun = MAX(10, MIN(100, epochs.num>>3))` consecutive zero-score epochs, or when `segmentSize < d`, or tail==0.\n- Then calls `ZDICT_finalizeDictionary(dict, capacity, dict+tail, capacity-tail, samples, sizes, nbSamples, zParams)` and returns its result (finalize's error codes propagate). Memory ≈ 9 bytes/input byte.\n\n## `ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_cover` — `cover.c:1167-1302` (decl `zdict.h:374`)\n```c\nsize_t ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_cover(void* dictBuffer, size_t dictBufferCapacity,\n                                           const void* samplesBuffer, const size_t* samplesSizes,\n                                           unsigned nbSamples, ZDICT_cover_params_t* parameters);\n```\n- Defaults: `splitPoint <= 0.0 → 1.0` (`:1174`); `d==0 → {6,8}` else fixed (`:1176-1177`); `k==0 → [50,2000]` else fixed (`:1178-1179`); `steps==0 → 40` (`:1180`); `shrinkDict` forced 0 (`:1184`).\n- Checks: `splitPoint<=0||>1` → `parameter_outOfBound`; `kMinK < kMaxD || kMaxK < kMinK` → `parameter_outOfBound` (`:1199`) — e.g. `k==0` with `d > 50` fails here; `nbSamples==0` → `srcSize_wrong`; `dictBufferCapacity < 256` → `dstSize_tooSmall`; `nbThreads > 1` → `POOL_create` (never fails with MT off).\n- **Quirk**: the `nbSamples==0` / capacity messages use `DISPLAYLEVEL` on the *stale* `g_displayLevel` (`:1204`, `:1208`); `g_displayLevel = displayLevel==0 ? 0 : displayLevel-1` is only set at `:1221` (optimize deliberately turns display down one notch).\n- Per-`d` a fresh `COVER_ctx_t`; init failure returns the ctx error. Inner k loop: allocates `COVER_tryParameters_data_t` (malloc failure → `memory_allocation`), overrides `k`, `d`, `splitPoint`, `steps=kSteps`, `shrinkDict=0`, `zParams.notificationLevel = g_displayLevel`; re-validates via `COVER_checkParameters` and silently `continue`s on rejection.\n- `COVER_tryParameters` (`:1122-1165`) copies freqs, builds dict, then `COVER_selectDict(..., nbFinalizeSamples = nbTrainSamples, nbCheckSamples = nbTrainSamples, ...)`; it measures `COVER_checkTotalCompressedSize` at `zParams.compressionLevel` (0 → whatever `ZSTD_createCDict` treats as default) and keeps the best via `COVER_best_finish`.\n- Result: if `best.compressedSize` is an error (incl. the initial `(size_t)-1` when *no* iteration succeeded) it is returned; else `*parameters = best.parameters` (with `shrinkDict=0`, `steps=kSteps`, chosen `k`,`d`, and `zParams.notificationLevel` **lowered by one**), `memcpy(dictBuffer, best.dict, dictSize)`, return `dictSize`.\n\n## `ZDICT_trainFromBuffer_fastCover` — `fastcover.c:548-614` (decl `zdict.h:395`)\n```c\nsize_t ZDICT_trainFromBuffer_fastCover(void* dictBuffer, size_t dictBufferCapacity,\n                                       const void* samplesBuffer, const size_t* samplesSizes,\n                                       unsigned nbSamples, ZDICT_fastCover_params_t parameters);\n```\n- `g_displayLevel = notificationLevel` (`:559`); `splitPoint = 1.0` forced (`:561`); `f==0 → 20` (`:562`); `accel==0 → 1` (`:563`); converted to `ZDICT_cover_params_t` (`:518-528`, note `accel`/`f` are not part of coverParams).\n- `FASTCOVER_checkParameters` (`:229-261`) → `ERROR(parameter_outOfBound)` on: `d==0||k==0`; **`d != 6 && d != 8`**; `k > dictBufferCapacity`; `d > k`; `f == 0 || f > 31`; `splitPoint<=0||>1`; `accel == 0 || accel > 10`.\n- `nbSamples==0` → `srcSize_wrong` (`:573`); `dictBufferCapacity < 256` → `dstSize_tooSmall` (`:577`).\n- `FASTCOVER_ctx_init` (`:312-393`) same sample checks as cover (`totalSamplesSize >= MAX(d,8)`, `< FASTCOVER_MAX_SAMPLES_SIZE`, `nbTrainSamples >= 5` ⇒ **`nbSamples >= 5`**, `nbTestSamples >= 1`), `calloc(nbSamples+1)` offsets and `calloc(2^f, 4)` freqs → `ERROR(memory_allocation)`. `nbDmers = trainingSamplesSize - MAX(d,8) + 1`. Frequency counting strides by `skip+1` (`:296-300`), reading `MAX(d,8)` bytes.\n- `FASTCOVER_buildDictionary` (`:399-455`): `COVER_computeEpochs(..., passes = 1)`, `maxZeroScoreRun = 10` (fixed, unlike cover).\n- `nbFinalizeSamples = nbTrainSamples * accelParams.finalize / 100` (`:602`) — for accel=1 this is all train samples; for accel=10 only 10%. Then `ZDICT_finalizeDictionary(dict, capacity, dict+tail, capacity-tail, samplesBuffer, samplesSizes, nbFinalizeSamples, zParams)`.\n- **Robustness gap**: `segmentFreqs = calloc(2^f, sizeof(U16))` at `fastcover.c:599` is **not NULL-checked** before `FASTCOVER_buildDictionary` dereferences it (contrast `fastcover.c:487` in the optimize worker, which does check). Also `ctx` is leaked-free'd correctly, but on `calloc` failure this is a NULL deref.\n- `shrinkDict`/`shrinkDictMaxRegression`/`steps`/`nbThreads`/`splitPoint` are ignored on this path.\n\n## `ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_fastCover` — `fastcover.c:617-766` (decl `zdict.h:418`)\n```c\nsize_t ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_fastCover(void* dictBuffer, size_t dictBufferCapacity,\n                                               const void* samplesBuffer, const size_t* samplesSizes,\n                                               unsigned nbSamples, ZDICT_fastCover_params_t* parameters);\n```\n- Defaults: `splitPoint <= 0.0 → 0.75` (`:628`); `d==0 → {6,8}` (`:630-631`); `k==0 → [50,2000]` (`:632-633`); `steps==0 → 40` (`:634`); `f==0 → 20` (`:638`); `accel==0 → 1` (`:639`); `shrinkDict` forced 0 (`:640`, `:725`).\n- Top-level checks (all → `ERROR(parameter_outOfBound)` / `srcSize_wrong` / `dstSize_tooSmall`): `splitPoint<=0||>1` (`:650`); `accel==0||accel>10` (`:654`); `kMinK < kMaxD || kMaxK < kMinK` (`:658`); `nbSamples==0` (`:662`); `dictBufferCapacity < 256` (`:666`); `nbThreads>1` → `POOL_create` (no-op singleton here).\n- **`f` is not