n_t COVER_selectDict(BYTE* customDictContent, size_t dictBufferCapacity, size_t dictContentSize, const BYTE* samplesBuffer, const size_t* samplesSizes, unsigned nbFinalizeSamples, size_t nbCheckSamples, size_t nbSamples, ZDICT_cover_params_t params, size_t* offsets, size_t totalCompressedSize)` — `cover.c:1020`, `cover.h:150`. The `totalCompressedSize` argument is immediately overwritten (`:1050`) — it is a dead parameter. Two `malloc(dictBufferCapacity)`; failure → `COVER_dictSelectionError(dictContentSize)` (note: returns the *size* as if it were an error code — a latent bug if `dictContentSize` isn't in error range). `params.shrinkDict == 0` → returns the single full-size dictionary. `shrinkDict == 1` → loop from `dictContentSize = ZDICT_DICTSIZE_MIN (256)` doubling, taking content from `customDictContentEnd - dictContentSize` (i.e. the tail), accepting the first candidate whose total compressed size `<= largestCompressed * (shrinkDictMaxRegression/100 + 1)`. Caller owns the returned `dictContent` (free via `COVER_dictSelectionFree`).\n\n## divsufsort (external linkage, `dictBuilder/divsufsort.h`)\n- `int divsufsort(const unsigned char* T, int* SA, int n, int openMP)` — `divsufsort.c:1846-1874`. Returns 0 ok, `-1` bad args (`T==NULL || SA==NULL || n<0`), `-2` on internal alloc failure. `n==0` → 0; `n==1` → `SA[0]=0`; `n==2` handled inline. `openMP` is a no-op unless built with `_OPENMP`. Note `int n` caps input at `INT_MAX`, which is why `ZDICT_MAX_SAMPLES_SIZE` exists.\n- `int divbwt(const unsigned char* T, unsigned char* U, int* A, int n, unsigned char* num_indexes, int* indexes, int openMP)` — `divsufsort.c:1875+`. Exported but unused by zstd.\n\n---\n\n## Cross-cutting notes\n- `g_displayLevel`, `g_time`, `g_refreshRate` are separate file-static copies in `cover.c:67,84,85` and `fastcover.c:54,71,72`; `zdict.c` instead uses a local `notificationLevel` variable in each function. Consequence: the cover/fastcover entry points mutate global state and are **not re