ic numbers accepted by the shim (`ZSTD_isLegacy`, zstd_legacy.h:56-86):** exactly three, compared against `MEM_readLE32(src)`:\n\n| version | macro | value tested | zstd_legacy.h line |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 5 | `ZSTDv05_MAGICNUMBER` | `0xFD2FB525` | 75-77 |\n| 6 | `ZSTDv06_MAGICNUMBER` | `0xFD2FB526` | 78-80 |\n| 7 | `ZSTDv07_MAGICNUMBER` | `0xFD2FB527` | 81-83 |\n\n`srcSize<4` → 0; anything else → 0 (default, L84).\n\nTherefore:\n- `ZSTD_decompressLegacy` (zstd_legacy.h:121-193): only cases 5/6/7 are compiled in; 1/2/3/4 arms are `#if`-ed out; unmatched → `ERROR(prefix_unknown)`.\n- `ZSTD_findFrameSizeInfoLegacy` (zstd_legacy.h:195-267): only 5/6/7; else `compressedSize = ERROR(prefix_unknown)`, `decompressedBound = ZSTD_CONTENTSIZE_ERROR`.\n- `ZSTD_getDecompressedSize_legacy` (zstd_legacy.h:89-118): `version < 5` → 0, so only 5/6/7 can ever return non-zero.\n- `ZSTD_freeLegacyStreamContext` (275-298) / `ZSTD_initLegacyStream` (301-362) / `ZSTD_decompressLegacyStream` (366-445): cases 1/2/3 → `ERROR(version_unsupported)` (or `0` for init); case 4 is `#if`-ed out and falls into the `default:` group → also `version_unsupported`; only 5/6/7 active.\n\n**Full magic-number table (all versions, per header):**\n\n| version | header + line | magic |\n|---|---|---|\n| v01 | `/local/home/.../src/legacy/zstd_v01.h:86-87` | `ZSTDv01_magicNumber 0xFD2FB51E` (BE), `ZSTDv01_magicNumberLE 0x1EB52FFD` |\n| v02 | `zstd_v02.h:86` | `ZSTDv02_magicNumber 0xFD2FB522` |\n| v03 | `zstd_v03.h:86` | `ZSTDv03_magicNumber 0xFD2FB523` |\n| v04 | `zstd_v04.h:135` | `ZSTDv04_magicNumber 0xFD2FB524` |\n| v05 | `zstd_v05.h:153` | `ZSTDv05_MAGICNUMBER 0xFD2FB525` |\n| v06 | `zstd_v06.h:164` | `ZSTDv06_MAGICNUMBER 0xFD2FB526` |\n| v07 | `zstd_v07.h:180` | `ZSTDv07_MAGICNUMBER 0xFD2FB527` |\n\nExtra magics in the **active** set:\n- `zstd_v07.c:41` `ZSTDv07_MAGIC_SKIPPABLE_START 0x184D2A50U` (mask `0xFFFFFFF0`) — skippable frames, handled inside v07 only.\n- Dictionary magics: `zstd_v05.c:390` `ZSTDv