city, const void* src, size_t srcSize, const void* dict, size_t dictSize);`\n- L97-98 `struct ZSTDv06_frameParams_s { unsigned long long frameContentSize; unsigned windowLog; }; typedef ... ZSTDv06_frameParams;`\n- L100 `size_t ZSTDv06_getFrameParams(ZSTDv06_frameParams* fparamsPtr, const void* src, size_t srcSize);`\n- L101 `size_t ZSTDv06_decompressBegin_usingDict(ZSTDv06_DCtx* dctx, const void* dict, size_t dictSize);`\n- L102 `void ZSTDv06_copyDCtx(ZSTDv06_DCtx* dctx, const ZSTDv06_DCtx* preparedDCtx);`\n- L104 `size_t ZSTDv06_nextSrcSizeToDecompress(ZSTDv06_DCtx* dctx);`\n- L105 `size_t ZSTDv06_decompressContinue(ZSTDv06_DCtx* dctx, void* dst, size_t dstCapacity, const void* src, size_t srcSize);`\n- L113 `typedef struct ZBUFFv06_DCtx_s ZBUFFv06_DCtx;`\n- L114 `ZBUFFv06_DCtx* ZBUFFv06_createDCtx(void);`\n- L115 `size_t ZBUFFv06_freeDCtx(ZBUFFv06_DCtx* dctx);`\n- L117 `size_t ZBUFFv06_decompressInit(ZBUFFv06_DCtx* dctx);`\n- L118 `size_t ZBUFFv06_decompressInitDictionary(ZBUFFv06_DCtx* dctx, const void* dict, size_t dictSize);`\n- L120 `size_t ZBUFFv06_decompressContinue(ZBUFFv06_DCtx* dctx, void* dst, size_t* dstCapacityPtr, const void* src, size_t* srcSizePtr);`\n- L152 `unsigned ZBUFFv06_isError(size_t errorCode);`\n- L153 `const char* ZBUFFv06_getErrorName(size_t errorCode);`\n- L157 `size_t ZBUFFv06_recommendedDInSize(void);`\n- L158 `size_t ZBUFFv06_recommendedDOutSize(void);`\n- Extra exported-but-unheadered: `zstd_v06.c:2771 ZSTDv06_sizeofDCtx`, `:2773 ZSTDv06_decompressBegin`, `:3493 ZSTDv06_decompressBlock`, `:3567 ZSTDv06_decompress_usingPreparedDCtx`, `:557 ZSTDv06_seqToCodes`.\n\n### v07 — `.../legacy/zstd_v07.h` (**ACTIVE**) — richest surface; adds DDict\n- L42 `unsigned long long ZSTDv07_getDecompressedSize(const void* src, size_t srcSize);` — **only version exporting this**\n- L49 `size_t ZSTDv07_decompress(void* dst, size_t dstCapacity, const void* src, size_t compressedSize);`\n- L62 `void ZSTDv07_findFrameSizeInfoLegacy(const void *src, size_t srcSize, size_t* cSize, unsigned long long* dBound);`\n- L66 `unsigned ZSTDv07_isError(size_t code);`\n- L67 `const char* ZSTDv07_getErrorName(size_t code);`\n- L74 `typedef struct ZSTDv07_DCtx_s ZSTDv07_DCtx;`\n- L75 `ZSTDv07_DCtx* ZSTDv07_createDCtx(void);`\n- L76 `size_t ZSTDv07_freeDCtx(ZSTDv07_DCtx* dctx);`\n- L80 `size_t ZSTDv07_decompressDCtx(ZSTDv07_DCtx* ctx, void* dst, size_t dstCapacity, const void* src, size_t srcSize);`\n- L90 `size_t ZSTDv07_decompress_usingDict(ZSTDv07_DCtx* dctx, void* dst, size_t dstCapacity, const void* src, size_t srcSize, const void* dict, size_t dictSize);`\n- L102 `typedef struct ZSTDv07_DDict_s ZSTDv07_DDict;`\n- L103 `ZSTDv07_DDict* ZSTDv07_createDDict(const void* dict, size_t dictSize);`\n- L104 `size_t ZSTDv07_freeDDict(ZSTDv07_DDict* ddict);`\n- L109 `size_t ZSTDv07_decompress_usingDDict(ZSTDv07_DCtx* dctx, void* dst, size_t dstCapacity, const void* src, size_t srcSize, const ZSTDv07_DDict* ddict);`\n- L114-119 `typedef struct { unsigned long long frameContentSize; unsigned windowSize; unsigned dictID; unsigned checksumFlag; } ZSTDv07_frameParams;`\n- L121 `size_t ZSTDv07_getFrameParams(ZSTDv07_frameParams* fparamsPtr, const void* src, size_t srcSize);`\n- L129 `typedef struct ZBUFFv07_DCtx_s ZBUFFv07_DCtx;`\n- L130 `ZBUFFv07_DCtx* ZBUFFv07_createDCtx(void);`\n- L131 `size_t ZBUFFv07_freeDCtx(ZBUFFv07_DCtx* dctx);`\n- L133 `size_t ZBUFFv07_decompressInit(ZBUFFv07_DCtx* dctx);`\n- L134 `size_t ZBUFFv07_decompressInitDictionary(ZBUFFv07_DCtx* dctx, const void* dict, size_t dictSize);`\n- L136 `size_t ZBUFFv07_decompressContinue(ZBUFFv07_DCtx* dctx, void* dst, size_t* dstCapacityPtr, const void* src, size_t* srcSizePtr);`\n- L168 `unsigned ZBUFFv07_isError(size_t errorCode);`\n- L169 `const char* ZBUFFv07_getErrorName(size_t errorCode);`\n- L173 `size_t ZBUFFv07_recommendedDInSize(void);`\n- L174 `size_t ZBUFFv07_recommendedDOutSize(void);`\n- **Notably absent from the v07 header:** `ZSTDv07_nextSrcSizeToDecompress` / `ZSTDv07_decompressContinue` / `ZSTDv07_decompressBegin_usingDict` / `ZSTDv07_copyDCtx` — they are defined and exported in `zstd_v07.c` (`:3920`, `:3933`, `:4114`, `:2951`) but only declared in the `ZSTDv07_STATIC_LINKING_ONLY` block inside the .c. Other .c-only exports: `:2903 ZSTDv07_sizeofDCtx`, `:2905 ZSTDv07_estimateDCtxSize`, `:2907 ZSTDv07_decompressBegin`, `:2922 ZSTDv07_createDCtx_advanced`, `:3706 ZSTDv07_decompressBlock`, `:3534 ZSTDv07_execSequence`, `:4285 ZBUFFv07_createDCtx_advanced`, `:2792 ZSTDv07_seqToCodes`.\n\n---\n\n## A.3 Valid-input axes for the ACTIVE versions (v05, v06, v07)\n\nCommon to all three: block header is 3 bytes; `blockType_t = { bt_compressed=0, bt_raw=1, bt_rle=2, bt_end=3 }` from the top 2 bits (`v05.c:445`, `v06.c:421`, `v07.c:2660`); block size = 21-bit LE-ish field (`v05.c:3596`: `in[2] + (in[1]<<8) + ((in[0]&7)<<16)`).\n\n### v05 (`/local/home/.../src/legacy/zstd_v05.c`)\n- Magic: `0xFD2FB525` only. `v05.c:2745`, `:2756`, `:3496`.\n- **Frame header is fixed 5 bytes.** `ZSTDv05_frameHeaderSize_min = 5` (`:399`), `_max 5` (`:400`). No variant axis.\n- Byte 4 = frame descriptor: low 4 bits = `windowLog - ZSTDv05_WINDOWLOG_ABSOLUTEMIN(11)` (`:256`, `:2758`); **high 4 bits are reserved and must be 0** else `frameParameter_unsupported` (`:2759`). → windowLog axis 11..26.\n- 32-bit-host axis: `MEM_32bits() && windowLog > 25` → `frameParameter_unsupported` (`:2773`).\n- **No frame content size in the header** — `ZSTDv05_parameters.srcSize` is memset to 0 (`:2757`), so `ZSTD_getDecompressedSize_legacy` always yields 0 for v05 even though `zstd_legacy.h:94-99` handles version 5.\n- **No checksum** (zero `XXH64` references in `zstd_v05.c`).\n- Block types: `bt_compressed` and `bt_raw` supported; **`bt_rle` → `ERROR(GENERIC)` \"not yet handled\"** in both the one-shot path (`:3413-3415`) and `decompressContinue` (`:3592-3594`); `bt_end` terminates.\n- Single vs multi block: loop in `ZSTDv05_decompressFrame` (`:3380`-onwards) / `findFrameSizeInfoLegacy` (`:3484`); `bt_end` breaks.\n- Dictionary: yes. `ZSTDv05_decompress_insertDictionary` (`:3662`) — two modes: raw/\"pure content\" if first LE32 != `ZSTDv05_DICT_MAGIC 0xEC30A435`, else skip 4 bytes and `ZSTDv05_loadEntropy`. No dictID check.\n- Streaming, non-buffered: `ZSTDv05_dStage = { ZSTDv05ds_getFrameHeaderSize, ZSTDv05ds_decodeFrameHeader, ZSTDv05ds_decodeBlockHeader, ZSTDv05ds_decompressBlock }`; `decompressContinue` requires `srcSize == dctx->expected` exactly (`:3540`).\n- Streaming, buffered (ZBUFF): stages `{ ZBUFFv05ds_init, _readHeader, _loadHeader, _decodeHeader, _read, _load, _flush }` (`:3782-3783`) — v05 uniquely has both `_readHeader` and `_loadHeader`/`_decodeHeader` because it re-parses from a `headerBuffer` when input is split (`:3875-3890`). `ZBUFFv05ds_init` → `ERROR(init_missing)`. Out-buffer sized from `1 << windowLog` (`:3896`).\n- Sizes: `BLOCKSIZE = 128 KB` (`:396`), `blockHeaderSize = 3` (`:398`); `ZBUFFv05_recommendedDInSize = 128KB+3`, `DOutSize = 128KB` (`:4004-4005`).\n\n### v06 (`/local/home/.../src/legacy/zstd_v06.c`)\n- Magic: `0xFD2FB526` only (`:2929`, `:3630`).\n- **Variable frame header, 5..13 bytes.** `frameHeaderSize_min = 5` (`:283`), `FRAMEHEADERSIZE_MAX 13` (`:282`); `ZSTDv06_frameHeaderSize()` (`:2911-2915`) = `5 + ZSTDv06_fcs_fieldSize[fcsId]` where `fcs_fieldSize[4] = {0,1,2,8}` (`:417`) and `fcsId = frameDesc >> 6`.\n- Frame descriptor byte (`:2829`): bits 0-3 = `windowLog - ZSTDv06_WINDOWLOG_ABSOLUTEMIN(12)` (`:416`, `:2937`); bits 6-7 = fcsId.\n- **Frame content size axis (4 values)** (`:2942-2945`): `0` → 0/unknown; `1` → `ip[5]` (1 byte); `2` → `MEM_readLE16(ip+5)+256`; `3` → `MEM_readLE64(ip+5)`.\n- **No dictID field, no checksum** (zero `XXH64` in `zstd_v06.c`).\n- Block types: `bt_compressed`, `bt_raw`, `bt_end` supported; **`bt_rle` → `ERROR(GENERIC)` \"not yet supported\"** (`:3545-3547`). `bt_end` requires `remainingSize == 0` else `srcSize_wrong` (`:3548-3551`).\n- Dictionary: `ZSTDv06_decompress_insertDictionary` (`:3802`) — raw-content mode if magic != `ZSTDv06_DICT_MAGIC 0xEC30A436`, else 4-byte skip + `loadEntropy`. Note it reads `MEM_readLE32(dict)` **without a dictSize>=4 guard** (contrast v07:4093).\n- Streaming, non-buffered: `ZSTDv06_dStage = { ZSTDds_getFrameHeaderSize, ZSTDds_decodeFrameHeader, ZSTDds_decodeBlockHeader, ZSTDds_decompressBlock }` (`:2745-2746`).\n- Streaming, buffered: `ZBUFFv06_dStage = { ZBUFFds_init, ZBUFFds_loadHeader, ZBUFFds_read, ZBUFFds_load, ZBUFFds_flush }` (`:3895-3896`) — 5 stages, no separate readHeader/decodeHeader.\n- Sizes: `ZSTDv06_BLOCKSIZE_MAX = 128KB` (`:344`); DIn = 128KB+3, DOut = 128KB (`:4109-4110`).\n\n### v07 (`/local/home/.../src/legacy/zstd_v07.c`)\n- Magics: `ZSTDv07_MAGICNUMBER 0xFD2FB527`, **plus skippable frames** `(LE32 & 0xFFFFFFF0) == 0x184D2A50` (`:3102-3106`) → `frameContentSize` = LE32 at +4, `windowSize = 0` sentinel meaning skippable.\n- **Variable frame header, 5..18 bytes.** `frameHeaderSize_min = 5` (`:60`), `FRAMEHEADERSIZE_MAX 18` (`:59`); size formula `:3084-3085`: `5 + !directMode + did_fieldSize[dictID] + fcs_fieldSize[fcsId] + (directMode && !fcs_fieldSize[fcsId])`, with `fcs_fieldSize[4]={0,2,4,8}` (`:2655`) and `did_fieldSize[4]={0,1,2,4}` (`:2656`).\n- Frame header descriptor byte bit layout (`:2980-2994`, parsed `:3117-3152`):\n  - bits 0-1 `dictIDSizeCode` → dictID field of 0/1/2/4 bytes (4-way axis, `:3136-3143`)\n  - bit 2 `checksumFlag` (`:3118`)\n  - bit 5 `directMode` / single-segment (`:3084`, `:3126-3134`) — when set there is **no window-descriptor byte** and windowSize is derived from frameContentSize (`:3152`)\n  - bits 6-7 `fcsID` (4-way axis, `:3144-3151`): `0` → 1 byte only if directMode else absent; `1` → LE16+256; `2` → LE32; `3` → LE64\n  - window descriptor byte (non-direct mode): `windowLog = (wlByte>>3) + ZSTDv07_WINDOWLOG_ABSOLUTEMIN(10)` (`:2654`, `:3129`), then `windowSize = (1<<windowLog); windowSize += (windowSize>>3)*(wlByte&7)` — 8-step fractional mantissa (`:3130-3133`).\n  - `windowSize > windowSizeMax` (`1U << ZSTDv07_WINDOWLOG_MAX`; 25 on 32-bit, 27 on 64-bit — `:43-45`) → error (`:3121`, `:3153-3154`).\n- **Checksum: yes, XXH64.** `XXH64_reset` at `:3187` when `fParams.checksumFlag`; `XXH64_update` per block (`:3796`). 7 `XXH64` sites in the file.\n- **dictID validation:** `:3186` `if (dctx->fParams.dictID && (dctx->dictID != dctx->fParams.dictID)) return ERROR(dictionary_wrong);`\n- Block types: **all four supported** — `bt_compressed`, `bt_raw`, `bt_rle` (via `ZSTDv07_generateNxBytes`, `:3782-3784`), `bt_end` (requires `remainingSize==0`). v07 is the only active version implementing RLE blocks.\n- Block-size guard: `srcSize >= ZSTDv07_BLOCKSIZE_ABSOLUTEMAX (128KB)` → `srcSize_wrong` (`:3694`); literal-size guards `:3264`, `:3347`.\n- Dictionary: `ZSTDv07_decompress_insertDictionary` (`:4091-4111`) — three branches: `dictSize < 8` → pure content; magic != `ZSTDv07_DICT_MAGIC 0xEC30A437` → pure content; else dictID = LE32 at +4, 8-byte skip + `loadEntropy` + content ref. Plus digested-dict path `ZSTDv07_createDDict` (`:4172`) / `decompress_usingDDict`.\n- Streaming, non-buffered: `ZSTDv07_dStage = { ZSTDds_getFrameHeaderSize, ZSTDds_decodeFrameHeader, ZSTDds_decodeBlockHeader, ZSTDds_decompressBlock, ZSTDds_decodeSkippableHeader, ZSTDds_skipFrame }` (`:2870-2872`) — 6 stages, two extra for skippable frames; `ZSTDv07_isSkipFrame` at `:3927`.\n- Streaming, buffered: `ZBUFFv07_dStage = { ZBUFFds_init, ZBUFFds_loadHeader, ZBUFFds_read, ZBUFFds_load, ZBUFFds_flush }` (`:4257-4258`). `ZBUFFds_init` → `ERROR(init_missing)` (`:4360`). Buffer sizing (`:4388-4406`): `windowSize = MAX(windowSize, 1<<10)`; `blockSize = MIN(windowSize, 128KB)`; `neededOutSize = windowSize + blockSize + 2*WILDCOPY_OVERLENGTH`. Partial-header path returns hint `(hSize - lhSize) + blockHeaderSize` (`:4372`). Skip-frame path passes `0` dstCapacity (`:4419-4421`).\n- Sizes: DIn = 128KB+3, DOut = 128KB (`:4489-4490`).\n\n**Axis summary table (active versions):**\n\n| axis | v05 | v06 | v07 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| frame header size | fixed 5 | 5..13 | 5..18 |\n| windowLog base / range | 11, 4 bits | 12, 4 bits | 10, 5 bits + 3-bit fractional |\n| frameContentSize in header | none | 4-way (0/1/2/8 B) | 4-way (0/2/4/8 B) + directMode 1 B |\n| single-segment / directMode | no | no | yes (bit 5) |\n| dictID in frame | no | no | yes (0/1/2/4 B) + validated |\n| checksum (XXH64) | no | no | yes (bit 2) |\n| skippable frames | no | no | yes (`0x184D2A5x`) |\n| bt_raw | yes | yes | yes |\n| bt_rle | **error** | **error** | yes |\n| bt_compressed | yes | yes | yes |\n| multi-block | yes | yes | yes |\n| dict raw vs entropy | 4-B magic | 4-B magic | 8-B magic + dictSize<8 shortcut |\n| digested DDict | no | no | yes |\n| ZBUFF dStage count | 7 | 5 | 5 (+2 ZSTDds skip stages) |\n\n---\n\n# Part B — Deprecated ZBUFF\n\nAll in `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-iPPPON/c_src/src/deprecated/`. This is a **pure thin shim over the modern `ZSTD_*Stream` API** — no ZBUFF-owned state at all. Typedefs: `typedef ZSTD_CStream ZBUFF_CCtx;` (`zbuff.h:71`), `typedef ZSTD_DStream ZBUFF_DCtx;` (`zbuff.h:123`). Every prototype is wrapped in `ZBUFF_DEPRECATED(\"use ...\")` which expands to `ZSTDLIB_API __attribute__((deprecated(msg)))` on GCC/clang (`zbuff.h:44-59`); `-w` in CMakeLists silences the warnings.\n\nNote: `ZBUFF_compressInit_advanced`, `ZBUFF_createCCtx_advanced`, `ZBUFF_createDCtx_advanced` are declared **only under `#ifdef ZBUFF_STATIC_LINKING_ONLY`** (`zbuff.h:176-209`), but both `zbuff_compress.c:16` and `zbuff_decompress.c:18` `#define ZBUFF_STATIC_LINKING_ONLY`, so they are compiled and exported.\n\n## B.1 Full exported list + underlying ZSTD mapping\n\n### Compression — `/local/home/.../src/deprecated/zbuff_compress.c`\n| signature | decl | def | maps to |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `ZBUFF_CCtx* ZBUFF_createCCtx(void)` | zbuff.h:72 | zbuff_compress.c:54 | `ZSTD_createCStream()` |\n| `ZBUFF_CCtx* ZBUFF_createCCtx_advanced(ZSTD_customMem customMem)` | zbuff.h:195 | zbuff_compress.c:59 | `ZSTD_createCStream_advanced(customMem)` |\n| `size_t ZBUFF_freeCCtx(ZBUFF_CCtx* cctx)` | zbuff.h:73 | zbuff_compress.c:64 | `ZSTD_freeCStream()` |\n| `size_t ZBUFF_compressInit(ZBUFF_CCtx* cctx, int compressionLevel)` | zbuff.h:75 | zbuff_compress.c:105 | `ZSTD_initCStream(zbc, compressionLevel)` |\n| `size_t ZBUFF_compressInitDictionary(ZBUFF_CCtx* cctx, const void* dict, size_t dictSize, int compressionLevel)` | zbuff.h:76 | zbuff_compress.c:97 | `ZSTD_CCtx_reset(ZSTD_reset_session_only)` + `ZSTD_CCtx_setParameter(ZSTD_c_compressionLevel)` + `ZSTD_CCtx_loadDictionary` |\n| `size_t ZBUFF_compressInit_advanced(ZBUFF_CCtx* zbc, const void* dict, size_t dictSize, ZSTD_parameters params, unsigned long long pledgedSrcSize)` | zbuff.h:203-205 | zbuff_compress.c:72 | see below |\n| `size_t ZBUFF_compressContinue(ZBUFF_CCtx* cctx, void* dst, size_t* dstCapacityPtr, const void* src, size_t* srcSizePtr)` | zbuff.h:78 | zbuff_compress.c:113 | `ZSTD_compressStream` |\n| `size_t ZBUFF_compressFlush(ZBUFF_CCtx* cctx, void* dst, size_t* dstCapacityPtr)` | zbuff.h:79 | zbuff_compress.c:136 | `ZSTD_flushStream` |\n| `size_t ZBUFF_compressEnd(ZBUFF_CCtx* cctx, void* dst, size_t* dstCapacityPtr)` | zbuff.h:80 | zbuff_compress.c:149 | `ZSTD_endStream` |\n| `size_t ZBUFF_recommendedCInSize(void)` | zbuff.h:168 | zbuff_compress.c:166 | `ZSTD_CStreamInSize()` |\n| `size_t ZBUFF_recommendedCOutSize(void)` | zbuff.h:169 | zbuff_compress.c:167 | `ZSTD_CStreamOutSize()` |\n\n### Decompression — `/local/home/.../src/deprecated/zbuff_decompress.c`\n| signature | decl | def | maps to |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `ZBUFF_DCtx* ZBUFF_createDCtx(void)` | zbuff.h:124 | zbuff_decompress.c:22 | `ZSTD_createDStream()` |\n| `ZBUFF_DCtx* ZBUFF_createDCtx_advanced(ZSTD_customMem customMem)` | zbuff.h:199 | zbuff_decompress.c:27 | `ZSTD_createDStream_advanced(customMem)` |\n| `size_t ZBUFF_freeDCtx(ZBUFF_DCtx* dctx)` | zbuff.h:125 | zbuff_decompress.c:32 | `ZSTD_freeDStream()` |\n| `size_t ZBUFF_decompressInit(ZBUFF_DCtx* dctx)` | zbuff.h:127 | zbuff_decompress.c:45 | `ZSTD_initDStream(zbd)` |\n| `size_t ZBUFF_decompressInitDictionary(ZBUFF_DCtx* dctx, const void* dict, size_t dictSize)` | zbuff.h:128 | zbuff_decompress.c:40 | `ZSTD_initDStream_usingDict(zbd, dict, dictSize)` (itself deprecated; warning suppressed by `#define ZSTD_DISABLE_DEPRECATE_WARNINGS` at zbuff_decompress.c:16) |\n| `size_t ZBUFF_decompressContinue(ZBUFF_DCtx* dctx, void* dst, size_t* dstCapacityPtr, const void* src, size_t* srcSizePtr)` | zbuff.h:130-132 | zbuff_decompress.c:53 | `ZSTD_decompressStream` |\n| `size_t ZBUFF_recommendedDInSize(void)` | zbuff.h:170 | zbuff_decompress.c:76 | `ZSTD_DStreamInSize()` |\n| `size_t ZBUFF_recommendedDOutSize(void)` | zbuff.h:171 | zbuff_decompress.c:77 | `ZSTD_DStreamOutSize()` |\n\n### Error handling — `/local/home/.../src/deprecated/zbuff_common.c`\n| signature | decl | def | maps to |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `unsigned ZBUFF_isError(size_t errorCode)` | zbuff.h:163 | zbuff_common.c:23 | `ERR_isError(errorCode)` — direct, **not** `ZSTD_isError` |\n| `const char* ZBUFF_getErrorName(size_t errorCode)` | zbuff.h:164 | zbuff_common.c:26 | `ERR_getErrorName(errorCode)` |\n\n## B.2 Valid-input branches / semantics\n\n**`ZBUFF_compressInit` vs `_InitDictionary` vs `_advanced`:**\n- `ZBUFF_compressInit(cctx, compressionLevel)` — level only; a single `ZSTD_initCStream` call. No dict, no pledged size.\n- `ZBUFF_compressInitDictionary(cctx, dict, dictSize, compressionLevel)` — level + dict; 3-step (reset session_only → set `ZSTD_c_compressionLevel` → `loadDictionary`). `dict==NULL`/`dictSize==0` is legal (loadDictionary no-op). No pledged size.\n- `ZBUFF_compressInit_advanced(zbc, dict, dictSize, params, pledgedSrcSize)` (zbuff_compress.c:72-95) — **no compression level**; instead pushes 7 cParams + 3 fParams individually:\n  - `ZSTD_c_windowLog, ZSTD_c_hashLog, ZSTD_c_chainLog, ZSTD_c_searchLog, ZSTD_c_minMatch, ZSTD_c_targetLength, ZSTD_c_strategy`\n  - `ZSTD_c_contentSizeFlag ← params.fParams.contentSizeFlag`, `ZSTD_c_checksumFlag ← params.fParams.checksumFlag`\n  - **`ZSTD_c_dictIDFlag ← params.fParams.noDictIDFlag`** (zbuff_compress.c:91) — the polarity is inverted relative to the parameter name; a load-bearing quirk worth preserving in any port.\n  - `pledgedSrcSize == 0` is remapped to `ZSTD_CONTENTSIZE_UNKNOWN` (zbuff_compress.c:76) to preserve legacy \"0 == unknown\".\n  - Validates via `ZSTD_checkCParams(params.cParams)` (L80); every step is `FORWARD_IF_ERROR`, so it short-circuits on the first bad param. Returns `0` on success.\n  - Its deprecation message is wrong: `ZBUFF_DEPRECATED(\"use ZSTD_initDStream_usingDict\")` at zbuff.h:203 (D-side name on a C-side function).\n\n**`ZBUFF_compressContinue` (zbuff_compress.c:113-130):** builds `ZSTD_outBuffer{dst, size=*dstCapacityPtr, pos=0}` / `ZSTD_inBuffer{src, size=*srcSizePtr, pos=0}`, calls `ZSTD_compressStream`, then writes back `*dstCapacityPtr = outBuff.pos` and `*srcSizePtr = inBuff.pos`. **Return = raw `ZSTD_compressStream` result** = a hint for the preferred next input size, or an error (zbuff.h:98-99). Note the in/out params are overwritten with *consumed/produced* counts, so a caller cannot re-use them as capacities.\n\n**`ZBUFF_compressFlush` (L136-146) / `ZBUFF_compressEnd` (L149-159):** identical shape, out-buffer only; return = `ZSTD_flushStream` / `ZSTD_endStream` result = **number of bytes still left in the internal buffer, 0 when fully flushed**, or an error (zbuff.h:105-106, 113-114). `compressEnd` writes the frame epilogue; if `*dstCapacityPtr` was too small it may return >0 and the caller must follow up with `ZBUFF_compressFlush` (zbuff.h:111-112).\n\n**Buffer-size hints:**\n- `ZBUFF_recommendedCInSize()` = `ZSTD_CStreamInSize()` (= `ZSTD_BLOCKSIZE_MAX`, 128 KB).\n- `ZBUFF_recommendedCOutSize()` = `ZSTD_CStreamOutSize()` (= `ZSTD_compressBound(128KB) + blockHeaderSize + endFrameSize`; zbuff.h:118, zbuff_compress.c:51).\n- `ZBUFF_recommendedDInSize()` = `ZSTD_DStreamInSize()` (128 KB + 3).\n- `ZBUFF_recommendedDOutSize()` = `ZSTD_DStreamOutSize()` (128 KB).\n\n**`ZBUFF_decompressInit` vs `_InitDictionary`:** `_Init` → `ZSTD_initDStream`; `_InitDictionary(dict,dictSize)` → `ZSTD_initDStream_usingDict`. Both re-initable on an existing ctx.\n\n**`ZBUFF_decompressContinue` hint semantics (zbuff_decompress.c:53-70, doc zbuff.h:148-151):** return value is the raw `ZSTD_decompressStream` result, reinterpreted as:\n- `0` → frame completely decoded **and** fully flushed\n- `1` → data still buffered internally, call again to flush\n- `>1` → more input expected; the value is a suggested next input size (hint only)\n- error → test with `ZBUFF_isError`\n\nThis differs from the **legacy** `ZBUFFv0x_decompressContinue` convention (`0 == frame complete`, `>0 == hint`) — see zstd_v05.h:127-129 / zstd_v07.h:154-156 vs zbuff.h:148-151. Same in/out writeback pattern as the compress side (`*dstCapacityPtr = outBuff.pos`, `*srcSizePtr = inBuff.pos`).\n\n**`ZBUFF_isError`:** `ERR_isError` directly (zbuff_common.c:23), i.e. `code > ZSTD_error_maxCode`-style check from `common/error_private.h`; no ZSTD-level wrapper, so it is valid for both the ZBUFF and legacy `ZBUFFv0x_*` return codes (which use the same `ERR_isError`, e.g. zstd_v05.c:4001)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4023,"cache_read_input_tokens":86031,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4023,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01XS1K3BDjwATQcA7xKzok9z","session_id":"73cb0b47-bb13-46d2-9cdb-cbadffb29d99","uuid":"7024bb44-b073-411e-aa5e-21b73ac17622","timestamp":"2026-08-31T10:41:57.844Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Legacy + ZBUFF API surface"}
