`size_t ZBUFFv07_recommendedDInSize(void);`\n- L174 `size_t ZBUFFv07_recommendedDOutSize(void);`\n- **Notably absent from the v07 header:** `ZSTDv07_nextSrcSizeToDecompress` / `ZSTDv07_decompressContinue` / `ZSTDv07_decompressBegin_usingDict` / `ZSTDv07_copyDCtx` — they are defined and exported in `zstd_v07.c` (`:3920`, `:3933`, `:4114`, `:2951`) but only declared in the `ZSTDv07_STATIC_LINKING_ONLY` block inside the .c. Other .c-only exports: `:2903 ZSTDv07_sizeofDCtx`, `:2905 ZSTDv07_estimateDCtxSize`, `:2907 ZSTDv07_decompressBegin`, `:2922 ZSTDv07_createDCtx_advanced`, `:3706 ZSTDv07_decompressBlock`, `:3534 ZSTDv07_execSequence`, `:4285 ZBUFFv07_createDCtx_advanced`, `:2792 ZSTDv07_seqToCodes`.\n\n---\n\n## A.3 Valid-input axes for the ACTIVE versions (v05, v06, v07)\n\nCommon to all three: block header is 3 bytes; `blockType_t = { bt_compressed=0, bt_raw=1, bt_rle=2, bt_end=3 }` from the top 2 bits (`v05.c:445`, `v06.c:421`, `v07.c:2660`); block size = 21-bit LE-ish field (`v05.c:3596`: `in[2] + (in[1]<<8) + ((in[0]&7)<<16)`).\n\n### v05 (`/local/home/.../src/legacy/zstd_v05.c`)\n- Magic: `0xFD2FB525` only. `v05.c:2745`, `:2756`, `:3496`.\n- **Frame header is fixed 5 bytes.** `ZSTDv05_frameHeaderSize_min = 5` (`:399`), `_max 5` (`:400`). No variant axis.\n- Byte 4 = frame descriptor: low 4 bits = `windowLog - ZSTDv05_WINDOWLOG_ABSOLUTEMIN(11)` (`:256`, `:2758`); **high 4 bits are reserved and must be 0** else `frameParameter_unsupported` (`:2759`). → windowLog axis 11..26.\n- 32-bit-host axis: `MEM_32bits() && windowLog > 25` → `frameParameter_unsupported` (`:2773`).\n- **No frame content size in the header** — `ZSTDv05_parameters.srcSize` is memset to 0 (`:2757`), so `ZSTD_getDecompressedSize_legacy` always yields 0 for v05 even though `zstd_legacy.h:94-99` handles version 5.\n- **No checksum** (zero `XXH64` references in `zstd_v05.c`).\n- Block types: `bt_compressed` and `bt_raw` supported; **`bt_rle` → `ERROR(GENERIC)` \"not yet handled\"** in both the one-shot path (`:3413-3415`) and `decompressContinue` (`:3592-3594`); `bt_end` terminates.\n- Single vs multi block: loop in `ZSTDv05_decompressFrame` (`:3380`-onwards) / `findFrameSizeInfoLegacy` (`:3484`); `bt_end` breaks.\n- Dictionary: yes. `ZSTDv05_decompress_insertDictionary` (`:3662`) — two modes: raw/\"pure content\" if first LE32 != `ZSTDv05_DICT_MAGIC 0xEC30A435`, else skip 4 bytes and `ZSTDv05_loadEntropy`. No dictID check.\n- Streaming, non-buffered: `ZSTDv05_dStage = { ZSTDv05ds_getFrameHeaderSize, ZSTDv05ds_decodeFrameHeader, ZSTDv05ds_decodeBlockHeader, ZSTDv05ds_decompressBlock }`; `decompressContinue` requires `srcSize == dctx->expected` exactly (`:3540`).\n- Streaming, buffered (ZBUFF): stages `{ ZBUFFv05ds_init, _readHeader, _loadHeader, _decodeHeader, _read, _load, _flush }` (`:3782-3783`) — v05 uniquely has both `_readHeader` and `_loadHeader`/`_decodeHeader` because it re-parses from a `headerBuffer` when input is split (`:3875-3890`). `ZBUFFv05ds_init` → `ERROR(init_missing)`. Out-buffer sized from `1 << windowLog` (`:3896`).\n- Sizes: `BLOCKSIZE = 128 KB` (`:396`), `blockHeaderSize = 3` (`:398`); `ZBUFFv05_recommendedDInSize = 128KB+3`, `DOutSize = 128KB` (`:4004-4005`).\n\n### v06 (`/local/home/.../src/legacy/zstd_v06.c`)\n- Magic: `0xFD2FB526` only (`:2929`, `:3630`).\n- **Variable frame header, 5..13 bytes.** `frameHeaderSize_min = 5` (`:283`), `FRAMEHEADERSIZE_MAX 13` (`:282`); `ZSTDv06_frameHeaderSize()` (`:2911-2915`) = `5 + ZSTDv06_fcs_fieldSize[fcsId]` where `fcs_fieldSize[4] = {0,1,2,8}` (`:417`) and `fcsId = frameDesc >> 6`.\n- Frame descriptor byte (`:2829`): bits 0-3 = `windowLog - ZSTDv06_WINDOWLOG_ABSOLUTEMIN(12)` (`:416`, `:2937`); bits 6-7 = fcsId.\n- **Frame content size axis (4 values)** (`:2942-2945`): `0` → 0/unknown; `1` → `ip[5]` (1 byte); `2` → `MEM_readLE16(ip+5)+256`; `3` → `MEM_readLE64(ip+5)`.\n- **No dictID field, no checksum** (zero `XXH64` in `zstd_v06.c`).\n- Block types: `bt_compressed`, `bt_raw`, `bt_end` supported; **`bt_rle` → `ERROR(GENERIC)` \"not yet supported\"** (`:3545-3547`). `bt_end` requires `remainingSize == 0` else `srcSize_wrong` (`:3548-3551`).\n- Dictionary: `ZSTDv06_decompress_insertDictionary` (`:3802`) — raw-content mode if magic != `ZSTDv06_DICT_MAGIC 0xEC30A436`, else 4-byte skip + `loadEntropy`. Note it reads `MEM_readLE32(dict)` **without a dictSize>=4 guard** (contrast v07:4093).\n- Streaming, non-buffered: `ZSTDv06_dStage = { ZSTDds_getFrameHeaderSize, ZSTDds_decodeFrameHeader, ZSTDds_decodeBlockHeader, ZSTDds_decompressBlock }` (`:2745-2746`).\n- Streaming, buffered: `ZBUFFv06_dStage = { ZBUFFds_init, ZBUFFds_loadHeader, ZBUFFds_read, ZBUFFds_load, ZBUFFds_flush }` (`:3895-3896`) — 5 stages, no separate readHeader/decodeHeader.\n- Sizes: `ZSTDv06_BLOCKSIZE_MAX = 128KB` (`:344`); DIn = 128KB+3, DOut = 128KB (`:4109-4110`).\n\n### v07 (`/local/home/.../src/legacy/zstd_v07.c`)\n- Magics: `ZSTDv07_MAGICNUMBER 0xFD2FB527`, **plus skippable frames** `(LE32 & 0xFFFFFFF0) == 0x184D2A50` (`:3102-3106`) → `frameContentSize` = LE32 at +4, `windowSize = 0` sentinel meaning skippable.\n- **Variable frame header, 5..18 bytes.** `frameHeaderSize_min = 5` (`:60`), `FRAMEHEADERSIZE_MAX 18` (`:59`); size formula `:3084-3085`: `5 + !directMode + did_fieldSize[dictID] + fcs_fieldSize[fcsId] + (directMode && !fcs_fieldSize[fcsId])`, with `fcs_fieldSize[4]={0,2,4,8}` (`:2655`) and `did_fieldSize[4]={0,1,2,4}` (`:2656`).\n- Frame header descriptor byte bit layout (`:2980-2994`, parsed `:3117-3152`):\n  - bits 0-1 `dictIDSizeCode` → dictID field of 0/1/2/4 bytes (4-way axis, `:3136-3143`)\n  - bit 2 `checksumFlag` (`:3118`)\n  - bit 5 `directMode` / single-segment (`:3084`, `:3126-3134`) — when set there is **no window-descriptor byte** and windowSize is derived from frameContentSize (`:3152`)\n  - bits 6-7 `fcsID` (4-way axis, `:3144-3151`): `0` → 1 byte only if directMode else absent; `1` → LE16+256; `2` → LE32; `3` → LE64\n  - window descriptor byte (non-direct mode): `windowLog = (wlByte>>3) + ZSTDv07_WINDOWLOG_ABSOLUTEMIN(10)` (`:2654`, `:3129`), then `windowSize = (1<<windowLog); windowSize += (windowSize>>3)*(wlByte&7)` — 8-step fractional mantissa (`:3130-3133`).\n  - `windowSize > windowSizeMax` (`1U << ZSTDv07_WINDOWLOG_MAX`; 25 on 32-bit, 27 on 64-bit — `:43-45`) → error (`:3121`, `:3153-3154`).\n- **Checksum: yes, XXH64.** `XXH64_reset` at `:3187` when `fParams.checksumFlag`; `XXH64_update` per block (`:3796`). 7 `XXH64` sites in the file.\n- **dictID validation:** `:3186` `if (dctx->fParams.dictID && (dctx->dictID != dctx->fParams.dictID)) return ERROR(dictionary_wrong);`\n- Block types: **all four supported** — `bt_compressed`, `bt_raw`, `bt_rle` (via `ZSTDv07_generateNxBytes`, `:3782-3784`), `bt_end` (requires `remainingSize==0`). v07 is the only active version implementing RLE blocks.\n- Block-size guard: `srcSize >= ZSTDv07_BLOCKSIZE_ABSOLUTEMAX (128KB)` → `srcSize_wrong` (`:3694`); literal-size guards `:3264`, `:3347`.\n- Dictionary: `ZSTDv07_decompress_insertDictionary` (`:4091-4111`) — three branches: `dictSize < 8` → pure content; magic != `ZSTDv07_DICT_MAGIC 0xEC30A437` → pure content; else dictID = LE32 at +4, 8-byte skip + `loadEntropy` + content ref. Plus digested-dict path `ZSTDv07_createDDict` (`:4172`) / `decompress_usingDDict`.\n- Streaming, non-buffered: `ZSTDv07_dStage = { ZSTDds_getFrameHeaderSize, ZSTDds_decodeFrameHeader, ZSTDds_decodeBlockHeader, ZSTDds_decompressBlock, ZSTDds_decodeSkippableHeader, ZSTDds_skipFrame }` (`:2870-2872`) — 6 stages, two extra for skippable frames; `ZSTDv07_isSkipFrame` at `:3927`.\n- Streaming, buffered: `ZBUFFv07_dStage = { ZBUFFds_init, ZBUFFds_loadHeader, ZBUFFds_read, ZBUFFds_load, ZBUFFds_flush }` (`:4257-4258`). `ZBUFFds_init` → `ERROR(init_missing)` (`:4360`). Buffer sizing (`:4388-4406`): `windowSize = MAX(windowSize, 1<<10)`; `blockSize = MIN(windowSize, 128KB)`; `neededOutSize = windowSize + blockSize + 2*WILDCOPY_OVERLENGTH`. Partial-header path returns hint `(hSize - lhSize) + blockHeaderSize` (`:4372`). Skip-frame path passes `0` dstCapacity (`:4419-4421`).\n- Sizes: DIn = 128KB+3, DOut = 128KB (`:4489-4490`).\n\n**Axis summary table (active versions):**\n\n| axis | v05 | v06 | v07 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| frame header size | fixed 5 | 5..13 | 5..18 |\n| windowLog base / range | 11, 4 bits | 12, 4 bits | 10, 5 bits + 3-bit fractional |\n| frameContentSize in header | none | 4-way (0/1/2/8 B) | 4-way (0/2/4/8 B) + directMode 1 B |\n| single-segment / directMode | no | no | yes (bit 5) |\n| dictID in frame | no | no | yes (0/1/2/4 B) + validated |\n| checksum (XXH64) | no | no | yes (bit 2) |\n| skippable frames | no | no | yes (`0x184D2A5x`) |\n| bt_raw | yes | yes | yes |\n| bt_rle | **error** | **error** | yes |\n| bt_compressed | yes | yes | yes |\n| multi-block | yes | yes | yes |\n| dict raw vs entropy | 4-B magic | 4-B magic | 8-B magic + dictSize<8 shortcut |\n| digested DDict | no | no | yes |\n| ZBUFF dStage count | 7 | 5 | 5 (+2 ZSTDds skip stages) |\n\n---\n\n# Part B — Deprecated ZBUFF\n\nAll in `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-iPPPON/c_src/src/deprecated/`. This is a **pure thin shim over the modern `ZSTD_*Stream` API** — no ZBUFF-owned state at all. Typedefs: `typedef ZSTD_CStream ZBUFF_CCtx;` (`zbuff.h:71`), `typedef ZSTD_DStream ZBUFF_DCtx;` (`zbuff.h:123`). Every prototype is wrapped in `ZBUFF_DEPRECATED(\"use ...\")` which expands to `ZSTDLIB_API __attribute__((deprecated(msg)))` on GCC/clang (`zbuff.h:44-59`); `-w` in CMakeLists silences the warnings.\n\nNote: `ZBUFF_compressInit_advanced`, `ZBUFF_createCCtx_advanced`, `ZBUFF_createDCtx_advanced` are declared **only under `#ifdef ZBUFF_STATIC_LINKING_ONLY`** (`zbuff.h:176-209`), but both `zbuff_compress.c:16` and `zbuff_decompress.c:18` `#define ZBUFF_STATIC_LINKING_ONLY`, so they are compiled and exported.\n\n## B.1 Full exported list + underlying ZSTD mapping\n\n### Compression — `/local/home/.../src/deprecated/zbuff_compress.c`\n| signature | decl | def | maps to |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `ZBUFF_CCtx* ZBUFF_createCCtx(void)` | zbuff.h:72 | zbuff_compress.c:54 | `ZSTD_createCStream()` |\n| `ZBUFF_CCtx* ZBUFF_createCCtx_advanced(ZSTD_customMem customMem)` | zbuff.h:195 | zbuff_compress.c:59 | `ZSTD_createCStream_advanced(customMem)` |\n| `size_t ZBUFF_freeCCtx(ZBUFF_CCtx* cctx)` | zbuff.h:73 | zbuff_compress.c:64 | `ZSTD_freeCStream()` |\n| `size_t ZBUFF_compressInit(ZBUFF_CCtx* cctx, int compressionLevel)` | zbuff.h:75 | zbuff_compress.c:105 | `ZSTD_initCStream(zbc, compressionLevel)` |\n| `size_t ZBUFF_compressInitDictionary(ZBUFF_CCtx* cctx, const void* dict, size_t dictSize, int compressionLevel)` | zbuff.h:76 | zbuff_compress.c:97 | `ZSTD_CCtx_reset(ZSTD_reset_session_only)` + `ZSTD_CCtx_setParameter(ZSTD_c_compressionLevel)` + `ZSTD_CCtx_loadDictionary` |\n| `size_t ZBUFF_compressInit_advanced(ZBUFF_CCtx* zbc, const void* dict, size_t dictSize, ZSTD_parameters params, unsigned long long pledgedSrcSize)` | zbuff.h:203-205 | zbuff_compress.c:72 | see below |\n| `size_t ZBUFF_compressContinue(ZBUFF_CCtx* cctx, void* dst, size_t* dstCapacityPtr, const void* src, size_t* srcSizePtr)` | zbuff.h:78 | zbuff_compress.c:113 | `ZSTD_compressStream` |\n| `size_t ZBUFF_compressFlush(ZBUFF_CCtx* cctx, void* dst, size_t* dstCapacityPtr)` | zbuff.h:79 | zbuff_compress.c:136 | `ZSTD_flushStream` |\n| `size_t ZBUFF_compressEnd(ZBUFF_CCtx* cctx, void* dst, size_t* dstCapacityPtr)` | zbuff.h:80 | zbuff_compress.c:149 | `ZSTD_endStream` |\n| `size_t ZBUFF_recommendedCInSize(void)` | zbuff.h:168 | zbuff_compress.c:166 | `ZSTD_CStreamInSize()` |\n| `size_t ZBUFF_recommendedCOutSize(void)` | zbuff.h:169 | zbuff_compress.c:167 | `ZSTD_CStreamOutSize()` |\n\n### Decompression — `/local/home/.../src/deprecated/zbuff_decompress.c`\n| signature | decl | def | maps to |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `ZBUFF_DCtx* ZBUFF_createDCtx(void)` | zbuff.h:124 | zbuff_decompress.c:22 | `ZSTD_createDStream()` |\n| `ZBUFF_DCtx* ZBUFF_createDCtx_advanced(ZSTD_customMem customMem)` | zbuff.h:199 | zbuff_decompress.c:27 | `ZSTD_createDStream_advanced(customMem)` |\n| `size_t ZBUFF_freeDCtx(ZBUFF_DCtx* dctx)` | zbuff.h:125 | zbuff_decompress.c:32 | `ZSTD_freeDStream()` |\n| `size_t ZBUFF_decompressInit(ZBUFF_DCtx* dctx)` | zbuff.h:127 | zbuff_decompress.c:45 | `ZSTD_initDStream(zbd)` |\n| `size_t ZBUFF_decompressInitDictionary(ZBUFF_DCtx* dctx, const void* dict, size_t dictSize)` | zbuff.h:128 | zbuff_decompress.c:40 | `ZSTD_initDStream_usingDict(zbd, dict, dictSize)` (itself deprecated; warning suppressed by `#define ZSTD_DISABLE_DEPRECATE_WARNINGS` at zbuff_decompress.c:16) |\n| `size_t ZBUFF_decompressContinue(ZBUFF_DCtx* dctx, void* dst, size_t* dstCapacityPtr, const void* src, size_t* srcSizePtr)` | zbuff.h:130-132 | zbuff_decompress.c:53 | `ZSTD_decompressStream` |\n| `size_t ZBUFF_recommendedDInSize(void)` | zbuff.h:170 | zbuff_decompress.c:76 | `ZSTD_DStreamInSize()` |\n| `size_t ZBUFF_recommendedDOutSize(void)` | zbuff.h:171 | zbuff_decompress.c:77 | `ZSTD_DStreamOutSize()` |\n\n### Error handling — `/local/home/.../src/deprecated/zbuff_common.c`\n| signature | decl | def | maps to |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `unsigned ZBUFF_isError(size_t errorCode)` | zbuff.h:163 | zbuff_common.c:23 | `ERR_isError(errorCode)` — direct, **not** `ZSTD_isError` |\n| `const char* ZBUFF_getErrorName(size_t errorCode)` | zbuff.h:164 | zbuff_common.c:26 | `ERR_getErrorName(errorCode)` |\n\n## B.2 Valid-input branches / semantics\n\n**`ZBUFF_compressInit` vs `_InitDictionary` vs `_advanced`:**\n- `ZBUFF_compressInit(cctx, compressionLevel)` — level only; a single `ZSTD_initCStream` call. No dict, no pledged size.\n- `ZBUFF_compressInitDictionary(cctx, dict, dictSize, compressionLevel)` — level + dict; 3-step (reset session_only → set `ZSTD_c_compressionLevel` → `loadDictionary`). `dict==NULL`/`dictSize==0` is legal (loadDictionary no-op). No pledged size.\n- `ZBUFF_compressInit_advanced(zbc, dict, dictSize, params, pledgedSrcSize)` (zbuff_compress.c:72-95) — **no compression level**; instead pushes 7 cParams + 3 fParams individually:\n  - `ZSTD_c_windowLog, ZSTD_c_hashLog, ZSTD_c_chainLog, ZSTD_c_searchLog, ZSTD_c_minMatch, ZSTD_c_targetLength, ZSTD_c_strategy`\n  - `ZSTD_c_contentSizeFlag ← params.fParams.contentSizeFlag`, `ZSTD_c_checksumFlag ← params.fParams.checksumFlag`\n  - **`ZSTD_c_dictIDFlag ← params.fParams.noDictIDFlag`** (zbuff_compress.c:91) — the polarity is inverted relative to the parameter name; a load-bearing quirk worth preserving in any port.\n  - `pledgedSrcSize == 0` is remapped to `ZSTD_CONTENTSIZE_UNKNOWN` (zbuff_compress.c:76) to preserve legacy \"0 == unknown\".\n  - Validates via `ZSTD_checkCParams(params.cParams)` (L80); every step is `FORWARD_IF_ERROR`, so it short-circuits on the first bad param. Returns `0` on success.\n  - Its deprecation message is wrong: `ZBUFF_DEPRECATED(\"use ZSTD_initDStream_usingDict\")` at zbuff.h:203 (D-side name on a C-side function).\n\n**`ZBUFF_compressContinue` (zbuff_compress.c:113-130):** builds `ZSTD_outBuffer{dst, size=*dstCapacityPtr, pos=0}` / `ZSTD_inBuffer{src, size=*srcSizePtr, pos=0}`, calls `ZSTD_compressStream`, then writes back `*dstCapacityPtr = outBuff.pos` and `*srcSizePtr = inBuff.pos`. **Return = raw `ZSTD_compressStream` result** = a hint for the preferred next input size, or an error (zbuff.h:98-99). Note the in/out params are overwritten with *consumed/produced* counts, so a caller cannot re-use them as capacities.\n\n**`ZBUFF_compressFlush` (L136-146) / `ZBUFF_compressEnd` (L149-159):** identical shape, out-buffer only; return = `ZSTD_flushStream` / `ZSTD_endStream` result = **number of bytes still left in the internal buffer, 0 when fully flushed**, or an error (zbuff.h:105-106, 113-114). `compressEnd` writes the frame epilogue; if `*dstCapacityPtr` was too small it may return >0 and the caller must follow up with `ZBUFF_compressFlush` (zbuff.h:111-112).\n\n**Buffer-size hints:**\n- `ZBUFF_recommendedCInSize()` = `ZSTD_CStreamInSize()` (= `ZSTD_BLOCKSIZE_MAX`, 128 KB).\n- `ZBUFF_recommendedCOutSize()` = `ZSTD_CStreamOutSize()` (= `ZSTD_compressBound(128KB) + blockHeaderSize + endFrameSize`; zbuff.h:118, zbuff_compress.c:51).\n- `ZBUFF_recommendedDInSize()` = `ZSTD_DStreamInSize()` (128 KB + 3).\n- `ZBUFF_recommendedDOutSize()` = `ZSTD_DStreamOutSize()` (128 KB).\n\n**`ZBUFF_decompressInit` vs `_InitDictionary`:** `_Init` → `ZSTD_initDStream`; `_InitDictionary(dict,dictSize)` → `ZSTD_initDStream_usingDict`. Both re-initable on an existing ctx.\n\n**`ZBUFF_decompressContinue` hint semantics (zbuff_decompress.c:53-70, doc zbuff.h:148-151):** return value is the raw `ZSTD_decompressStream` result, reinterpreted as:\n- `0` → frame completely decoded **and** fully flushed\n- `1` → data still buffered internally, call again to flush\n- `>1` → more input expected; the value is a suggested next input size (hint only)\n- error → test with `ZBUFF_isError`\n\nThis differs from the **legacy** `ZBUFFv0x_decompressContinue` convention (`0 == frame complete`, `>0 == hint`) — see zstd_v05.h:127-129 / zstd_v07.h:154-156 vs zbuff.h:148-151. Same in/out writeback pattern as the compress side (`*dstCapacityPtr = outBuff.pos`, `*srcSizePtr = inBuff.pos`).\n\n**`ZBUFF_isError`:** `ERR_isError` directly (zbuff_common.c:23), i.e. `code > ZSTD_error_maxCode`-style check from `common/error_private.h`; no ZSTD-level wrapper, so it is valid for both the ZBUFF and legacy `ZBUFFv0x_*` return codes (which use the same `ERR_isError`, e.g. zstd_v05.c:4001).","usage":{"total_tokens":90331,"tool_uses":33,"duration_ms":287660},"uuid":"2b041ec5-cb51-4626-8f6e-e41c41abcb38","session_id":"73cb0b47-bb13-46d2-9cdb-cbadffb29d99"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_e6b5kbejdq37qrcgh7sspdxd733s2taopd6tqwtjuqh6jkvyju3a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01KTP28quHJ4sZ6GwkiGAWmp","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-iPPPON/translation/tests/t02_params.rs","content":"//! Phase B/C: the advanced parameter surface.\n//!\n//! * `ZSTD_cParam_getBounds` / `ZSTD_dParam_getBounds` for EVERY parameter id,\n//!   including ids with no valid variant (out-of-range enum values across FFI).\n//! * `ZSTD_CCtx_setParameter` / `ZSTD_CCtxParams_setParameter` accept/reject\n//!   parity at, inside and one step past each documented bound.\n//! * `ZSTD_compress2` output equality for randomized valid parameter sets, so\n//!   the *effect* of each accepted parameter is verified, not just its return.\n\nmod common;\nuse common::*;\n\ntype CCtx = *mut std::ffi::c_void;\ntype CCtxParams = *mut std::ffi::c_void;\ntype DCtx = *mut std::ffi::c_void;\n\ntype Fn_createCCtx = unsafe extern \"C\" fn() -> CCtx;\ntype Fn_freeCCtx = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(CCtx) -> usize;\ntype Fn_createDCtx = unsafe extern \"C\" fn() -> DCtx;\ntype Fn_freeDCtx = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(DCtx) -> usize;\ntype Fn_cParamBounds = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(i32) -> ZSTD_bounds;\ntype Fn_setParam = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(CCtx, i32, i32) -> usize;\ntype Fn_getParam = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(CCtx, i32, *mut i32) -> usize;\ntype Fn_setPledged = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(CCtx, u64) -> usize;\ntype Fn_reset = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(CCtx, i32) -> usize;\ntype Fn_compress2 = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(CCtx, *mut u8, usize, *const u8, usize) -> usize;\ntype Fn_decompressDCtx =\n    unsafe extern \"C\" fn(DCtx, *mut u8, usize, *const u8, usize) -> usize;\ntype Fn_dSetParam = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(DCtx, i32, i32) -> usize;\ntype Fn_bound = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(usize) -> usize;\n\ntype Fn_createParams = unsafe extern \"C\" fn() -> CCtxParams;\ntype Fn_freeParams = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(CCtxParams) -> usize;\ntype Fn_paramsSet = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(CCtxParams, i32, i32) -> usize;\ntype Fn_paramsGet = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(CCtxParams, i32, *mut i32) -> usize;\ntype Fn_paramsInit = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(CCtxParams, i32) -> usize;\ntype Fn_paramsReset = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(CCtxParams) -> usize;\ntype Fn_setParamsUsingCCtxParams = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(CCtx, CCtxParams) -> usize;\n\n/// Every parameter id the public header names, plus deliberately invalid ids.\nfn all_cparam_ids() -> Vec<i32> {\n    let mut v = vec![\n        ZSTD_c_compressionLevel,\n        ZSTD_c_windowLog,\n        ZSTD_c_hashLog,\n        ZSTD_c_chainLog,\n        ZSTD_c_searchLog,\n        ZSTD_c_minMatch,\n        ZSTD_c_targetLength,\n        ZSTD_c_strategy,\n        ZSTD_c_targetCBlockSize,\n        ZSTD_c_enableLongDistanceMatching,\n        ZSTD_c_ldmHashLog,\n        ZSTD_c_ldmMinMatch,\n        ZSTD_c_ldmBucketSizeLog,\n        ZSTD_c_ldmHashRateLog,\n        ZSTD_c_contentSizeFlag,\n        ZSTD_c_checksumFlag,\n        ZSTD_c_dictIDFlag,\n        ZSTD_c_nbWorkers,\n        ZSTD_c_jobSize,\n        ZSTD_c_overlapLog,\n        ZSTD_c_rsyncable,\n        ZSTD_c_format,\n        ZSTD_c_forceMaxWindow,\n        ZSTD_c_forceAttachDict,\n        ZSTD_c_literalCompressionMode,\n        ZSTD_c_experimentalParam6,\n        ZSTD_c_srcSizeHint,\n        ZSTD_c_enableDedicatedDictSearch,\n        ZSTD_c_stableInBuffer,\n        ZSTD_c_stableOutBuffer,\n        ZSTD_c_blockDelimiters,\n        ZSTD_c_validateSequences,\n        ZSTD_c_splitAfterSequences,\n        ZSTD_c_useRowMatchFinder,\n        ZSTD_c_deterministicRefPrefix,\n        ZSTD_c_prefetchCDictTables,\n        ZSTD_c_enableSeqProducerFallback,\n        ZSTD_c_maxBlockSize,\n        ZSTD_c_repcodeResolution,\n        ZSTD_c_blockSplitterLevel,\n    ];\n    // out-of-range / no-valid-variant enum values that C must still handle\n    v.extend([\n        i32::MIN, -1, 0, 1, 2, 9, 11, 99, 108, 129, 131, 159, 165, 199, 203, 399, 403, 499,\n        501, 999, 1018, 1019, 5000, i32::MAX,\n    ]);\n    v\n}\n\nfn all_dparam_ids() -> Vec<i32> {\n    let mut v = vec![\n        ZSTD_d_windowLogMax,\n        ZSTD_d_format,\n        ZSTD_d_stableOutBuffer,\n        ZSTD_d_forceIgnoreChecksum,\n        ZSTD_d_refMultipleDDicts,\n        ZSTD_d_disableHuffmanAssembly,\n        ZSTD_d_maxBlockSize,\n    ];\n    v.extend([i32::MIN, -1, 0, 1, 99, 101, 999, 1006, 1007, 12345, i32::MAX]);\n    v\n}\n\n/// Phase C + Phase B: bounds for every id must match exactly, including the\n/// `error` field for ids that are not valid parameters at all.\n#[test]\nfn cparam_dparam_bounds_match_including_invalid_ids() {\n    let i = impls();\n    let (c_cb, r_cb) = i.pair::<Fn_cParamBounds>(\"ZSTD_cParam_getBounds\");\n    let (c_db, r_db) = i.pair::<Fn_cParamBounds>(\"ZSTD_dParam_getBounds\");\n\n    for id in all_cparam_ids() {\n        let (a, b) = unsafe { (c_cb(id), r_cb(id)) };\n        assert_eq_dbg(&format!(\"ZSTD_cParam_getBounds({id})\"), a, b);\n    }\n    for id in all_dparam_ids() {\n        let (a, b) = unsafe { (c_db(id), r_db(id)) };\n        assert_eq_dbg(&format!(\"ZSTD_dParam_getBounds({id})\"), a, b);\n    }\n}\n\n/// For every parameter, probe values at the bound, inside it, and one step past\n/// it in both directions. Accept/reject and the resulting *stored* value (via\n/// getParameter) must match. This is the bulk of the ERRORS.md parameter rows.\n#[test]\nfn setparameter_accept_reject_and_readback_match() {\n    let i = impls();\n    let (c_new, r_new) = i.pair::<Fn_createCCtx>(\"ZSTD_createCCtx\");\n    let (c_free, r_free) = i.pair::<Fn_freeCCtx>(\"ZSTD_freeCCtx\");\n    let (c_set, r_set) = i.pair::<Fn_setParam>(\"ZSTD_CCtx_setParameter\");\n    let (c_get, r_get) = i.pair::<Fn_getParam>(\"ZSTD_CCtx_getParameter\");\n    let (c_cb, _) = i.pair::<Fn_cParamBounds>(\"ZSTD_cParam_getBounds\");\n    let (c_rst, r_rst) = i.pair::<Fn_reset>(\"ZSTD_CCtx_reset\");\n\n    let cc = unsafe { c_new() };\n    let rc = unsafe { r_new() };\n    assert!(!cc.is_null() && !rc.is_null());\n\n    for id in all_cparam_ids() {\n        let b = unsafe { c_cb(id) };\n        // probe set: bounds +- 1, extremes, and a few interior points\n        let mut probes: Vec<i32> = vec![\n            i32::MIN,\n            i32::MIN + 1,\n            -1,\n            0,\n            1,\n            i32::MAX - 1,\n            i32::MAX,\n        ];\n        if b.error == 0 {\n            for base in [b.lower_bound, b.upper_bound] {\n                for d in [-2i32, -1, 0, 1, 2] {\n                    probes.push(base.saturating_add(d));\n                }\n            }\n            let mid = (b.lower_bound as i64 + b.upper_bound as i64) / 2;\n            probes.push(mid as i32);\n        }\n\n        for v in probes {\n            // fresh parameter state each probe so results are independent\n            unsafe {\n                c_rst(cc, ZSTD_reset_session_and_parameters);\n                r_rst(rc, ZSTD_reset_session_and_parameters);\n            }\n            let (a, bb) = unsafe { (c_set(cc, id, v), r_set(rc, id, v)) };\n            let tag = format!(\"ZSTD_CCtx_setParameter(id={id}, value={v})\");\n            assert_eq_dbg(&tag, a, bb);\n\n            // read back — must agree whether or not the set succeeded\n            let mut ov1 = -12345i32;\n            let mut ov2 = -12345i32;\n            let (g1, g2) = unsafe { (c_get(cc, id, &mut ov1), r_get(rc, id, &mut ov2)) };\n            assert_eq_dbg(&format!(\"{tag} / getParameter rc\"), g1, g2);\n            assert_eq_dbg(&format!(\"{tag} / getParameter value\"), ov1, ov2);\n        }\n    }\n\n    unsafe {\n        c_free(cc);\n        r_free(rc);\n    }\n}\n\n/// Same sweep against the standalone `ZSTD_CCtx_params` object, which has its\n/// own validation path in the C (`ZSTD_CCtxParams_setParameter`).\n#[test]\nfn cctxparams_accept_reject_and_readback_match() {\n    let i = impls();\n    let (c_new, r_new) = i.pair::<Fn_createParams>(\"ZSTD_createCCtxParams\");\n    let (c_free, r_free) = i.pair::<Fn_freeParams>(\"ZSTD_freeCCtxParams\");\n    let (c_set, r_set) = i.pair::<Fn_paramsSet>(\"ZSTD_CCtxParams_setParameter\");\n    let (c_get, r_get) = i.pair::<Fn_paramsGet>(\"ZSTD_CCtxParams_getParameter\");\n    let (c_init, r_init) = i.pair::<Fn_paramsInit>(\"ZSTD_CCtxParams_init\");\n    let (c_rst, r_rst) = i.pair::<Fn_paramsReset>(\"ZSTD_CCtxParams_reset\");\n    let (c_cb, _) = i.pair::<Fn_cParamBounds>(\"ZSTD_cParam_getBounds\");\n\n    let cp = unsafe { c_new() };\n    let rp = unsafe { r_new() };\n    assert!(!cp.is_null() && !rp.is_null());\n\n    // ZSTD_CCtxParams_init over a level sweep (incl. invalid levels)\n    for lvl in [-1000i32, -1, 0, 1, 3, 19, 22, 23, 100] {\n        let (a, b) = unsafe { (c_init(cp, lvl), r_init(rp, lvl)) };\n        assert_eq_dbg(&format!(\"ZSTD_CCtxParams_init({lvl})\"), a, b);\n    }\n\n    for id in all_cparam_ids() {\n        let b = unsafe { c_cb(id) };\n        let mut probes: Vec<i32> = vec![i32::MIN, -1, 0, 1, i32::MAX];\n        if b.error == 0 {\n            for base in [b.lower_bound, b.upper_bound] {\n                for d in [-1i32, 0, 1] {\n                    probes.push(base.saturating_add(d));\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        for v in probes {\n            unsafe {\n                c_rst(cp);\n                r_rst(rp);\n            }\n            let (a, bb) = unsafe { (c_set(cp, id, v), r_set(rp, id, v)) };\n            let tag = format!(\"ZSTD_CCtxParams_setParameter(id={id}, value={v})\");\n            assert_eq_dbg(&tag, a, bb);\n\n            let mut o1 = -999i32;\n            let mut o2 = -999i32;\n            let (g1, g2) = unsafe { (c_get(cp, id, &mut o1), r_get(rp, id, &mut o2)) };\n            assert_eq_dbg(&format!(\"{tag} / get rc\"), g1, g2);\n            assert_eq_dbg(&format!(\"{tag} / get value\"), o1, o2);\n        }\n    }\n\n    unsafe {\n        c_free(cp);\n        r_free(rp);\n    }\n}\n\n/// A named, reproducible parameter configuration applied through the low-level\n/// `ZSTD_CCtx_setParameter` path, then run end-to-end with `ZSTD_compress2`.\nstruct Cfg {\n    name: &'static str,\n    params: Vec<(i32, i32)>,\n}\n\nfn configurations() -> Vec<Cfg> {\n    let mut v: Vec<Cfg> = Vec::new();\n\n    // one row per strategy — each selects a different match finder source file\n    for &s in &ALL_STRATEGIES {\n        v.push(Cfg {\n            name: \"strategy\",\n            params: vec![(ZSTD_c_strategy, s), (ZSTD_c_compressionLevel, 5)],\n        });\n    }\n    // checksum / contentSize / dictID flag cross product\n    for &ck in &[0, 1] {\n        for &cs in &[0, 1] {\n            for &di in &[0, 1] {\n                v.push(Cfg {\n                    name: \"frame-flags\",\n                    params: vec![\n                        (ZSTD_c_checksumFlag, ck),\n                        (ZSTD_c_contentSizeFlag, cs),\n                        (ZSTD_c_dictIDFlag, di),\n                    ],\n                });\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    // magicless format x checksum\n    for &f in &[ZSTD_f_zstd1, ZSTD_f_zstd1_magicless] {\n        for &ck in &[0, 1] {\n            v.push(Cfg {\n                name: \"format\",\n                params: vec![(ZSTD_c_format, f), (ZSTD_c_checksumFlag, ck)],\n            });\n        }\n    }\n    // long distance matching, with explicit ldm tuning\n    for &ldm in &[0, 1] {\n        v.push(Cfg {\n            name: \"ldm\",\n            params: vec![\n                (ZSTD_c_enableLongDistanceMatching, ldm),\n                (ZSTD_c_windowLog, 20),\n            ],\n        });\n    }\n    v.push(Cfg {\n        name: \"ldm-tuned\",\n        params: vec![\n            (ZSTD_c_enableLongDistanceMatching, 1),\n            (ZSTD_c_ldmHashLog, 17),\n            (ZSTD_c_ldmMinMatch, 32),\n            (ZSTD_c_ldmBucketSizeLog, 3),\n            (ZSTD_c_ldmHashRateLog, 4),\n            (ZSTD_c_windowLog, 21),\n        ],\n    });\n    // literal compression modes\n    for &m in &[ZSTD_lcm_auto, ZSTD_lcm_huffman, ZSTD_lcm_uncompressed] {\n        v.push(Cfg {\n            name: \"literalCompressionMode\",\n            params: vec![(ZSTD_c_literalCompressionMode, m)],\n        });\n    }\n    // row match finder toggle (auto/enable/disable) x strategy in its valid range\n    for &ps in &[ZSTD_ps_auto, ZSTD_ps_enable, ZSTD_ps_disable] {\n        for &s in &[ZSTD_greedy, ZSTD_lazy, ZSTD_lazy2] {\n            v.push(Cfg {\n                name: \"useRowMatchFinder\",\n                params: vec![(ZSTD_c_useRowMatchFinder, ps), (ZSTD_c_strategy, s)],\n            });\n        }\n    }\n    // block splitter / splitAfterSequences / blockSplitterLevel\n    for &ps in &[ZSTD_ps_auto, ZSTD_ps_enable, ZSTD_ps_disable] {\n        v.push(Cfg {\n            name: \"splitAfterSequences\",\n            params: vec![(ZSTD_c_splitAfterSequences, ps), (ZSTD_c_compressionLevel, 9)],\n        });\n    }\n    for lvl in 0..=6 {\n        v.push(Cfg {\n            name: \"blockSplitterLevel\",\n            params: vec![(ZSTD_c_blockSplitterLevel, lvl)],\n        });\n    }\n    // targetCBlockSize / maxBlockSize\n    for &t in &[0, 1340, 2048, 65536, 131_072] {\n        v.push(Cfg {\n            name: \"targetCBlockSize\",\n            params: vec![(ZSTD_c_targetCBlockSize, t)],\n        });\n    }\n    for &m in &[0, 1024, 8192, 65536, 131_072] {\n        v.push(Cfg {\n            name: \"maxBlockSize\",\n            params: vec![(ZSTD_c_maxBlockSize, m)],\n        });\n    }\n    // explicit window/hash/chain/search/minMatch/targetLength tuning\n    v.push(Cfg {\n        name: \"manual-tuning-fast\",\n        params: vec![\n            (ZSTD_c_strategy, ZSTD_fast),\n            (ZSTD_c_windowLog, 17),\n            (ZSTD_c_hashLog, 16),\n            (ZSTD_c_searchLog, 1),\n            (ZSTD_c_minMatch, 5),\n            (ZSTD_c_targetLength, 0),\n        ],\n    });\n    v.push(Cfg {\n        name: \"manual-tuning-btultra2\",\n        params: vec![\n            (ZSTD_c_strategy, ZSTD_btultra2),\n            (ZSTD_c_windowLog, 18),\n            (ZSTD_c_hashLog, 17),\n            (ZSTD_c_chainLog, 17),\n            (ZSTD_c_searchLog, 6),\n            (ZSTD_c_minMatch, 3),\n            (ZSTD_c_targetLength, 999),\n        ],\n    });\n    v.push(Cfg {\n        name: \"minMatch-sweep-3\",\n        params: vec![(ZSTD_c_strategy, ZSTD_lazy2), (ZSTD_c_minMatch, 3)],\n    });\n    v.push(Cfg {\n        name: \"minMatch-sweep-7\",\n        params: vec![(ZSTD_c_strategy, ZSTD_fast), (ZSTD_c_minMatch, 7)],\n    });\n    // srcSizeHint / forceMaxWindow / deterministicRefPrefix / repcodeResolution\n    for &h in &[0, 1, 1000, 1 << 20] {\n        v.push(Cfg {\n            name: \"srcSizeHint\",\n            params: vec![(ZSTD_c_srcSizeHint, h)],\n        });\n    }\n    for &f in &[0, 1] {\n        v.push(Cfg {\n            name: \"forceMaxWindow\",\n            params: vec![(ZSTD_c_forceMaxWindow, f)],\n        });\n    }\n    for &d in &[0, 1] {\n        v.push(Cfg {\n            name: \"deterministicRefPrefix\",\n            params: vec![(ZSTD_c_deterministicRefPrefix, d)],\n        });\n    }\n    for &rr in &[ZSTD_ps_auto, ZSTD_ps_enable, ZSTD_ps_disable] {\n        v.push(Cfg {\n            name: \"repcodeResolution\",\n            params: vec![(ZSTD_c_repcodeResolution, rr)],\n        });\n    }\n    for &r in &[0, 1] {\n        v.push(Cfg {\n            name: \"rsyncable\",\n            params: vec![(ZSTD_c_rsyncable, r), (ZSTD_c_windowLog, 20)],\n        });\n    }\n    // negative / fast levels and the extremes\n    for &lvl in &[-131_072, -5000, -100, -10, -3, -1, 0, 1, 19, 22] {\n        v.push(Cfg {\n            name: \"level\",\n            params: vec![(ZSTD_c_compressionLevel, lvl)],\n        });\n    }\n    // window log extremes (valid range)\n    for &wl in &[10, 11, 15, 20, 27] {\n        v.push(Cfg {\n            name: \"windowLog\",\n            params: vec![(ZSTD_c_windowLog, wl)],\n        });\n    }\n    v\n}\n\n/// Phase B core: for each configuration, drive `ZSTD_compress2` through the\n/// low-level cctx API on many randomized inputs and require byte-identical\n/// frames, then require the frame to decode back to the input in both libs.\n#[test]\nfn compress2_configurations_match() {\n    let i = impls();\n    let (c_new, r_new) = i.pair::<Fn_createCCtx>(\"ZSTD_createCCtx\");\n    let (c_free, r_free) = i.pair::<Fn_freeCCtx>(\"ZSTD_freeCCtx\");\n    let (c_set, r_set) = i.pair::<Fn_setParam>(\"ZSTD_CCtx_setParameter\");\n    let (c_rst, r_rst) = i.pair::<Fn_reset>(\"ZSTD_CCtx_reset\");\n    let (c_c2, r_c2) = i.pair::<Fn_compress2>(\"ZSTD_compress2\");\n    let (c_bound, _) = i.pair::<Fn_bound>(\"ZSTD_compressBound\");\n    let (c_isE, _) = i.pair::<unsafe extern \"C\" fn(usize) -> u32>(\"ZSTD_isError\");\n\n    let (cd_new, rd_new) = i.pair::<Fn_createDCtx>(\"ZSTD_createDCtx\");\n    let (cd_free, rd_free) = i.pair::<Fn_freeDCtx>(\"ZSTD_freeDCtx\");\n    let (cd_dec, rd_dec) = i.pair::<Fn_decompressDCtx>(\"ZSTD_decompressDCtx\");\n    let (cd_set, rd_set) = i.pair::<Fn_dSetParam>(\"ZSTD_DCtx_setParameter\");\n\n    let cc = unsafe { c_new() };\n    let rc = unsafe { r_new() };\n    let cd = unsafe { cd_new() };\n    let rd = unsafe { rd_new() };\n\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(0x5EED_1234);\n\n    for cfg in configurations() {\n        // several randomized inputs per configuration row\n        for trial in 0..6 {\n            let shape = ALL_SHAPES[rng.below(ALL_SHAPES.len())];\n            let len = match trial {\n                0 => 0,\n                1 => 1,\n                2 => rng.range(2, 300),\n                3 => rng.range(300, 20_000),\n                4 => rng.range(120_000, 140_000),\n                _ => rng.range(200_000, 400_000),\n            };\n            let src = gen_shape(shape, len, &mut rng);\n\n            unsafe {\n                c_rst(cc, ZSTD_reset_session_and_parameters);\n                r_rst(rc, ZSTD_reset_session_and_parameters);\n            }\n\n            let mut magicless = false;\n            let mut skip = false;\n            for &(id, val) in &cfg.params {\n                let (a, b) = unsafe { (c_set(cc, id, val), r_set(rc, id, val)) };\n                assert_eq_dbg(\n                    &format!(\"[{}] setParameter({id},{val})\", cfg.name),\n                    a,\n                    b,\n                );\n                if unsafe { c_isE(a) } != 0 {\n                    // both rejected identically; nothing to compress for this row\n                    skip = true;\n                }\n                if id == ZSTD_c_format && val == ZSTD_f_zstd1_magicless {\n                    magicless = true;\n                }\n            }\n            if skip {\n                continue;\n            }\n\n            let cap = unsafe { c_bound(len) } + 64;\n            let mut cb = vec![0xA5u8; cap];\n            let mut rb = vec![0x5Au8; cap];\n            let cn = unsafe { c_c2(cc, cb.as_mut_ptr(), cap, src.as_ptr(), len) };\n            let rn = unsafe { r_c2(rc, rb.as_mut_ptr(), cap, src.as_ptr(), len) };\n\n            let tag = format!(\n                \"[{}] params={:?} shape={shape:?} len={len}\",\n                cfg.name, cfg.params\n            );\n            assert_eq_dbg(&tag, cn, rn);\n            if unsafe { c_isE(cn) } != 0 {\n                continue; // identical rejection, verified above\n            }\n            assert_bytes_eq(&tag, &cb[..cn], &rb[..rn]);\n\n            // round trip through both decoders (magicless frames need the dctx flag)\n            let mut d1 = vec![0u8; len + 64];\n            let mut d2 = vec![0u8; len + 64];\n            unsafe {\n                cd_set(cd, ZSTD_d_format, if magicless { 1 } else { 0 });\n                rd_set(rd, ZSTD_d_format, if magicless { 1 } else { 0 });\n                let a = cd_dec(cd, d1.as_mut_ptr(), d1.len(), cb.as_ptr(), cn);\n                let b = rd_dec(rd, d2.as_mut_ptr(), d2.len(), rb.as_ptr(), rn);\n                assert_eq_dbg(&format!(\"{tag} / decode rc\"), a, b);\n                assert_eq_dbg(&format!(\"{tag} / decode len\"), a, len);\n                assert_bytes_eq(&format!(\"{tag} / payload\"), &src, &d1[..a]);\n                assert_bytes_eq(&format!(\"{tag} / payload\"), &src, &d2[..b]);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    unsafe {\n        c_free(cc);\n        r_free(rc);\n        cd_free(cd);\n        rd_free(rd);\n    }\n}\n\n/// `ZSTD_CCtx_setParametersUsingCCtxParams` — the params-object path into a cctx\n/// must produce the same frames as setting the parameters directly.\n#[test]\nfn set_parameters_using_cctxparams_matches() {\n    let i = impls();\n    let (c_new, r_new) = i.pair::<Fn_createCCtx>(\"ZSTD_createCCtx\");\n    let (c_free, r_free) = i.pair::<Fn_freeCCtx>(\"ZSTD_freeCCtx\");\n    let (c_pnew, r_pnew) = i.pair::<Fn_createParams>(\"ZSTD_createCCtxParams\");\n    let (c_pfree, r_pfree) = i.pair::<Fn_freeParams>(\"ZSTD_freeCCtxParams\");\n    let (c_pset, r_pset) = i.pair::<Fn_paramsSet>(\"ZSTD_CCtxParams_setParameter\");\n    let (c_apply, r_apply) =\n        i.pair::<Fn_setParamsUsingCCtxParams>(\"ZSTD_CCtx_setParametersUsingCCtxParams\");\n    let (c_rst, r_rst) = i.pair::<Fn_reset>(\"ZSTD_CCtx_reset\");\n    let (c_c2, r_c2) = i.pair::<Fn_compress2>(\"ZSTD_compress2\");\n    let (c_bound, _) = i.pair::<Fn_bound>(\"ZSTD_compressBound\");\n\n    let cc = unsafe { c_new() };\n    let rc = unsafe { r_new() };\n    let cp = unsafe { c_pnew() };\n    let rp = unsafe { r_pnew() };\n\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(0xABCD_0001);\n    for cfg in configurations() {\n        for _ in 0..3 {\n            let shape = ALL_SHAPES[rng.below(ALL_SHAPES.len())];\n            let len = rng.range(0, 40_000);\n            let src = gen_shape(shape, len, &mut rng);\n\n            unsafe {\n                c_rst(cc, ZSTD_reset_session_and_parameters);\n                r_rst(rc, ZSTD_reset_session_and_parameters);\n            }\n            let mut bad = false;\n            for &(id, val) in &cfg.params {\n                let (a, b) = unsafe { (c_pset(cp, id, val), r_pset(rp, id, val)) };\n                assert_eq_dbg(&format!(\"params set({id},{val})\"), a, b);\n                if a > usize::MAX - 200 {\n                    bad = true;\n                }\n            }\n            let (a, b) = unsafe { (c_apply(cc, cp), r_apply(rc, rp)) };\n            assert_eq_dbg(\"ZSTD_CCtx_setParametersUsingCCtxParams\", a, b);\n            if bad || a > usize::MAX - 200 {\n                continue;\n            }\n\n            let cap = unsafe { c_bound(len) } + 64;\n            let mut cb = vec![0u8; cap];\n            let mut rb = vec![0u8; cap];\n            let cn = unsafe { c_c2(cc, cb.as_mut_ptr(), cap, src.as_ptr(), len) };\n            let rn = unsafe { r_c2(rc, rb.as_mut_ptr(), cap, src.as_ptr(), len) };\n            let tag = format!(\"[{}] usingCCtxParams len={len} shape={shape:?}\", cfg.name);\n            assert_eq_dbg(&tag, cn, rn);\n            if cn <= usize::MAX - 200 {\n                assert_bytes_eq(&tag, &cb[..cn], &rb[..rn]);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    unsafe {\n        c_pfree(cp);\n        r_pfree(rp);\n        c_free(cc);\n        r_free(rc);\n    }\n}\n\n/// `ZSTD_CCtx_setPledgedSrcSize` interacts with the frame header (content size\n/// field) and is validated against the actual input length. Cover matching,\n/// mismatching and unknown pledges — plus out-of-range reset directives.\n#[test]\nfn pledged_src_size_and_reset_directives() {\n    let i = impls();\n    let (c_new, r_new) = i.pair::<Fn_createCCtx>(\"ZSTD_createCCtx\");\n    let (c_free, r_free) = i.pair::<Fn_freeCCtx>(\"ZSTD_freeCCtx\");\n    let (c_pl, r_pl) = i.pair::<Fn_setPledged>(\"ZSTD_CCtx_setPledgedSrcSize\");\n    let (c_rst, r_rst) = i.pair::<Fn_reset>(\"ZSTD_CCtx_reset\");\n    let (c_c2, r_c2) = i.pair::<Fn_compress2>(\"ZSTD_compress2\");\n    let (c_bound, _) = i.pair::<Fn_bound>(\"ZSTD_compressBound\");\n\n    let cc = unsafe { c_new() };\n    let rc = unsafe { r_new() };\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(0x9911);\n\n    // every reset directive, including out-of-range enum values\n    for d in [-3i32, -1, 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 7, i32::MAX, i32::MIN] {\n        let (a, b) = unsafe { (c_rst(cc, d), r_rst(rc, d)) };\n        assert_eq_dbg(&format!(\"ZSTD_CCtx_reset(directive={d})\"), a, b);\n    }\n\n    for len in [0usize, 1, 100, 5000, 200_000] {\n        let src = gen_shape(Shape::SkewedText, len, &mut rng);\n        for pledge in [\n            0u64,\n            1,\n            len as u64,\n            len as u64 + 1,\n            len.saturating_sub(1) as u64,\n            1 << 40,\n            ZSTD_CONTENTSIZE_UNKNOWN,\n        ] {\n            unsafe {\n                c_rst(cc, ZSTD_reset_session_and_parameters);\n                r_rst(rc, ZSTD_reset_session_and_parameters);\n            }\n            let (a, b) = unsafe { (c_pl(cc, pledge), r_pl(rc, pledge)) };\n            assert_eq_dbg(&format!(\"setPledgedSrcSize({pledge})\"), a, b);\n\n            let cap = unsafe { c_bound(len) } + 64;\n            let mut cb = vec![0u8; cap];\n            let mut rb = vec![0u8; cap];\n            let cn = unsafe { c_c2(cc, cb.as_mut_ptr(), cap, src.as_ptr(), len) };\n            let rn = unsafe { r_c2(rc, rb.as_mut_ptr(), cap, src.as_ptr(), len) };\n            let tag = format!(\"compress2 pledge={pledge} len={len}\");\n            assert_eq_dbg(&tag, cn, rn);\n            if cn <= usize::MAX - 200 {\n                assert_bytes_eq(&tag, &cb[..cn], &rb[..rn]);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    unsafe {\n        c_free(cc);\n        r_free(rc);\n    }\n}\n\n/// Undersized destination buffers must produce the same `dstSize_tooSmall`\n/// behaviour at every capacity from 0 up to the exact frame size.\n#[test]\nfn compress2_dst_too_small_matches() {\n    let i = impls();\n    let (c_new, r_new) = i.pair::<Fn_createCCtx>(\"ZSTD_createCCtx\");\n    let (c_free, r_free) = i.pair::<Fn_freeCCtx>(\"ZSTD_freeCCtx\");\n    let (c_rst, r_rst) = i.pair::<Fn_reset>(\"ZSTD_CCtx_reset\");\n    let (c_c2, r_c2) = i.pair::<Fn_compress2>(\"ZSTD_compress2\");\n    let (c_bound, _) = i.pair::<Fn_bound>(\"ZSTD_compressBound\");\n    let (c_cd, r_cd) = i.pair::<unsafe extern \"C\" fn(usize) -> i32>(\"ZSTD_getErrorCode\");\n\n    let cc = unsafe { c_new() };\n    let rc = unsafe { r_new() };\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(0x4242);\n\n    for &shape in &[Shape::Random, Shape::Constant, Shape::SkewedText] {\n        let len = 3000;\n        let src = gen_shape(shape, len, &mut rng);\n        let full = {\n            unsafe {\n                c_rst(cc, ZSTD_reset_session_and_parameters);\n            }\n            let cap = unsafe { c_bound(len) };\n            let mut b = vec![0u8; cap];\n            unsafe { c_c2(cc, b.as_mut_ptr(), cap, src.as_ptr(), len) }\n        };\n\n        for cap in 0..=full {\n            unsafe {\n                c_rst(cc, ZSTD_reset_session_and_parameters);\n                r_rst(rc, ZSTD_reset_session_and_parameters);\n            }\n            let mut cb = vec![0u8; cap.max(1)];\n            let mut rb = vec![0u8; cap.max(1)];\n            let a = unsafe { c_c2(cc, cb.as_mut_ptr(), cap, src.as_ptr(), len) };\n            let b = unsafe { r_c2(rc, rb.as_mut_ptr(), cap, src.as_ptr(), len) };\n            let tag = format!(\"compress2 shape={shape:?} dstCapacity={cap} (full={full})\");\n            assert_eq_dbg(&tag, a, b);\n            unsafe { assert_eq_dbg(&format!(\"{tag} errcode\"), c_cd(a), r_cd(b)) };\n        }\n    }\n\n    unsafe {\n        c_free(cc);\n        r_free(rc);\n    }\n}\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2463,"cache_read_input_tokens":68026,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2463,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"73cb0b47-bb13-46d2-9cdb-cbadffb29d99","uuid":"95b6c934-5c5a-4805-b2d5-c11720d128a0","timestamp":"2026-08-31T10:42:21.651Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01KTP28quHJ4sZ6GwkiGAWmp","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-iPPPON/translation/tests/t02_params.rs (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"73cb0b47-bb13-46d2-9cdb-cbadffb29d99","uuid":"2e41ab11-2f21-4aaa-9753-7a1378c46abd","timestamp":"2026-08-31T10:42:21.661Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-iPPPON/translation/tests/t02_params.rs","content":"//! Phase B/C: the advanced parameter surface.\n//!\n//! * `ZSTD_cParam_getBounds` / `ZSTD_dParam_getBounds` for EVERY parameter id,\n//!   including ids with no valid variant (out-of-range enum values across FFI).\n//! * `ZSTD_CCtx_setParameter` / `ZSTD_CCtxParams_setParameter` accept/reject\n//!   parity at, inside and one step past each documented bound.\n//! * `ZSTD_compress2` output equality for randomized valid parameter sets, so\n//!   the *effect* of each accepted parameter is verified, not just its return.\n\nmod common;\nuse common::*;\n\ntype CCtx = *mut std::ffi::c_void;\ntype CCtxParams = *mut std::ffi::c_void;\ntype DCtx = *mut std::ffi::c_void;\n\ntype Fn_createCCtx = unsafe extern \"C\" fn() -> CCtx;\ntype Fn_freeCCtx = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(CCtx) -> usize;\ntype Fn_createDCtx = unsafe extern \"C\" fn() -> DCtx;\ntype Fn_freeDCtx = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(DCtx) -> usize;\ntype Fn_cParamBounds = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(i32) -> ZSTD_bounds;\ntype Fn_setParam = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(CCtx, i32, i32) -> usize;\ntype Fn_getParam = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(CCtx, i32, *mut i32) -> usize;\ntype Fn_setPledged = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(CCtx, u64) -> usize;\ntype Fn_reset = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(CCtx, i32) -> usize;\ntype Fn_compress2 = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(CCtx, *mut u8, usize, *const u8, usize) -> usize;\ntype Fn_decompressDCtx =\n    unsafe extern \"C\" fn(DCtx, *mut u8, usize, *const u8, usize) -> usize;\ntype Fn_dSetParam = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(DCtx, i32, i32) -> usize;\ntype Fn_bound = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(usize) -> usize;\n\ntype Fn_createParams = unsafe extern \"C\" fn() -> CCtxParams;\ntype Fn_freeParams = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(CCtxParams) -> usize;\ntype Fn_paramsSet = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(CCtxParams, i32, i32) -> usize;\ntype Fn_paramsGet = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(CCtxParams, i32, *mut i32) -> usize;\ntype Fn_paramsInit = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(CCtxParams, i32) -> usize;\ntype Fn_paramsReset = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(CCtxParams) -> usize;\ntype Fn_setParamsUsingCCtxParams = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(CCtx, CCtxParams) -> usize;\n\n/// Every parameter id the public header names, plus deliberately invalid ids.\nfn all_cparam_ids() -> Vec<i32> {\n    let mut v = vec![\n        ZSTD_c_compressionLevel,\n        ZSTD_c_windowLog,\n        ZSTD_c_hashLog,\n        ZSTD_c_chainLog,\n        ZSTD_c_searchLog,\n        ZSTD_c_minMatch,\n        ZSTD_c_targetLength,\n        ZSTD_c_strategy,\n        ZSTD_c_targetCBlockSize,\n        ZSTD_c_enableLongDistanceMatching,\n        ZSTD_c_ldmHashLog,\n        ZSTD_c_ldmMinMatch,\n        ZSTD_c_ldmBucketSizeLog,\n        ZSTD_c_ldmHashRateLog,\n        ZSTD_c_contentSizeFlag,\n        ZSTD_c_checksumFlag,\n        ZSTD_c_dictIDFlag,\n        ZSTD_c_nbWorkers,\n        ZSTD_c_jobSize,\n        ZSTD_c_overlapLog,\n        ZSTD_c_rsyncable,\n        ZSTD_c_format,\n        ZSTD_c_forceMaxWindow,\n        ZSTD_c_forceAttachDict,\n        ZSTD_c_literalCompressionMode,\n        ZSTD_c_experimentalParam6,\n        ZSTD_c_srcSizeHint,\n        ZSTD_c_enableDedicatedDictSearch,\n        ZSTD_c_stableInBuffer,\n        ZSTD_c_stableOutBuffer,\n        ZSTD_c_blockDelimiters,\n        ZSTD_c_validateSequences,\n        ZSTD_c_splitAfterSequences,\n        ZSTD_c_useRowMatchFinder,\n        ZSTD_c_deterministicRefPrefix,\n        ZSTD_c_prefetchCDictTables,\n        ZSTD_c_enableSeqProducerFallback,\n        ZSTD_c_maxBlockSize,\n        ZSTD_c_repcodeResolution,\n        ZSTD_c_blockSplitterLevel,\n    ];\n    // out-of-range / no-valid-variant enum values that C must still handle\n    v.extend([\n        i32::MIN, -1, 0, 1, 2, 9, 11, 99, 108, 129, 131, 159, 165, 199, 203, 399, 403, 499,\n        501, 999, 1018, 1019, 5000, i32::MAX,\n    ]);\n    v\n}\n\nfn all_dparam_ids() -> Vec<i32> {\n    let mut v = vec![\n        ZSTD_d_windowLogMax,\n        ZSTD_d_format,\n        ZSTD_d_stableOutBuffer,\n        ZSTD_d_forceIgnoreChecksum,\n        ZSTD_d_refMultipleDDicts,\n        ZSTD_d_disableHuffmanAssembly,\n        ZSTD_d_maxBlockSize,\n    ];\n    v.extend([i32::MIN, -1, 0, 1, 99, 101, 999, 1006, 1007, 12345, i32::MAX]);\n    v\n}\n\n/// Phase C + Phase B: bounds for every id must match exactly, including the\n/// `error` field for ids that are not valid parameters at all.\n#[test]\nfn cparam_dparam_bounds_match_including_invalid_ids() {\n    let i = impls();\n    let (c_cb, r_cb) = i.pair::<Fn_cParamBounds>(\"ZSTD_cParam_getBounds\");\n    let (c_db, r_db) = i.pair::<Fn_cParamBounds>(\"ZSTD_dParam_getBounds\");\n\n    for id in all_cparam_ids() {\n        let (a, b) = unsafe { (c_cb(id), r_cb(id)) };\n        assert_eq_dbg(&format!(\"ZSTD_cParam_getBounds({id})\"), a, b);\n    }\n    for id in all_dparam_ids() {\n        let (a, b) = unsafe { (c_db(id), r_db(id)) };\n        assert_eq_dbg(&format!(\"ZSTD_dParam_getBounds({id})\"), a, b);\n    }\n}\n\n/// For every parameter, probe values at the bound, inside it, and one step past\n/// it in both directions. Accept/reject and the resulting *stored* value (via\n/// getParameter) must match. This is the bulk of the ERRORS.md parameter rows.\n#[test]\nfn setparameter_accept_reject_and_readback_match() {\n    let i = impls();\n    let (c_new, r_new) = i.pair::<Fn_createCCtx>(\"ZSTD_createCCtx\");\n    let (c_free, r_free) = i.pair::<Fn_freeCCtx>(\"ZSTD_freeCCtx\");\n    let (c_set, r_set) = i.pair::<Fn_setParam>(\"ZSTD_CCtx_setParameter\");\n    let (c_get, r_get) = i.pair::<Fn_getParam>(\"ZSTD_CCtx_getParameter\");\n    let (c_cb, _) = i.pair::<Fn_cParamBounds>(\"ZSTD_cParam_getBounds\");\n    let (c_rst, r_rst) = i.pair::<Fn_reset>(\"ZSTD_CCtx_reset\");\n\n    let cc = unsafe { c_new() };\n    let rc = unsafe { r_new() };\n    assert!(!cc.is_null() && !rc.is_null());\n\n    for id in all_cparam_ids() {\n        let b = unsafe { c_cb(id) };\n        // probe set: bounds +- 1, extremes, and a few interior points\n        let mut probes: Vec<i32> = vec![\n            i32::MIN,\n            i32::MIN + 1,\n            -1,\n            0,\n            1,\n            i32::MAX - 1,\n            i32::MAX,\n        ];\n        if b.error == 0 {\n            for base in [b.lower_bound, b.upper_bound] {\n                for d in [-2i32, -1, 0, 1, 2] {\n                    probes.push(base.saturating_add(d));\n                }\n            }\n            let mid = (b.lower_bound as i64 + b.upper_bound as i64) / 2;\n            probes.push(mid as i32);\n        }\n\n        for v in probes {\n            // fresh parameter state each probe so results are independent\n            unsafe {\n                c_rst(cc, ZSTD_reset_session_and_parameters);\n                r_rst(rc, ZSTD_reset_session_and_parameters);\n            }\n            let (a, bb) = unsafe { (c_set(cc, id, v), r_set(rc, id, v)) };\n            let tag = format!(\"ZSTD_CCtx_setParameter(id={id}, value={v})\");\n            assert_eq_dbg(&tag, a, bb);\n\n            // read back — must agree whether or not the set succeeded\n            let mut ov1 = -12345i32;\n            let mut ov2 = -12345i32;\n            let (g1, g2) = unsafe { (c_get(cc, id, &mut ov1), r_get(rc, id, &mut ov2)) };\n            assert_eq_dbg(&format!(\"{tag} / getParameter rc\"), g1, g2);\n            assert_eq_dbg(&format!(\"{tag} / getParameter value\"), ov1, ov2);\n        }\n    }\n\n    unsafe {\n        c_free(cc);\n        r_free(rc);\n    }\n}\n\n/// Same sweep against the standalone `ZSTD_CCtx_params` object, which has its\n/// own validation path in the C (`ZSTD_CCtxParams_setParameter`).\n#[test]\nfn cctxparams_accept_reject_and_readback_match() {\n    let i = impls();\n    let (c_new, r_new) = i.pair::<Fn_createParams>(\"ZSTD_createCCtxParams\");\n    let (c_free, r_free) = i.pair::<Fn_freeParams>(\"ZSTD_freeCCtxParams\");\n    let (c_set, r_set) = i.pair::<Fn_paramsSet>(\"ZSTD_CCtxParams_setParameter\");\n    let (c_get, r_get) = i.pair::<Fn_paramsGet>(\"ZSTD_CCtxParams_getParameter\");\n    let (c_init, r_init) = i.pair::<Fn_paramsInit>(\"ZSTD_CCtxParams_init\");\n    let (c_rst, r_rst) = i.pair::<Fn_paramsReset>(\"ZSTD_CCtxParams_reset\");\n    let (c_cb, _) = i.pair::<Fn_cParamBounds>(\"ZSTD_cParam_getBounds\");\n\n    let cp = unsafe { c_new() };\n    let rp = unsafe { r_new() };\n    assert!(!cp.is_null() && !rp.is_null());\n\n    // ZSTD_CCtxParams_init over a level sweep (incl. invalid levels)\n    for lvl in [-1000i32, -1, 0, 1, 3, 19, 22, 23, 100] {\n        let (a, b) = unsafe { (c_init(cp, lvl), r_init(rp, lvl)) };\n        assert_eq_dbg(&format!(\"ZSTD_CCtxParams_init({lvl})\"), a, b);\n    }\n\n    for id in all_cparam_ids() {\n        let b = unsafe { c_cb(id) };\n        let mut probes: Vec<i32> = vec![i32::MIN, -1, 0, 1, i32::MAX];\n        if b.error == 0 {\n            for base in [b.lower_bound, b.upper_bound] {\n                for d in [-1i32, 0, 1] {\n                    probes.push(base.saturating_add(d));\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        for v in probes {\n            unsafe {\n                c_rst(cp);\n                r_rst(rp);\n            }\n            let (a, bb) = unsafe { (c_set(cp, id, v), r_set(rp, id, v)) };\n            let tag = format!(\"ZSTD_CCtxParams_setParameter(id={id}, value={v})\");\n            assert_eq_dbg(&tag, a, bb);\n\n            let mut o1 = -999i32;\n            let mut o2 = -999i32;\n            let (g1, g2) = unsafe { (c_get(cp, id, &mut o1), r_get(rp, id, &mut o2)) };\n            assert_eq_dbg(&format!(\"{tag} / get rc\"), g1, g2);\n            assert_eq_dbg(&format!(\"{tag} / get value\"), o1, o2);\n        }\n    }\n\n    unsafe {\n        c_free(cp);\n        r_free(rp);\n    }\n}\n\n/// A named, reproducible parameter configuration applied through the low-level\n/// `ZSTD_CCtx_setParameter` path, then run end-to-end with `ZSTD_compress2`.\nstruct Cfg {\n    name: &'static str,\n    params: Vec<(i32, i32)>,\n}\n\nfn configurations() -> Vec<Cfg> {\n    let mut v: Vec<Cfg> = Vec::new();\n\n    // one row per strategy — each selects a different match finder source file\n    for &s in &ALL_STRATEGIES {\n        v.push(Cfg {\n            name: \"strategy\",\n            params: vec![(ZSTD_c_strategy, s), (ZSTD_c_compressionLevel, 5)],\n        });\n    }\n    // checksum / contentSize / dictID flag cross product\n    for &ck in &[0, 1] {\n        for &cs in &[0, 1] {\n            for &di in &[0, 1] {\n                v.push(Cfg {\n                    name: \"frame-flags\",\n                    params: vec![\n                        (ZSTD_c_checksumFlag, ck),\n                        (ZSTD_c_contentSizeFlag, cs),\n                        (ZSTD_c_dictIDFlag, di),\n                    ],\n                });\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    // magicless format x checksum\n    for &f in &[ZSTD_f_zstd1, ZSTD_f_zstd1_magicless] {\n        for &ck in &[0, 1] {\n            v.push(Cfg {\n                name: \"format\",\n                params: vec![(ZSTD_c_format, f), (ZSTD_c_checksumFlag, ck)],\n            });\n        }\n    }\n    // long distance matching, with explicit ldm tuning\n    for &ldm in &[0, 1] {\n        v.push(Cfg {\n            name: \"ldm\",\n            params: vec![\n                (ZSTD_c_enableLongDistanceMatching, ldm),\n                (ZSTD_c_windowLog, 20),\n            ],\n        });\n    }\n    v.push(Cfg {\n        name: \"ldm-tuned\",\n        params: vec![\n            (ZSTD_c_enableLongDistanceMatching, 1),\n            (ZSTD_c_ldmHashLog, 17),\n            (ZSTD_c_ldmMinMatch, 32),\n            (ZSTD_c_ldmBucketSizeLog, 3),\n            (ZSTD_c_ldmHashRateLog, 4),\n            (ZSTD_c_windowLog, 21),\n        ],\n    });\n    // literal compression modes\n    for &m in &[ZSTD_lcm_auto, ZSTD_lcm_huffman, ZSTD_lcm_uncompressed] {\n        v.push(Cfg {\n            name: \"literalCompressionMode\",\n            params: vec![(ZSTD_c_literalCompressionMode, m)],\n        });\n    }\n    // row match finder toggle (auto/enable/disable) x strategy in its valid range\n    for &ps in &[ZSTD_ps_auto, ZSTD_ps_enable, ZSTD_ps_disable] {\n        for &s in &[ZSTD_greedy, ZSTD_lazy, ZSTD_lazy2] {\n            v.push(Cfg {\n                name: \"useRowMatchFinder\",\n                params: vec![(ZSTD_c_useRowMatchFinder, ps), (ZSTD_c_strategy, s)],\n            });\n        }\n    }\n    // block splitter / splitAfterSequences / blockSplitterLevel\n    for &ps in &[ZSTD_ps_auto, ZSTD_ps_enable, ZSTD_ps_disable] {\n        v.push(Cfg {\n            name: \"splitAfterSequences\",\n            params: vec![(ZSTD_c_splitAfterSequences, ps), (ZSTD_c_compressionLevel, 9)],\n        });\n    }\n    for lvl in 0..=6 {\n        v.push(Cfg {\n            name: \"blockSplitterLevel\",\n            params: vec![(ZSTD_c_blockSplitterLevel, lvl)],\n        });\n    }\n    // targetCBlockSize / maxBlockSize\n    for &t in &[0, 1340, 2048, 65536, 131_072] {\n        v.push(Cfg {\n            name: \"targetCBlockSize\",\n            params: vec![(ZSTD_c_targetCBlockSize, t)],\n        });\n    }\n    for &m in &[0, 1024, 8192, 65536, 131_072] {\n        v.push(Cfg {\n            name: \"maxBlockSize\",\n            params: vec![(ZSTD_c_maxBlockSize, m)],\n        });\n    }\n    // explicit window/hash/chain/search/minMatch/targetLength tuning\n    v.push(Cfg {\n        name: \"manual-tuning-fast\",\n        params: vec![\n            (ZSTD_c_strategy, ZSTD_fast),\n            (ZSTD_c_windowLog, 17),\n            (ZSTD_c_hashLog, 16),\n            (ZSTD_c_searchLog, 1),\n            (ZSTD_c_minMatch, 5),\n            (ZSTD_c_targetLength, 0),\n        ],\n    });\n    v.push(Cfg {\n        name: \"manual-tuning-btultra2\",\n        params: vec![\n            (ZSTD_c_strategy, ZSTD_btultra2),\n            (ZSTD_c_windowLog, 18),\n            (ZSTD_c_hashLog, 17),\n            (ZSTD_c_chainLog, 17),\n            (ZSTD_c_searchLog, 6),\n            (ZSTD_c_minMatch, 3),\n            (ZSTD_c_targetLength, 999),\n        ],\n    });\n    v.push(Cfg {\n        name: \"minMatch-sweep-3\",\n        params: vec![(ZSTD_c_strategy, ZSTD_lazy2), (ZSTD_c_minMatch, 3)],\n    });\n    v.push(Cfg {\n        name: \"minMatch-sweep-7\",\n        params: vec![(ZSTD_c_strategy, ZSTD_fast), (ZSTD_c_minMatch, 7)],\n    });\n    // srcSizeHint / forceMaxWindow / deterministicRefPrefix / repcodeResolution\n    for &h in &[0, 1, 1000, 1 << 20] {\n        v.push(Cfg {\n            name: \"srcSizeHint\",\n            params: vec![(ZSTD_c_srcSizeHint, h)],\n        });\n    }\n    for &f in &[0, 1] {\n        v.push(Cfg {\n            name: \"forceMaxWindow\",\n            params: vec![(ZSTD_c_forceMaxWindow, f)],\n        });\n    }\n    for &d in &[0, 1] {\n        v.push(Cfg {\n            name: \"deterministicRefPrefix\",\n            params: vec![(ZSTD_c_deterministicRefPrefix, d)],\n        });\n    }\n    for &rr in &[ZSTD_ps_auto, ZSTD_ps_enable, ZSTD_ps_disable] {\n        v.push(Cfg {\n            name: \"repcodeResolution\",\n            params: vec![(ZSTD_c_repcodeResolution, rr)],\n        });\n    }\n    for &r in &[0, 1] {\n        v.push(Cfg {\n            name: \"rsyncable\",\n            params: vec![(ZSTD_c_rsyncable, r), (ZSTD_c_windowLog, 20)],\n        });\n    }\n    // negative / fast levels and the extremes\n    for &lvl in &[-131_072, -5000, -100, -10, -3, -1, 0, 1, 19, 22] {\n        v.push(Cfg {\n            name: \"level\",\n            params: vec![(ZSTD_c_compressionLevel, lvl)],\n        });\n    }\n    // window log extremes (valid range)\n    for &wl in &[10, 11, 15, 20, 27] {\n        v.push(Cfg {\n            name: \"windowLog\",\n            params: vec![(ZSTD_c_windowLog, wl)],\n        });\n    }\n    v\n}\n\n/// Phase B core: for each configuration, drive `ZSTD_compress2` through the\n/// low-level cctx API on many randomized inputs and require byte-identical\n/// frames, then require the frame to decode back to the input in both libs.\n#[test]\nfn compress2_configurations_match() {\n    let i = impls();\n    let (c_new, r_new) = i.pair::<Fn_createCCtx>(\"ZSTD_createCCtx\");\n    let (c_free, r_free) = i.pair::<Fn_freeCCtx>(\"ZSTD_freeCCtx\");\n    let (c_set, r_set) = i.pair::<Fn_setParam>(\"ZSTD_CCtx_setParameter\");\n    let (c_rst, r_rst) = i.pair::<Fn_reset>(\"ZSTD_CCtx_reset\");\n    let (c_c2, r_c2) = i.pair::<Fn_compress2>(\"ZSTD_compress2\");\n    let (c_bound, _) = i.pair::<Fn_bound>(\"ZSTD_compressBound\");\n    let (c_isE, _) = i.pair::<unsafe extern \"C\" fn(usize) -> u32>(\"ZSTD_isError\");\n\n    let (cd_new, rd_new) = i.pair::<Fn_createDCtx>(\"ZSTD_createDCtx\");\n    let (cd_free, rd_free) = i.pair::<Fn_freeDCtx>(\"ZSTD_freeDCtx\");\n    let (cd_dec, rd_dec) = i.pair::<Fn_decompressDCtx>(\"ZSTD_decompressDCtx\");\n    let (cd_set, rd_set) = i.pair::<Fn_dSetParam>(\"ZSTD_DCtx_setParameter\");\n\n    let cc = unsafe { c_new() };\n    let rc = unsafe { r_new() };\n    let cd = unsafe { cd_new() };\n    let rd = unsafe { rd_new() };\n\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(0x5EED_1234);\n\n    for cfg in configurations() {\n        // several randomized inputs per configuration row\n        for trial in 0..6 {\n            let shape = ALL_SHAPES[rng.below(ALL_SHAPES.len())];\n            let len = match trial {\n                0 => 0,\n                1 => 1,\n                2 => rng.range(2, 300),\n                3 => rng.range(300, 20_000),\n                4 => rng.range(120_000, 140_000),\n                _ => rng.range(200_000, 400_000),\n            };\n            let src = gen_shape(shape, len, &mut rng);\n\n            unsafe {\n                c_rst(cc, ZSTD_reset_session_and_parameters);\n                r_rst(rc, ZSTD_reset_session_and_parameters);\n            }\n\n            let mut magicless = false;\n            let mut skip = false;\n            for &(id, val) in &cfg.params {\n                let (a, b) = unsafe { (c_set(cc, id, val), r_set(rc, id, val)) };\n                assert_eq_dbg(\n                    &format!(\"[{}] setParameter({id},{val})\", cfg.name),\n                    a,\n                    b,\n                );\n                if unsafe { c_isE(a) } != 0 {\n                    // both rejected identically; nothing to compress for this row\n                    skip = true;\n                }\n                if id == ZSTD_c_format && val == ZSTD_f_zstd1_magicless {\n                    magicless = true;\n                }\n            }\n            if skip {\n                continue;\n            }\n\n            let cap = unsafe { c_bound(len) } + 64;\n            let mut cb = vec![0xA5u8; cap];\n            let mut rb = vec![0x5Au8; cap];\n            let cn = unsafe { c_c2(cc, cb.as_mut_ptr(), cap, src.as_ptr(), len) };\n            let rn = unsafe { r_c2(rc, rb.as_mut_ptr(), cap, src.as_ptr(), len) };\n\n            let tag = format!(\n                \"[{}] params={:?} shape={shape:?} len={len}\",\n                cfg.name, cfg.params\n            );\n            assert_eq_dbg(&tag, cn, rn);\n            if unsafe { c_isE(cn) } != 0 {\n                continue; // identical rejection, verified above\n            }\n            assert_bytes_eq(&tag, &cb[..cn], &rb[..rn]);\n\n            // round trip through both decoders (magicless frames need the dctx flag)\n            let mut d1 = vec![0u8; len + 64];\n            let mut d2 = vec![0u8; len + 64];\n            unsafe {\n                cd_set(cd, ZSTD_d_format, if magicless { 1 } else { 0 });\n                rd_set(rd, ZSTD_d_format, if magicless { 1 } else { 0 });\n                let a = cd_dec(cd, d1.as_mut_ptr(), d1.len(), cb.as_ptr(), cn);\n                let b = rd_dec(rd, d2.as_mut_ptr(), d2.len(), rb.as_ptr(), rn);\n                assert_eq_dbg(&format!(\"{tag} / decode rc\"), a, b);\n                assert_eq_dbg(&format!(\"{tag} / decode len\"), a, len);\n                assert_bytes_eq(&format!(\"{tag} / payload\"), &src, &d1[..a]);\n                assert_bytes_eq(&format!(\"{tag} / payload\"), &src, &d2[..b]);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    unsafe {\n        c_free(cc);\n        r_free(rc);\n        cd_free(cd);\n        rd_free(rd);\n    }\n}\n\n/// `ZSTD_CCtx_setParametersUsingCCtxParams` — the params-object path into a cctx\n/// must produce the same frames as setting the parameters directly.\n#[test]\nfn set_parameters_using_cctxparams_matches() {\n    let i = impls();\n    let (c_new, r_new) = i.pair::<Fn_createCCtx>(\"ZSTD_createCCtx\");\n    let (c_free, r_free) = i.pair::<Fn_freeCCtx>(\"ZSTD_freeCCtx\");\n    let (c_pnew, r_pnew) = i.pair::<Fn_createParams>(\"ZSTD_createCCtxParams\");\n    let (c_pfree, r_pfree) = i.pair::<Fn_freeParams>(\"ZSTD_freeCCtxParams\");\n    let (c_pset, r_pset) = i.pair::<Fn_paramsSet>(\"ZSTD_CCtxParams_setParameter\");\n    let (c_apply, r_apply) =\n        i.pair::<Fn_setParamsUsingCCtxParams>(\"ZSTD_CCtx_setParametersUsingCCtxParams\");\n    let (c_rst, r_rst) = i.pair::<Fn_reset>(\"ZSTD_CCtx_reset\");\n    let (c_c2, r_c2) = i.pair::<Fn_compress2>(\"ZSTD_compress2\");\n    let (c_bound, _) = i.pair::<Fn_bound>(\"ZSTD_compressBound\");\n\n    let cc = unsafe { c_new() };\n    let rc = unsafe { r_new() };\n    let cp = unsafe { c_pnew() };\n    let rp = unsafe { r_pnew() };\n\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(0xABCD_0001);\n    for cfg in configurations() {\n        for _ in 0..3 {\n            let shape = ALL_SHAPES[rng.below(ALL_SHAPES.len())];\n            let len = rng.range(0, 40_000);\n            let src = gen_shape(shape, len, &mut rng);\n\n            unsafe {\n                c_rst(cc, ZSTD_reset_session_and_parameters);\n                r_rst(rc, ZSTD_reset_session_and_parameters);\n            }\n            let mut bad = false;\n            for &(id, val) in &cfg.params {\n                let (a, b) = unsafe { (c_pset(cp, id, val), r_pset(rp, id, val)) };\n                assert_eq_dbg(&format!(\"params set({id},{val})\"), a, b);\n                if a > usize::MAX - 200 {\n                    bad = true;\n                }\n            }\n            let (a, b) = unsafe { (c_apply(cc, cp), r_apply(rc, rp)) };\n            assert_eq_dbg(\"ZSTD_CCtx_setParametersUsingCCtxParams\", a, b);\n            if bad || a > usize::MAX - 200 {\n                continue;\n            }\n\n            let cap = unsafe { c_bound(len) } + 64;\n            let mut cb = vec![0u8; cap];\n            let mut rb = vec![0u8; cap];\n            let cn = unsafe { c_c2(cc, cb.as_mut_ptr(), cap, src.as_ptr(), len) };\n            let rn = unsafe { r_c2(rc, rb.as_mut_ptr(), cap, src.as_ptr(), len) };\n            let tag = format!(\"[{}] usingCCtxParams len={len} shape={shape:?}\", cfg.name);\n            assert_eq_dbg(&tag, cn, rn);\n            if cn <= usize::MAX - 200 {\n                assert_bytes_eq(&tag, &cb[..cn], &rb[..rn]);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    unsafe {\n        c_pfree(cp);\n        r_pfree(rp);\n        c_free(cc);\n        r_free(rc);\n    }\n}\n\n/// `ZSTD_CCtx_setPledgedSrcSize` interacts with the frame header (content size\n/// field) and is validated against the actual input length. Cover matching,\n/// mismatching and unknown pledges — plus out-of-range reset directives.\n#[test]\nfn pledged_src_size_and_reset_directives() {\n    let i = impls();\n    let (c_new, r_new) = i.pair::<Fn_createCCtx>(\"ZSTD_createCCtx\");\n    let (c_free, r_free) = i.pair::<Fn_freeCCtx>(\"ZSTD_freeCCtx\");\n    let (c_pl, r_pl) = i.pair::<Fn_setPledged>(\"ZSTD_CCtx_setPledgedSrcSize\");\n    let (c_rst, r_rst) = i.pair::<Fn_reset>(\"ZSTD_CCtx_reset\");\n    let (c_c2, r_c2) = i.pair::<Fn_compress2>(\"ZSTD_compress2\");\n    let (c_bound, _) = i.pair::<Fn_bound>(\"ZSTD_compressBound\");\n\n    let cc = unsafe { c_new() };\n    let rc = unsafe { r_new() };\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(0x9911);\n\n    // every reset directive, including out-of-range enum values\n    for d in [-3i32, -1, 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 7, i32::MAX, i32::MIN] {\n        let (a, b) = unsafe { (c_rst(cc, d), r_rst(rc, d)) };\n        assert_eq_dbg(&format!(\"ZSTD_CCtx_reset(directive={d})\"), a, b);\n    }\n\n    for len in [0usize, 1, 100, 5000, 200_000] {\n        let src = gen_shape(Shape::SkewedText, len, &mut rng);\n        for pledge in [\n            0u64,\n            1,\n            len as u64,\n            len as u64 + 1,\n            len.saturating_sub(1) as u64,\n            1 << 40,\n            ZSTD_CONTENTSIZE_UNKNOWN,\n        ] {\n            unsafe {\n                c_rst(cc, ZSTD_reset_session_and_parameters);\n                r_rst(rc, ZSTD_reset_session_and_parameters);\n            }\n            let (a, b) = unsafe { (c_pl(cc, pledge), r_pl(rc, pledge)) };\n            assert_eq_dbg(&format!(\"setPledgedSrcSize({pledge})\"), a, b);\n\n            let cap = unsafe { c_bound(len) } + 64;\n            let mut cb = vec![0u8; cap];\n            let mut rb = vec![0u8; cap];\n            let cn = unsafe { c_c2(cc, cb.as_mut_ptr(), cap, src.as_ptr(), len) };\n            let rn = unsafe { r_c2(rc, rb.as_mut_ptr(), cap, src.as_ptr(), len) };\n            let tag = format!(\"compress2 pledge={pledge} len={len}\");\n            assert_eq_dbg(&tag, cn, rn);\n            if cn <= usize::MAX - 200 {\n                assert_bytes_eq(&tag, &cb[..cn], &rb[..rn]);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    unsafe {\n        c_free(cc);\n        r_free(rc);\n    }\n}\n\n/// Undersized destination buffers must produce the same `dstSize_tooSmall`\n/// behaviour at every capacity from 0 up to the exact frame size.\n#[test]\nfn compress2_dst_too_small_matches() {\n    let i = impls();\n    let (c_new, r_new) = i.pair::<Fn_createCCtx>(\"ZSTD_createCCtx\");\n    let (c_free, r_free) = i.pair::<Fn_freeCCtx>(\"ZSTD_freeCCtx\");\n    let (c_rst, r_rst) = i.pair::<Fn_reset>(\"ZSTD_CCtx_reset\");\n    let (c_c2, r_c2) = i.pair::<Fn_compress2>(\"ZSTD_compress2\");\n    let (c_bound, _) = i.pair::<Fn_bound>(\"ZSTD_compressBound\");\n    let (c_cd, r_cd) = i.pair::<unsafe extern \"C\" fn(usize) -> i32>(\"ZSTD_getErrorCode\");\n\n    let cc = unsafe { c_new() };\n    let rc = unsafe { r_new() };\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(0x4242);\n\n    for &shape in &[Shape::Random, Shape::Constant, Shape::SkewedText] {\n        let len = 3000;\n        let src = gen_shape(shape, len, &mut rng);\n        let full = {\n            unsafe {\n                c_rst(cc, ZSTD_reset_session_and_parameters);\n            }\n            let cap = unsafe { c_bound(len) };\n            let mut b = vec![0u8; cap];\n            unsafe { c_c2(cc, b.as_mut_ptr(), cap, src.as_ptr(), len) }\n        };\n\n        for cap in 0..=full {\n            unsafe {\n                c_rst(cc, ZSTD_reset_session_and_parameters);\n                r_rst(rc, ZSTD_reset_session_and_parameters);\n            }\n            let mut cb = vec![0u8; cap.max(1)];\n            let mut rb = vec![0u8; cap.max(1)];\n            let a = unsafe { c_c2(cc, cb.as_mut_ptr(), cap, src.as_ptr(), len) };\n            let b = unsafe { r_c2(rc, rb.as_mut_ptr(), cap, src.as_ptr(), len) };\n            let tag = format!(\"compress2 shape={shape:?} dstCapacity={cap} (full={full})\");\n            assert_eq_dbg(&tag, a, b);\n            unsafe { assert_eq_dbg(&format!(\"{tag} errcode\"), c_cd(a), r_cd(b)) };\n        }\n    }\n\n    unsafe {\n        c_free(cc);\n        r_free(rc);\n    }\n}\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
