** — the srcSize==0 / srcSize==1 / RLE / not-compressible-return-0 / tableLog-default axes you listed live only in the *callers* (`HUF_compressWeights`, `ZSTD_compress*`). The closest surviving equivalent is `HUF_compressWeights` (static, `compress/huf_compress.c:146`).\n\n**`common/huf.h`** — there is **no `HUF_STATIC_LINKING_ONLY` guard at all** in zstd 1.5.7; the whole header is one `HUF_H_298734234` block, so *every* HUF symbol listed is unconditionally exported. Conditional compilation is only via `HUF_FORCE_DECOMPRESS_X1` (:257, :273) / `HUF_FORCE_DECOMPRESS_X2` (:265, :270).\n\n**`compress/hist.h`** — all unconditional; but `HIST_count` and `HIST_countFast` bodies are wrapped in `#ifndef ZSTD_NO_UNUSED_FUNCTIONS` (`compress/hist.c:176`–:191).\n\n**`common/xxhash.h`** — `XXH_NO_XXH3` is force-defined at `common/xxhash.h:14-16` and `XXH_NAMESPACE ZSTD_` at :18-20. So **no `ZSTD_XXH3_*`/`ZSTD_XXH128*` symbols exist**. Exported: `ZSTD_XXH_versionNumber`, `ZSTD_XXH32*`, `ZSTD_XXH64*` (streaming present: `XXH_NO_STREAM` is not defined).\n\n---\n\n# 2. FSE\n\n### `unsigned FSE_versionNumber(void)` — `common/entropy_common.c:27`\n- No branches. Returns `FSE_VERSION_NUMBER` = 0*10000+9*100+0 = **900**.\n\n### `unsigned FSE_isError(size_t code)` / `const char* FSE_getErrorName(size_t code)` — `common/entropy_common.c:31,32`\n- Thin forwards to `ERR_isError` / `ERR_getErrorName`. Branch axis: `code > ERROR(maxCode)` (i.e. `code` in the error band vs a normal size).\n\n### `size_t FSE_compressBound(size_t size)` — `compress/fse_compress.c:623`\n- No branches. `= FSE_NCOUNTBOUND(512) + size + (size>>7) + 4 + sizeof(size_t)`.\n\n### `unsigned FSE_optimalTableLog_internal(unsigned maxTableLog, size_t srcSize, unsigned maxSymbolValue, unsigned minus)` — `compress/fse_compress.c:357`\nBranch axes (all on valid input), :363-:367:\n- `maxTableLog == 0` → `tableLog = FSE_DEFAULT_TABLELOG` (**11**).\n- `maxBitsSrc < tableLog` (where `maxBitsSrc = highbit32(srcSize-1) - minus`) → clamp down to `maxBitsSrc`. Axis = **srcSize small relative to maxTableLog**.\n- `minBits > tableLog` → raise to `minBits`, where `minBits = min(highbit32(srcSize)+1, highbit32(maxSymbolValue)+2)` (`FSE_minTableLog`, :348). Axis = **large alphabet / tiny srcSize**.\n- `tableLog < FSE_MIN_TABLELOG` (**5**) → clamp to 5.\n- `tableLog > FSE_MAX_TABLELOG` (**12**, = `FSE_MAX_MEMORY_USAGE 14` − 2) → clamp to 12.\n- `minus` axis: 2 (via `FSE_optimalTableLog`), 1 (via `HUF_optimalTableLog`, `compress/huf_compress.c:1286`).\n- Precondition `srcSize > 1` (assert at :362) — srcSize 0/1 is UB, callers must use RLE.\n\n### `unsigned FSE_optimalTableLog(unsigned maxTableLog, size_t srcSize, unsigned maxSymbolValue)` — `compress/fse_compress.c:371`\n- No own branches; `minus = 2`.\n\n### `size_t FSE_normalizeCount(short* normalizedCounter, unsigned tableLog, const unsigned* count, size_t total, unsigned maxSymbolValue, unsigned useLowProbCount)` — `compress/fse_compress.c:465`\nBranch axes:\n- `tableLog == 0` → default **11** (:470).\n- `tableLog < FSE_MIN_TABLELOG (5)` → `ERROR(GENERIC)` (:471).\n- `tableLog > FSE_MAX_TABLELOG (12)` → `ERROR(tableLog_tooLarge)` (:472).\n- `tableLog < FSE_minTableLog(total, maxSymbolValue)` → `ERROR(GENERIC)` (:473).\n- `useLowProbCount` → `lowProbCount = -1` else `+1` (:476). This is the axis that toggles the low-prob (`-1`) encoding, which in turn selects the *slow* spread path in `FSE_buildCTable_wksp`/`FSE_buildDTable_internal`.\n- Per-symbol loop (:486-:501): `count[s] == total` → **return 0 immediately (RLE special case)**; `count[s] == 0` → norm 0; `count[s] <= lowThreshold` (`= total >> tableLog`) → `lowProbCount`; else proportional `proba`, with sub-branch `proba < 8` → round-up test against `rtbTable[proba]` = `{0, 473195, 504333, 520860, 550000, 700000, 750000, 830000}` (:475).\n- **Secondary normalization axis** (:502): `-stillToDistribute >= (normalizedCounter[largest] >> 1)` → call `FSE_normalizeM2`, else just `normalizedCounter[largest] += stillToDistribute`.\n- Success returns `tableLog`; returns `0` for the RLE case.\n\n### `static size_t FSE_normalizeM2(...)` — `compress/fse_compress.c:379` (reached only from the above)\nBranch axes:\n- Per-symbol classification (:390-:409): `count[s]==0`; `count[s] <= lowThreshold` (`total >> tableLog`); `count[s] <= lowOne` (`(total*3) >> (tableLog+1)`); else `NOT_YET_ASSIGNED (-2)`.\n- `ToDistribute == 0` → return 0 (:412).\n- `(total / ToDistribute) > lowOne` → **\"risk of rounding to zero\"** second pass with `lowOne = (total*3)/(ToDistribute*2)` (:415-:426).\n- `distributed == maxSymbolValue+1` → **\"all values pretty poor\"**: dump all remaining points on argmax, return 0 (:428-:437).\n- `total == 0` → round-robin `ToDistribute` over symbols with `norm[s] > 0` (:439-:444).\n- Otherwise fixed-point scaling with `vStepLog = 62 - tableLog` (:446); `weight < 1` → `ERROR(GENERIC)` (:456).\n\n### `size_t FSE_NCountWriteBound(unsigned maxSymbolValue, unsigned tableLog)` — `compress/fse_compress.c:223`\n- Single branch (:230): `maxSymbolValue == 0` → return `FSE_NCOUNTBOUND` (**512**); else the computed `maxHeaderSize`.\n\n### `size_t FSE_writeNCount(void* buffer, size_t bufferSize, const short* normalizedCounter, unsigned maxSymbolValue, unsigned tableLog)` — `compress/fse_compress.c:330`\nBranch axes:\n- `tableLog > FSE_MAX_TABLELOG (12)` → `ERROR(tableLog_tooLarge)` (:333).\n- `tableLog < FSE_MIN_TABLELOG (5)` → `ERROR(GENERIC)` (:334).\n- **Bitstream-writer variant selection** (:336-:339): `bufferSize < FSE_NCountWriteBound(...)` → `FSE_writeNCount_generic(..., writeIsSafe=0)` (bounds-checked, can return `ERROR(dstSize_tooSmall)`); else `writeIsSafe=1` (all `out > oend-2` checks compiled out).\n- Inside `FSE_writeNCount_generic` (:233): axes are `previousIs0` run-length encoding — `symbol >= start+24` (0xFFFF 24-zero escape, :265), `symbol >= start+3` (2-bit triple, :275), `bitCount > 16` flush (:282, :304); per-symbol `count >= threshold` (:295), `count < max` bit-saving (:299), `remaining < threshold` → `nbBits--, threshold >>= 1` (:302); `remaining < 1` → `ERROR(GENERIC)` (:301); final `remaining != 1` → `ERROR(GENERIC)` (:314); `symbol == alphabetSize` mid-run → `break` (:264).\n\n### `size_t FSE_readNCount(short*, unsigned* maxSVPtr, unsigned* tableLogPtr, const void* headerBuffer, size_t hbSize)` — `common/entropy_common.c:219`\n- Zero branches of its own: forwards to `FSE_readNCount_bmi2(..., bmi2=0)`.\n\n### `size_t FSE_readNCount_bmi2(short*, unsigned*, unsigned*, const void*, size_t hbSize, int bmi2)` — `common/entropy_common.c:206`\n- **Dispatch axis**: `#if DYNAMIC_BMI2` and `bmi2 != 0` → `FSE_readNCount_body_bmi2` (BMI2_TARGET_ATTRIBUTE clone, :198), else `FSE_readNCount_body_default` (:190). When `DYNAMIC_BMI2==0` the `bmi2` arg is ignored (`(void)bmi2`, :215).\n- Body `FSE_readNCount_body` (:42) axes:\n  - **`hbSize < 8`** → copy into an 8-byte zero-padded stack `buffer[8]` and **recurse** through `FSE_readNCount` (always the non-BMI2 body); then `countSize > hbSize` → `ERROR(corruption_detected)` (:57-:66). This is a distinct code path from `hbSize >= 8`.\n  - tableLog read: `nbBits = (bitStream & 0xF) + FSE_MIN_TABLELOG(5)`; `nbBits > FSE_TABLELOG_ABSOLUTE_MAX (15)` → `ERROR(tableLog_tooLarge)` (:73).\n  - `previous0` zero-run path (:82-:130): `repeats >= 12` loop (consumes 36 symbols at a time, :89); refill sub-branch `ip <= iend-7` (fast, `ip += 3`) vs. the `ip = iend - 4` clamp (:91-:97 and again :120-:128).\n  - per-symbol: `(bitStream & (threshold-1)) < max` → short code (`nbBits-1`) vs. long code (`nbBits`, with `count >= threshold ? count -= max`) (:135-:142).\n  - `count >= 0` vs `count == -1` (:148-:153) — the low-prob branch.\n  - `remaining < threshold` → `remaining <= 1` → break; else `nbBits = highbit32(remaining)+1; threshold = 1 << (nbBits-1)` (:158-:166).\n  - `charnum >= maxSV1` → break (:114, :167).\n  - Final validation: `remaining != 1` → `corruption_detected` (:179); `charnum > maxSV1` → `maxSymbolValue_tooSmall` (:181); `bitCount > 32` → `corruption_detected` (:182).\n\n### `size_t FSE_buildCTable_wksp(FSE_CTable* ct, const short* normalizedCounter, unsigned maxSymbolValue, unsigned tableLog, void* workSpace, size_t wkspSize)` — `compress/fse_compress.c:68`\nBranch axes:\n- `FSE_BUILD_CTABLE_WORKSPACE_SIZE(maxSymbolValue, tableLog) > wkspSize` → `ERROR(tableLog_tooLarge)` (:87). Required size = `((maxSymbolValue+2) + (1<<tableLog))/2 + 2` U32.\n- `tableLog == 0` vs `!= 0` affects the `FSCT` offset (`tableLog ? tableSize>>1 : 1`, :76).\n- Per-symbol cumul loop: `normalizedCounter[u-1] == -1` (low-proba → placed at `highThreshold--`) vs `>= 0` (:104-:111). **This is the axis** that decides the next branch.\n- **Spread-symbols dispatch (:116)**: `highThreshold == tableSize - 1` (i.e. **no `-1` low-prob symbols**) → the 8-bytes-at-a-time `spread[]` + unroll-2 fast path (:116-:153); else the variable-length inner-loop path with the `while (position > highThreshold)` low-proba skip (:154-:167).\n- Symbol-transform `switch (normalizedCounter[s])` (:179): `case 0` (fake cost `tableLog+1` bits), `case -1`/`case 1` (shared), `default` (>1, uses `highbit32(n-1)`).\n- Returns `0` on success.\n\n### `size_t FSE_buildCTable_rle(FSE_CTable* ct, unsigned char symbolValue)` — `compress/fse_compress.c:528`\n- **No branches at all.** Writes tableLog=0, maxSymbolValue=symbolValue, always returns 0.\n\n### `size_t FSE_compress_usingCTable(void* dst, size_t dstSize, const void* src, size_t srcSize, const FSE_CTable* ct)` — `compress/fse_compress.c:610`\n- **One dispatch axis** (:614-:619): `fast = (dstSize >= FSE_BLOCKBOUND(srcSize))` i.e. `dstSize >= srcSize + (srcSize>>7) + 4 + sizeof(size_t)` → `FSE_compress_usingCTable_generic(..., fast=1)` (uses `BIT_flushBitsFast`, no bounds clamping) else `fast=0` (`BIT_flushBits`).\n- Generic body (:551) axes:\n  - **`srcSize <= 2` → return 0** (:563) — this is the \"not compressible / too small\" return.\n  - `BIT_initCStream` error (i.e. `dstSize <= sizeof(size_t)`) → **return 0**, not an error code (:564-:565).\n  - **`srcSize & 1`** (odd) → 3 symbols primed with `FSE_initCState2` ×2 + one `FSE_encodeSymbol` + flush; even → 2 `FSE_initCState2` (:569-:577).\n  - `srcSize & 2` join-to-mod-4, gated on the *static* `sizeof(bitContainer)*8 > FSE_MAX_TABLELOG*4+7` i.e. 64 > 55 → true on 64-bit, false on 32-bit (:581).\n  - Main loop unroll is 4/iteration on 64-bit, 2/iteration on 32-bit (static tests at :592, :597).\n  - Return value from `BIT_closeCStream`: **0 if the bitstream overflowed `dst`** (`bitstream.h:240`).\n\n### `size_t FSE_buildDTable_wksp(FSE_DTable* dt, const short* normalizedCounter, unsigned maxSymbolValue, unsigned tableLog, void* workSpace, size_t wkspSize)` — `common/fse_decompress.c:161` → `FSE_buildDTable_internal` (:58)\nBranch axes:\n- `FSE_BUILD_DTABLE_WKSP_SIZE(tableLog, maxSymbolValue) > wkspSize` → `ERROR(maxSymbolValue_tooLarge)` (:70). Size = `sizeof(short)*(maxSymbolValue+1) + (1<<tableLog) + 8`.\n- `maxSymbolValue > FSE_MAX_SYMBOL_VALUE (255)` → `ERROR(maxSymbolValue_tooLarge)` (:71).\n- `tableLog > FSE_MAX_TABLELOG (12)` → `ERROR(tableLog_tooLarge)` (:72).\n- **`fastMode` axis** (:78-:86): `DTableH.fastMode` starts 1; set to **0** if any `normalizedCounter[s] >= (1 << (tableLog-1))` (any symbol with probability > 50%). This is the flag consumed by `FSE_decompress_wksp_body` to pick `FSE_decodeSymbolFast` vs `FSE_decodeSymbol`.\n- `normalizedCounter[s] == -1` → symbol placed at `highThreshold--`, `symbolNext[s]=1` (:81).\n- **Spread dispatch (:92)**: `highThreshold == tableSize - 1` (no low-prob) → `MEM_write64` spread + unroll-2; else the variable inner loop with `while (position > highThreshold)` and a `position != 0` → `ERROR(GENERIC)` check (:135-:147).\n- Returns 0.\n\n### `size_t FSE_decompress_wksp_bmi2(void* dst, size_t dstCapacity, const void* cSrc, size_t cSrcSize, unsigned maxLog, void* workSpace, size_t wkspSize, int bmi2)` — `common/fse_decompress.c:304`\nBranch axes:\n- **Dispatch**: `DYNAMIC_BMI2 && bmi2` → `_body_bmi2` (:298) else `_body_default` (:292).\n- Body `FSE_decompress_wksp_body` (:243):\n  - `wkspSize < sizeof(FSE_DecompressWksp)` (= `2*(FSE_MAX_SYMBOL_VALUE+1)` = **512** bytes) → `ERROR(GENERIC)` (:258).\n  - `FSE_readNCount_bmi2` error propagation; `tableLog > maxLog` → `ERROR(tableLog_tooLarge)` (:267). (`maxLog` is **6** when called from `HUF_readStats_body`, `entropy_common.c:272`.)\n  - `FSE_DECOMPRESS_WKSP_SIZE(tableLog, maxSymbolValue) > wkspSize` → `ERROR(tableLog_tooLarge)` (:273).\n  - **`fastMode` dispatch** (:283-:287): `DTableH->fastMode` → `FSE_decompress_usingDTable_generic(..., fast=1)` (`FSE_decodeSymbolFast`/`BIT_readBitsFast`) else `fast=0`.\n  - Generic body (:173): `BIT_initDStream` failure propagates; `BIT_reloadDStream == BIT_DStream_overflow` right after the two `FSE_initDState` → `ERROR(corruption_detected)` (:193). Main loop is 4 symbols/iteration with static reload tests `FSE_MAX_TABLELOG*2+7 (31) > 64?` (false on 64-bit) and `*4+7 (55) > 64?` (false on 64-bit) — so on 64-bit no intra-loop reloads; on 32-bit both fire (:201-:212). Tail loop returns `ERROR(dstSize_tooSmall)` if `op > omax-2` (:220, :227).\n\n---\n\n# 3. HIST\n\n### `unsigned HIST_isError(size_t code)` — `compress/hist.c:24`. Forwards to `ERR_isError`.\n\n### `void HIST_add(unsigned* count, const void* src, size_t srcSize)` — `compress/hist.c:29`\n- Only the `while (ip<end)` loop. No configuration axes. `count` is **not** reset. Assumes `count` has 256 entries.\n\n### `unsigned HIST_count_simple(unsigned* count, unsigned* maxSymbolValuePtr, const void* src, size_t srcSize)` — `compress/hist.c:39`\n- **`srcSize == 0`** → `*maxSymbolValuePtr = 0`, return 0 (:48) — but note `count` is memset to `(maxSymbolValue+1)` entries *before* that check (:47).\n- `while (!count[maxSymbolValue]) maxSymbolValue--` (:55) → *maxSymbolValuePtr shrinks. **No bounds check**: if all counts are 0 this underflows — protected only by the srcSize==0 early return.\n- Never returns an error code. Unsafe if any byte `> *maxSymbolValuePtr` (assert only, :51).\n\n### `static size_t HIST_count_parallel_wksp(unsigned* count, unsigned* maxSymbolValuePtr, const void* source, size_t sourceSize, HIST_checkInput_e check, U32* workSpace)` — `compress/hist.c:76`\n- `HIST_checkInput_e` axis (:66): **`trustInput` (0)** vs **`checkMaxSymbolValue` (1)**. Only under `check` does :138 run `maxSymbolValue > *maxSymbolValuePtr` → `ERROR(maxSymbolValue_tooSmall)`.\n- `!sourceSize` → memset `count`, `*maxSymbolValuePtr = 0`, return 0 (:93-:97).\n- **Stripe-of-16 loop** condition `ip < iend-15` (:102) then a `while (ip<iend)` scalar tail into `Counting1` only (:128). Note the unconditional `MEM_read32(ip)` at :101 — this function is only ever reached with `sourceSize >= 1500`.\n- 4 interleaved 256-entry tables `Counting1..4` = `HIST_WKSP_SIZE_U32` **1024** U32 = 4096 bytes.\n\n### `size_t HIST_countFast_wksp(unsigned* count, unsigned* maxSymbolValuePtr, const void* source, size_t sourceSize, void* workSpace, size_t workSpaceSize)` — `compress/hist.c:150`\n- **`sourceSize < 1500`** (\"heuristic threshold\") → `HIST_count_simple` (:154). **This is the dominant size axis.**\n- `(size_t)workSpace & 3` → `ERROR(GENERIC)` (4-byte alignment) (:156).\n- `workSpaceSize < HIST_WKSP_SIZE` (**4096**) → `ERROR(workSpace_tooSmall)` (:157).\n- Else `HIST_count_parallel_wksp(..., trustInput, ...)`.\n\n### `size_t HIST_count_wksp(unsigned* count, unsigned* maxSymbolValuePtr, const void* source, size_t sourceSize, void* workSpace, size_t workSpaceSize)` — `compress/hist.c:164`\n- `workSpace & 3` → `ERROR(GENERIC)`; `workSpaceSize < 4096` → `ERROR(workSpace_tooSmall)` (:168-:169).\n- **`*maxSymbolValuePtr < 255`** → `HIST_count_parallel_wksp(..., checkMaxSymbolValue, ...)` — *always* the parallel path, **even for tiny sourceSize** (:170-:171).\n- **`*maxSymbolValuePtr == 255`** → forces `*maxSymbolValuePtr = 255` then delegates to `HIST_countFast_wksp`, which re-branches on the 1500 threshold (:172-:173).\n- Net: 3 distinct code paths keyed on `(maxSymbolValuePtr<255, sourceSize<1500)`.\n\n### `size_t HIST_countFast(...)` — `compress/hist.c:178`, `size_t HIST_count(...)` — `compress/hist.c:185`\n- Both only allocate `unsigned tmpCounters[1024]` on the stack and forward. Bodies exist only when `ZSTD_NO_UNUSED_FUNCTIONS` is **not** defined (:176).\n\n---\n\n# 4. HUF — compression (`compress/huf_compress.c`)\n\n### `size_t HUF_compressBound(size_t size)` — :821. No branches. `= 129 + size + (size>>8) + 8`.\n\n### `unsigned HUF_cardinality(const unsigned* count, unsigned maxSymbolValue)` — :1254. Loop only, counts nonzero entries.\n\n### `unsigned HUF_minTableLog(unsigned symbolCardinality)` — :1266. No branches; `highbit32(cardinality)+1`.\n\n### `unsigned HUF_optimalTableLog(unsigned maxTableLog, size_t srcSize, unsigned maxSymbolValue, void* workSpace, size_t wkspSize, HUF_CElt* table, const unsigned* count, int flags)` — :1272\n- **Primary axis: `flags & HUF_flags_optimalDepth` (1<<1)**. Unset → single-shot `FSE_optimalTableLog_internal(maxTableLog, srcSize, maxSymbolValue, /*minus*/1)` (:1284-:1287).\n- Set → search loop `optLogGuess` from `HUF_minTableLog(HUF_cardinality(count,maxSymbolValue))` up to `maxTableLog` (:1300), with sub-branches: `ERR_isError(maxBits)` → `continue` (:1304); **`maxBits < optLogGuess && optLogGuess > minTableLog` → `break`** (:1306); `ERR_isError(hSize)` → `continue` (:1311); **`newSize > optSize + 1` → `break`** (:1315); `newSize < optSize` → record (:1319).\n- Preconditions asserted: `srcSize > 1` (:1281), `wkspSize >= sizeof(HUF_buildCTable_wksp_tables)` (:1282). `HUF_OPTIMAL_DEPTH_THRESHOLD` = `ZSTD_btultra` (`huf.h:117`) — used by callers, not here.\n\n### `size_t HUF_buildCTable_wksp(HUF_CElt* tree, const unsigned* count, U32 maxSymbolValue, U32 maxNbBits, void* workSpace, size_t wkspSize)` — :755\n- `wkspSize < sizeof(HUF_buildCTable_wksp_tables)` → `ERROR(workSpace_tooSmall)` (:770). Required = `HUF_CTABLE_WORKSPACE_SIZE` = `((4*256)+192)*4` = **4864** bytes (static-asserted equal at :765).\n- **`maxNbBits == 0` → `HUF_TABLELOG_DEFAULT` (11)** (:772).\n- `maxSymbolValue > HUF_SYMBOLVALUE_MAX (255)` → `ERROR(maxSymbolValue_tooLarge)` (:773).\n- Workspace realigned to `ZSTD_ALIGNOF(U32)` via `HUF_alignUpWorkspace` (:112) — which itself branches on `*workspaceSizePtr >= add` and may return NULL.\n- After `HUF_setMaxHeight`: `maxNbBits > HUF_TABLELOG_MAX (12)` → `ERROR(GENERIC)` (:786).\n- **Returns `maxNbBits`** (the achieved tableLog), not 0.\n- Internal sub-axes worth knowing:\n  - `HUF_sort` (:620) — bucket sort with `RANK_POSITION_TABLE_SIZE 192`, `RANK_POSITION_MAX_COUNT_LOG 32`, `RANK_POSITION_LOG_BUCKETS_BEGIN` = **158**, `RANK_POSITION_DISTINCT_COUNT_CUTOFF` = **166**. `HUF_getIndex` (:530) branches `count < 166 ? count : highbit32(count)+158`. Per-bucket: `bucketSize > 1` → `HUF_simpleQuickSort` (:658).\n  - `HUF_simpleQuickSort` (:591): `high - low < kInsertionSortThreshold (8)` → `HUF_insertionSort`, else quicksort with tail-recursion elimination on `idx-low < high-idx` (:599).\n  - `HUF_setMaxHeight` (:376): **early exit `largestBits <= targetNbBits` → return largestBits unchanged** (:380) — the common case; otherwise the cost-repayment loop `while (totalCost > 0)` (:423) and the overshoot correction `while (totalCost < 0)` (:478) with the `rankLast[1] == noSymbol` special case (:482).\n  - `HUF_buildTree` (:681): `while (huffNode[nonNullRank].count == 0) nonNullRank--`; `STARTNODE` = 256.\n\n### `HUF_CTableHeader HUF_readCTableHeader(const HUF_CElt* ctable)` — :223. No branches, pure `memcpy`.\n\n### `U32 HUF_getNbBitsFromCTable(const HUF_CElt* symbolTable, U32 symbolValue)` — :345\n- One branch: `symbolValue > HUF_readCTableHeader(CTable).maxSymbolValue` → **return 0** (:349-:350). Assert `symbolValue <= 255`.\n\n### `size_t HUF_writeCTable_wksp(void* dst, size_t maxDstSize, const HUF_CElt* CTable, unsigned maxSymbolValue, unsigned huffLog, void* workspace, size_t workspaceSize)` — :248\n- `workspaceSize < sizeof(HUF_WriteCTableWksp)` → `ERROR(GENERIC)` (:263).\n- `maxSymbolValue > HUF_SYMBOLVALUE_MAX (255)` → `ERROR(maxSymbolValue_tooLarge)` (:264).\n- `maxDstSize < 1` → `ERROR(dstSize_tooSmall)` (:274).\n- **Header-format axis (:276)**: `(hSize > 1) & (hSize < maxSymbolValue/2)` → **FSE-compressed weights**, `op[0] = hSize`, return `hSize+1`. Otherwise fall through to **raw 4-bit weights**.\n- Raw path: `maxSymbolValue > 128` (`256-128`) → `ERROR(GENERIC)` (:282); `((maxSymbolValue+1)/2)+1 > maxDstSize` → `ERROR(dstSize_tooSmall)` (:283); writes `op[0] = 128 + (maxSymbolValue-1)`, returns `((maxSymbolValue+1)/2)+1`.\n- Asserts that the CTable header agrees with the passed `maxSymbolValue`/`huffLog` (:259-:260).\n\n### `static size_t HUF_compressWeights(void* dst, size_t dstSize, const void* weightTable, size_t wtSize, void* workspace, size_t workspaceSize)` — :146 (the surviving FSE_compress analogue)\n- `workspaceSize < sizeof(HUF_CompressWeightsWksp)` → `ERROR(GENERIC)` (:159).\n- **`wtSize <= 1` → return 0 (not compressible)** (:162).\n- **`maxCount == wtSize` → return 1 (RLE)** (:166).\n- **`maxCount == 1` → return 0 (each symbol at most once, not compressible)** (:167).\n- Fixed `tableLog = MAX_FSE_TABLELOG_FOR_HUFF_HEADER` (**6**), `maxSymbolValue = HUF_TABLELOG_MAX` (12), `useLowProbCount = 0` (:171).\n- `FSE_compress_usingCTable` returns 0 → return 0 (:181).\n\n### `size_t HUF_readCTable(HUF_CElt* CTable, unsigned* maxSymbolValuePtr, const void* src, size_t srcSize, unsigned* hasZeroWeights)` — :292\n- Propagates `HUF_readStats` errors (:301); sets `*hasZeroWeights = (rankVal[0] > 0)` (:302).\n- `tableLog > HUF_TABLELOG_MAX (12)` → `ERROR(tableLog_tooLarge)` (:305).\n- `nbSymbols > *maxSymbolValuePtr+1` → `ERROR(maxSymbolValue_tooSmall)` (:306).\n- Per-symbol `(BYTE)(tableLog + 1 - w) & -(w != 0)` — the `w == 0` (zero-weight) axis, branchless (:323).\n\n### `size_t HUF_estimateCompressedSize(const HUF_CElt* CTable, const unsigned* count, unsigned maxSymbolValue)` — :793. Loop only; returns `nbBits >> 3`.\n\n### `int HUF_validateCTable(const HUF_CElt* CTable, const unsigned* count, unsigned maxSymbolValue)` — :804\n- `header.maxSymbolValue < maxSymbolValue` → **return 0** (:812).\n- Else branchless accumulation of `count[s] != 0 && nbBits == 0`; return `!bad`.\n\n### `size_t HUF_compress1X_usingCTable(void* dst, size_t dstSize, const void* src, size_t srcSize, const HUF_CElt* CTable, int flags)` — :1162\n- **bmi2 dispatch axis** (:1138-:1147, only under `#if DYNAMIC_BMI2`): `flags & HUF_flags_bmi2 (1<<0)` → `_internal_bmi2` else `_internal_default`. Without `DYNAMIC_BMI2`, `flags` is ignored (:1156).\n- Body `HUF_compress1X_usingCTable_internal_body` (:1055) axes:\n  - **`dstSize < 8` → return 0** (:1068).\n  - `HUF_initCStream` error (`dstSize <= sizeof(size_t)`) → **return 0** (:1071).\n  - **Slow/safe loop selection (:1073)**: `dstSize < HUF_tightCompressBound(srcSize, tableLog)` (= `((srcSize*tableLog)>>3) + 8`) **OR `tableLog > 11`** → `kUnroll = MEM_32bits()?2:4, kFastFlush=0, kLastFast=0`.\n  - Else a **`switch (tableLog)`** with two different tables keyed on `MEM_32bits()`:\n    - 32-bit (:1077): `11` → (2,1,0); `10`/`9`/`8` → (2,1,1); `7`/default → (3,1,1).\n    - 64-bit (:1092): `11` → (5,1,0); `10` → (5,1,1); `9` → (6,1,0); `8` → (7,1,0); `7` → (8,1,0); `6`/default → (9,1,1).\n  - `HUF_compress1X_usingCTable_internal_body_loop` (:990) further branches on `srcSize % kUnroll` (:999) and `n % (2*kUnroll)` (:1008) join-up prologues.\n  - `HUF_closeCStream` (:973): **`bitC->ptr >= bitC->endPtr` → return 0 (overflow)**.\n\n### `size_t HUF_compress4X_usingCTable(void* dst, size_t dstSize, const void* src, size_t srcSize, const HUF_CElt* CTable, int flags)` — :1217 → `_internal` :1167\n- **`dstSize < 6+1+1+1+8` (i.e. `< 17`) → return 0** (:1179).\n- **`srcSize < 12` → return 0** (\"no saving possible : too small input\") (:1180).\n- Writes a 6-byte jump table; segments 1..3 are `segmentSize = (srcSize+3)/4`, segment 4 is the remainder.\n- Per-segment: **`cSize == 0 || cSize > 65535` → return 0** (:1185, :1193, :1201, :1210). (The 4th segment's size is not written to the jump table.)\n- Each segment recurses into `HUF_compress1X_usingCTable_internal` → the whole 1X tableLog/unroll matrix applies per segment.\n\n### `size_t HUF_compress1X_repeat(void* dst, size_t dstSize, const void* src, size_t srcSize, unsigned maxSymbolValue, unsigned tableLog, void* workSpace, size_t wkspSize, HUF_CElt* hufTable, HUF_repeat* repeat, int flags)` — :1436\n### `size_t HUF_compress4X_repeat(...same signature...)` — :1453\nBoth are thin wrappers passing `HUF_singleStream` / `HUF_fourStreams` (`HUF_nbStreams_e`, :1222) into `HUF_compress_internal` (:1332). All the axes are there:\n- `wkspSize < sizeof(HUF_compress_tables_t)` → `ERROR(workSpace_tooSmall)` (:1349). `HUF_WORKSPACE_SIZE` = `(8<<10)+512` = **8704**, and `sizeof(*table) + HUF_WORKSPACE_MAX_ALIGNMENT(8) <= 8704` is static-asserted (:1346).\n- **`srcSize == 0` → return 0** (:1350).\n- **`dstSize == 0` → return 0** (:1351).\n- **`srcSize > HUF_BLOCKSIZE_MAX (128*1024 = 131072)` → `ERROR(srcSize_wrong)`** (:1352).\n- `huffLog > HUF_TABLELOG_MAX (12)` → `ERROR(tableLog_tooLarge)` (:1353).\n- `maxSymbolValue > HUF_SYMBOLVALUE_MAX (255)` → `ERROR(maxSymbolValue_tooLarge)` (:1354).\n- **`maxSymbolValue == 0` → 255** (:1355); **`huffLog == 0` → `HUF_TABLELOG_DEFAULT` (11)** (:1356).\n- **Repeat mode axis #1 (:1359)**: `(flags & HUF_flags_preferRepeat) && repeat && *repeat == HUF_repeat_valid` → **immediately** `HUF_compressCTable_internal` with `oldHufTable`, skipping histogram entirely.\n- **Uncompressible-sampling axis (:1367)**: `(flags & HUF_flags_suspectUncompressible) && srcSize >= SUSPECT_INCOMPRESSIBLE_SAMPLE_SIZE * SUSPECT_INCOMPRESSIBLE_SAMPLE_RATIO` = `4096 * 10` = **40960** → two `HIST_count_simple` calls of 4096 bytes each (head and tail); `largestTotal <= ((2*4096)>>7)+4` = **68** → **return 0**.\n- Full histogram `HIST_count_wksp` (:1382), then:\n  - **`largest == srcSize` → write 1 byte, return 1 (RLE)** (:1383).\n  - **`largest <= (srcSize>>7)+4` → return 0 (incompressible heuristic)** (:1384).\n- **Repeat mode axis #2 (:1389)**: `repeat && *repeat == HUF_repeat_check && !HUF_validateCTable(...)` → `*repeat = HUF_repeat_none`.\n- **Repeat mode axis #3 (:1395)**: `(flags & HUF_flags_preferRepeat) && repeat && *repeat != HUF_repeat_none` → use old table.\n- `HUF_optimalTableLog` (:1402, so `HUF_flags_optimalDepth` matters here) → `HUF_buildCTable_wksp` → `huffLog = maxBits` (**tableLog reduction**, :1407).\n- `HUF_writeCTable_wksp` (:1412), then **repeat-beneficial axis (:1415-:1422)**: `repeat && *repeat != HUF_repeat_none` and (`oldSize <= hSize + newSize` **or** `hSize + 12 >= srcSize`) → use old table.\n- **`hSize + 12 >= srcSize` → return 0** (:1425).\n- On the new-table path: `*repeat = HUF_repeat_none` (:1427), and `oldHufTable` (if non-NULL) is overwritten (:1428-:1429).\n- `HUF_compressCTable_internal` (:1224) final axes: `cSize == 0` → return 0; **`(op-ostart) >= srcSize-1` → return 0** (compressibility check, :1237).\n- `HUF_repeat` enum values: `HUF_repeat_none=0`, `HUF_repeat_check=1`, `HUF_repeat_valid=2` (`huf.h:139-143`).\n\n### Complete `HUF_flags_e` set — `common/huf.h:80-111`\n`HUF_flags_bmi2 = 1<<0`, `HUF_flags_optimalDepth = 1<<1`, `HUF_flags_preferRepeat = 1<<2`, `HUF_flags_suspectUncompressible = 1<<3`, `HUF_flags_disableAsm = 1<<4`, `HUF_flags_disableFast = 1<<5`. (Six flags; 0 is the default for all.)\n\n---\n\n# 5. HUF — `HUF_readStats` (`common/entropy_common.c`)\n\n### `size_t HUF_readStats(BYTE* huffWeight, size_t hwSize, U32* rankStats, U32* nbSymbolsPtr, U32* tableLogPtr, const void* src, size_t srcSize)` — :234\n- No branches: allocates `U32 wksp[HUF_READ_STATS_WORKSPACE_SIZE_U32]` on the stack and calls `HUF_readStats_wksp` with **`flags = 0`** (so always the non-BMI2 body). `HUF_READ_STATS_WORKSPACE_SIZE_U32` = `FSE_DECOMPRESS_WKSP_SIZE_U32(6, 11)` (`huf.h:181`).\n\n### `size_t HUF_readStats_wksp(BYTE* huffWeight, size_t hwSize, U32* rankStats, U32* nbSymbolsPtr, U32* tableLogPtr, const void* src, size_t srcSize, void* workspace, size_t wkspSize, int flags)` — :327\n- **Dispatch axis**: `DYNAMIC_BMI2 && (flags & HUF_flags_bmi2)` → `HUF_readStats_body_bmi2` (:318) else `_body_default` (:309).\n- Body `HUF_readStats_body` (:242) — the two **header-format paths**:\n  - `!srcSize` → `ERROR(srcSize_wrong)` (:254).\n  - **`iSize = ip[0] >= 128`** → **raw 4-bit weights path** (:258-:268): `oSize = iSize - 127`, `iSize = (oSize+1)/2`; checks `iSize+1 > srcSize` → `srcSize_wrong`, `oSize >= hwSize` → `corruption_detected`; then unpacks nibbles (`>>4` and `&15`).\n  - **`iSize < 128`** → **FSE-compressed weights path** (:269-:274): `iSize+1 > srcSize` → `srcSize_wrong`; `FSE_decompress_wksp_bmi2(huffWeight, hwSize-1, ip+1, iSize, /*maxLog*/ 6, workSpace, wkspSize, bmi2)`; error propagated.\n  - Common validation: `huffWeight[n] > HUF_TABLELOG_MAX (12)` → `corruption_detected` (:280); `weightTotal == 0` → `corruption_detected` (:284); `tableLog = highbit32(weightTotal)+1 > 12` → `corruption_detected` (:288); last implied weight `verif != rest` → `corruption_detected` (**must be a clean power of 2**, :295); **`(rankStats[1] < 2) || (rankStats[1] & 1)` → `corruption_detected`** (at least 2, and an even number of, rank-1 elements, :301).\n  - Returns `iSize + 1`; sets `*nbSymbolsPtr = oSize+1`, `*tableLogPtr`.\n\n---\n\n# 6. HUF — decompression (`decompress/huf_decompress.c`)\n\nKey constants: `HUF_DECODER_FAST_TABLELOG` = **11** (:31); `HUF_ENABLE_FAST_DECODE` = 1 unless `HUF_DISABLE_FAST_DECODE` (:37-:41); `HUF_DECOMPRESS_WORKSPACE_SIZE` = `(2<<10)+(1<<9)` = **2560** (`huf.h:235`).\n\n### `size_t HUF_readDTableX1_wksp(HUF_DTable* DTable, const void* src, size_t srcSize, void* workSpace, size_t wkspSize, int flags)` — :385\n- `sizeof(HUF_ReadDTableX1_Workspace) > wkspSize` → `ERROR(tableLog_tooLarge)` (:395).\n- `HUF_readStats_wksp` errors propagate (flags carries `HUF_flags_bmi2` through, :400).\n- **`HUF_rescaleStats` axis (:352-:375, called at :408)**: `targetTableLog = MIN(dtd.maxTableLog+1, HUF_DECODER_FAST_TABLELOG(11))`; `tableLog > targetTableLog` → no-op; `tableLog < targetTableLog` → **all non-zero weights bumped by `scale`, rankVal shifted** (this is what makes the fast loop usable).\n- `tableLog > dtd.maxTableLog+1` → `ERROR(tableLog_tooLarge)` (:409). Sets `dtd.tableType = 0`.\n- **DTable fill `switch (length)`** where `length = (1<<w)>>1` (:465): cases `1`, `2`, `4` (one `MEM_write64`), `8` (two `MEM_write64`), `default` (16-at-a-time loop). `HUF_DEltX1_set4` (:335) branches on `MEM_isLittleEndian()`.\n- Returns `iSize`.\n\n### `size_t HUF_readDTableX2_wksp(HUF_DTable* DTable, const void* src, size_t srcSize, void* workSpace, size_t wkspSize, int flags)` — :1179\n- `sizeof(HUF_ReadDTableX2_Workspace) > wkspSize` → `ERROR(GENERIC)` (:1193).\n- `dtd.maxTableLog > HUF_TABLELOG_MAX (12)` → `ERROR(tableLog_tooLarge)` (:1200).\n- `HUF_readStats_wksp` errors propagate (:1203).\n- `tableLog > maxTableLog` → `ERROR(tableLog_tooLarge)` (:1207).\n- **`tableLog <= HUF_DECODER_FAST_TABLELOG(11) && maxTableLog > 11` → `maxTableLog = 11`** (:1208) — the axis that lets the fast loop engage for X2.\n- `maxW` found by scanning down from `tableLog` (:1211).\n- `HUF_fillDTableX2` (:1124) axis: per weight `w`, **`targetLog - nbBits >= minBits`** → \"enough room for a second symbol\" → `HUF_fillDTableX2Level2` (double-symbol entries, level 2); else single-symbol (`level 1`) fill (:1141 vs :1159). `HUF_fillDTableX2Level2` (:1069) branches `minWeight > 1` → skip-fill with `switch (length)` cases `2`/`4`/`default` (:1084). `HUF_fillDTableX2ForWeight` (:1010) has `switch (length)` cases `1`/`2`/`4`/`8`/`default` (:1019). `HUF_buildDEltX2U32` (:961) branches on `MEM_isLittleEndian()` and `level == 1`.\n- Sets `dtd.tableLog = maxTableLog`, **`dtd.tableType = 1`**; returns `iSize`.\n\n### `U32 HUF_selectDecoder(size_t dstSize, size_t cSrcSize)` — :1821\n- Compile-time axes: `HUF_FORCE_DECOMPRESS_X1` → always 0; `HUF_FORCE_DECOMPRESS_X2` → always 1 (:1825-:1832).\n- Default: `Q = (cSrcSize >= dstSize) ? 15 : (cSrcSize*16/dstSize)` (so **Q ∈ [0,15]**, Q==0/1 are marked \"impossible\" in `algoTime`, :1797-:1798); `D256 = dstSize >> 8`; `DTime1 += DTime1 >> 5` (bias toward X1); returns `DTime1 < DTime0`. Table `algoTime[16][2]` at :1794-:1813.\n- Asserts `dstSize > 0 && dstSize <= 128*1024`.\n\n### `size_t HUF_decompress1X_DCtx_wksp(HUF_DTable* dctx, void* dst, size_t dstSize, const void* cSrc, size_t cSrcSize, void* workSpace, size_t wkspSize, int flags)` — :1845\n- **`dstSize == 0` → `ERROR(dstSize_tooSmall)`** (:1850).\n- **`cSrcSize > dstSize` → `ERROR(corruption_detected)`** (:1851).\n- **`cSrcSize == dstSize` → plain `memcpy`, return dstSize (not compressed)** (:1852).\n- **`cSrcSize == 1` → `memset(dst, *cSrc, dstSize)`, return dstSize (RLE)** (:1853).\n- Else `HUF_selectDecoder` → `HUF_decompress1X2_DCtx_wksp` (algoNb=1) or `HUF_decompress1X1_DCtx_wksp` (algoNb=0) (:1855-:1871).\n\n### `size_t HUF_decompress4X_hufOnly_wksp(HUF_DTable* dctx, void* dst, size_t dstSize, const void* cSrc, size_t cSrcSize, void* workSpace, size_t wkspSize, int flags)` — :1924\n- **`dstSize == 0` → `ERROR(dstSize_tooSmall)`** (:1927).\n- **`cSrcSize == 0` → `ERROR(corruption_detected)`** (:1928).\n- **No memcpy/RLE shortcuts** (unlike 1X) — this is the key difference from `HUF_decompress1X_DCtx_wksp`.\n- `HUF_selectDecoder` → `HUF_decompress4X2_DCtx_wksp` (:1769, static) or `HUF_decompress4X1_DCtx_wksp` (:930, static).\n\n### `size_t HUF_decompress1X1_DCtx_wksp(HUF_DTable* dctx, void* dst, size_t dstSize, const void* cSrc, size_t cSrcSize, void* workSpace, size_t wkspSize, int flags)` — :1894 (guarded `#ifndef HUF_FORCE_DECOMPRESS_X2`)\n### `size_t HUF_decompress1X2_DCtx_wksp(HUF_DTable* DCtx, ...same...)` — :1754 (guarded `#ifndef HUF_FORCE_DECOMPRESS_X1`)\nBoth: read the DTable, then **`hSize >= cSrcSize` → `ERROR(srcSize_wrong)`** (:1900 / :1763), then `..._usingDTable_internal`.\n\n### `size_t HUF_decompress1X_usingDTable(void* dst, size_t maxDstSize, const void* cSrc, size_t cSrcSize, const HUF_DTable* DTable, int flags)` — :1876\n- **`dtd.tableType` axis** (byte 1 of DTable[0]): `1` → X2 (double-symbol), `0` → X1 (:1888-:1889). Overridden at compile time by `HUF_FORCE_DECOMPRESS_X1/X2`.\n- The `_internal` here comes from `HUF_DGEN` (:98/:127): under `DYNAMIC_BMI2`, `flags & HUF_flags_bmi2` → `_bmi2` clone else `_default`. **`HUF_flags_disableAsm` / `HUF_flags_disableFast` do NOT apply to the 1X path** — there is no fast/asm loop for single-stream.\n- `HUF_decompress1X1_usingDTable_internal_body` (:574): `BIT_initDStream` failure propagates; `!BIT_endOfDStream` → `ERROR(corruption_detected)` (:592).\n- `HUF_decompress1X2_usingDTable_internal_body` (:1352): same shape (:1361, :1373).\n\n### `size_t HUF_decompress4X_usingDTable(void* dst, size_t maxDstSize, const void* cSrc, size_t cSrcSize, const HUF_DTable* DTable, int flags)` — :1907\n- **`dtd.tableType`** → `HUF_decompress4X2_usingDTable_internal` (:1719) or `HUF_decompress4X1_usingDTable_internal` (:897).\n- Each of those has the **full 3-way dispatch** (:897-:928 / :1719-:1750):\n  1. `#if DYNAMIC_BMI2`: `flags & HUF_flags_bmi2` unset → **immediately** return `fallbackFn` (the plain C 4-stream body); no fast loop at all.\n  2. Set → `fallbackFn = ..._bmi2`, and if `ZSTD_ENABLE_ASM_X86_64_BMI2 && !(flags & HUF_flags_disableAsm)` → `loopFn = ..._fast_asm_loop`.\n  3. `HUF_ENABLE_FAST_DECODE && !(flags & HUF_flags_disableFast)` → try `..._usingDTable_internal_fast(...)`; **`ret != 0` → return it, `ret == 0` → fall back**.\n- **`HUF_DecompressFastArgs_init` (:191) — the complete set of \"fall back to slow\" conditions** (returns 0) vs errors:\n  - `!MEM_isLittleEndian() || MEM_32bits()` → 0 (:203).\n  - `dstSize == 0` → 0 (:207).\n  - **`srcSize < 10` → `ERROR(corruption_detected)`** (:212).\n  - **`dtLog != HUF_DECODER_FAST_TABLELOG (11)` → 0** (:219).\n  - **any of `length1/2/3/4 < 8` → 0** (:236).\n  - `length4 > srcSize` → `ERROR(corruption_detected)` (:238).\n  - **`args->op[3] >= oend` → 0** (\"no point for tiny outputs\", :253) where `op[i] = dst + i*((dstSize+3)/4)`.\n  - `bits[i]` primed by `HUF_initFastDStream` (:150), which requires 8 readable bytes per stream.\n- After the loop, `HUF_initRemainingDStream` (:281): `args->op[stream] > segmentEnd` → `corruption_detected`; `args->ip[stream] < args->iend[stream] - 8` → `corruption_detected`; then each stream is finished with `HUF_decodeStreamX1`/`X2` and **`args.op[i] != segmentEnd` → `corruption_detected`** (:886 / :1710).\n- Plain-C 4-stream bodies `HUF_decompress4X1_usingDTable_internal_body` (:601) / `4X2` (:1383):\n  - **`cSrcSize < 10` → `corruption_detected`** (:608 / :1389).\n  - **`dstSize < 6` → `corruption_detected`** (\"stream 4-split doesn't work\") (:609 / :1390).\n  - `length4 > cSrcSize` → `corruption_detected`; `opStart4 > oend` → `corruption_detected` (:643-:644 / :1424-:1425).\n  - Four `BIT_initDStream` on `(istart1,length1)…(istart4,length4)`.\n  - Main-loop guard **`(size_t)(oend - op4) >= sizeof(size_t)`** (:652 / :1433) and `op4 < olimit` where `olimit = oend-3` for X1 and `oend-(sizeof(size_t)-1)` for X2.\n  - Symbol macros: `HUF_DECODE_SYMBOLX1_1` gated on `MEM_64bits() || HUF_TABLELOG_MAX<=12` (always true here), `_2` gated on `MEM_64bits()` (:533-:543). Same shape for X2 (:1295-:1305).\n  - X2 main loop has a **`__clang__ && (x86_64||i386)` variant** with per-pair reloads vs. the generic interleaved variant (:1435-:1478).\n  - Post-loop `op1 > opStart2` / `op2 > opStart3` / `op3 > opStart4` → `corruption_detected` (:680-:682 / :1483-:1485).\n  - Final `BIT_endOfDStream` AND over all 4 streams → `corruption_detected` (:692 / :1495).\n  - Returns `dstSize`.\n-