stack-buffer path, easy to miss.\n4. **HUF header format**: `ip[0] >= 128` (raw nibbles) vs `< 128` (FSE-compressed) in `HUF_readStats_body` (`common/entropy_common.c:258`); mirrored on the write side by `(hSize>1) & (hSize < maxSymbolValue/2)` in `HUF_writeCTable_wksp` (`compress/huf_compress.c:276`).\n5. **HUF 1X encode `switch (tableLog)` × `MEM_32bits()`** (`compress/huf_compress.c:1073-:1114`) — 12 distinct `(kUnroll, kFastFlush, kLastFast)` instantiations plus the slow path.\n6. **HUF 4X decode fast-loop bail-outs** — `HUF_DecompressFastArgs_init` (`decompress/huf_decompress.c:191`) returns 0 (silent fallback) for 5 different reasons and errors for 2; distinguishing them matters for equivalence testing.\n7. **`HIST_count_wksp`'s three paths** keyed on `(*maxSymbolValuePtr < 255, sourceSize < 1500)` (`compress/hist.c:164-174`).\n8. **XXH32 `large_len` vs XXH64 `total_len >= 32`** — the two streaming digests use structurally different \"did we ever see a full stripe\" tests.","usage":{"total_tokens":167731,"tool_uses":29,"duration_ms":356035},"uuid":"4cc1980e-90f2-4ee1-b911-4f87b527c7c9","session_id":"73cb0b47-bb13-46d2-9cdb-cbadffb29d99"}
