{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01AkKvD3avK3FFVDxTPqLbh6","type":"tool_result","content":"        for (u=0; u<=offcodeMax; u++) {\n            DISPLAYLEVEL(4, \"%2u :%7u \\n\", u, offcodeCount[u]);\n    }   }\n\n    /* analyze, build stats, starting with literals */\n    {   size_t maxNbBits = HUF_buildCTable_wksp(hufTable, countLit, 255, huffLog, wksp, sizeof(wksp));\n        if (HUF_isError(maxNbBits)) {\n            eSize = maxNbBits;\n            DISPLAYLEVEL(1, \" HUF_buildCTable error \\n\");\n            goto _cleanup;\n        }\n        if (maxNbBits==8) {  /* not compressible : will fail on HUF_writeCTable() */\n            DISPLAYLEVEL(2, \"warning : pathological dataset : literals are not compressible : samples are noisy or too regular \\n\");\n            ZDICT_flatLit(countLit);  /* replace distribution by a fake \"mostly flat but still compressible\" distribution, that HUF_writeCTable() can encode */\n            maxNbBits = HUF_buildCTable_wksp(hufTable, countLit, 255, huffLog, wksp, sizeof(wksp));\n            assert(maxNbBits==9);\n        }\n        huffLog = (U32)maxNbBits;\n    }\n\n    /* looking for most common first offsets */\n    {   U32 offset;\n        for (offset=1; offset<MAXREPOFFSET; offset++)\n            ZDICT_insertSortCount(bestRepOffset, offset, repOffset[offset]);\n    }\n    /* note : the result of this phase should be used to better appreciate the impact on statistics */\n\n    total=0; for (u=0; u<=offcodeMax; u++) total+=offcodeCount[u];\n    errorCode = FSE_normalizeCount(offcodeNCount, Offlog, offcodeCount, total, offcodeMax, /* useLowProbCount */ 1);\n    if (FSE_isError(errorCode)) {\n        eSize = errorCode;\n        DISPLAYLEVEL(1, \"FSE_normalizeCount error with offcodeCount \\n\");\n        goto _cleanup;\n    }\n    Offlog = (U32)errorCode;\n\n    total=0; for (u=0; u<=MaxML; u++) total+=matchLengthCount[u];\n    errorCode = FSE_normalizeCount(matchLengthNCount, mlLog, matchLengthCount, total, MaxML, /* useLowProbCount */ 1);\n    if (FSE_isError(errorCode)) {\n        eSize = errorCode;\n        DISPLAYLEVEL(1, \"FSE_normalizeCount error with matchLengthCount \\n\");\n        goto _cleanup;\n    }\n    mlLog = (U32)errorCode;\n\n    total=0; for (u=0; u<=MaxLL; u++) total+=litLengthCount[u];\n    errorCode = FSE_normalizeCount(litLengthNCount, llLog, litLengthCount, total, MaxLL, /* useLowProbCount */ 1);\n    if (FSE_isError(errorCode)) {\n        eSize = errorCode;\n        DISPLAYLEVEL(1, \"FSE_normalizeCount error with litLengthCount \\n\");\n        goto _cleanup;\n    }\n    llLog = (U32)errorCode;\n\n    /* write result to buffer */\n    {   size_t const hhSize = HUF_writeCTable_wksp(dstPtr, maxDstSize, hufTable, 255, huffLog, wksp, sizeof(wksp));\n        if (HUF_isError(hhSize)) {\n            eSize = hhSize;\n            DISPLAYLEVEL(1, \"HUF_writeCTable error \\n\");\n            goto _cleanup;\n        }\n        dstPtr += hhSize;\n        maxDstSize -= hhSize;\n        eSize += hhSize;\n    }\n\n    {   size_t const ohSize = FSE_writeNCount(dstPtr, maxDstSize, offcodeNCount, OFFCODE_MAX, Offlog);\n        if (FSE_isError(ohSize)) {\n            eSize = ohSize;\n            DISPLAYLEVEL(1, \"FSE_writeNCount error with offcodeNCount \\n\");\n            goto _cleanup;\n        }\n        dstPtr += ohSize;\n        maxDstSize -= ohSize;\n        eSize += ohSize;\n    }\n\n    {   size_t const mhSize = FSE_writeNCount(dstPtr, maxDstSize, matchLengthNCount, MaxML, mlLog);\n        if (FSE_isError(mhSize)) {\n            eSize = mhSize;\n            DISPLAYLEVEL(1, \"FSE_writeNCount error with matchLengthNCount \\n\");\n            goto _cleanup;\n        }\n        dstPtr += mhSize;\n        maxDstSize -= mhSize;\n        eSize += mhSize;\n    }\n\n    {   size_t const lhSize = FSE_writeNCount(dstPtr, maxDstSize, litLengthNCount, MaxLL, llLog);\n        if (FSE_isError(lhSize)) {\n            eSize = lhSize;\n            DISPLAYLEVEL(1, \"FSE_writeNCount error with litlengthNCount \\n\");\n            goto _cleanup;\n        }\n        dstPtr += lhSize;\n        maxDstSize -= lhSize;\n        eSize += lhSize;\n    }\n\n    if (maxDstSize<12) {\n        eSize = ERROR(dstSize_tooSmall);\n        DISPLAYLEVEL(1, \"not enough space to write RepOffsets \\n\");\n        goto _cleanup;\n    }\n# if 0\n    MEM_writeLE32(dstPtr+0, bestRepOffset[0].offset);\n    MEM_writeLE32(dstPtr+4, bestRepOffset[1].offset);\n    MEM_writeLE32(dstPtr+8, bestRepOffset[2].offset);\n#else\n    /* at this stage, we don't use the result of \"most common first offset\",\n     * as the impact of statistics is not properly evaluated */\n    MEM_writeLE32(dstPtr+0, repStartValue[0]);\n    MEM_writeLE32(dstPtr+4, repStartValue[1]);\n    MEM_writeLE32(dstPtr+8, repStartValue[2]);\n#endif\n    eSize += 12;\n\n_cleanup:\n    ZSTD_freeCDict(esr.dict);\n    ZSTD_freeCCtx(esr.zc);\n    free(esr.workPlace);\n\n    return eSize;\n}\n\n\n/**\n * @returns the maximum repcode value\n */\nstatic U32 ZDICT_maxRep(U32 const reps[ZSTD_REP_NUM])\n{\n    U32 maxRep = reps[0];\n    int r;\n    for (r = 1; r < ZSTD_REP_NUM; ++r)\n        maxRep = MAX(maxRep, reps[r]);\n    return maxRep;\n}\n\nsize_t ZDICT_finalizeDictionary(void* dictBuffer, size_t dictBufferCapacity,\n                          const void* customDictContent, size_t dictContentSize,\n                          const void* samplesBuffer, const size_t* samplesSizes,","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_017Kzzkdw62jfPRE91XmeNz9","session_id":"73cb0b47-bb13-46d2-9cdb-cbadffb29d99","uuid":"f94cc09c-b8ed-4ca0-b616-8522b6da5e4f","timestamp":"2026-08-31T10:43:33.406Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Enumerate dictBuilder error branches"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_2jpfetabpgbfghz723skkboxbjwbkjs5d35aka66t3ydhx5evjaa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01C1Mf9xFiLip3BNqL4SEpV6","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Entropy + xxhash differential tests","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"Working dir: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-iPPPON\n\nTask: write ONE new Rust integration test file `translation/tests/t05_entropy.rs` containing differential tests for the low-level ENTROPY + XXHASH API of zstd, comparing the C `.so` against the Rust `.so` through FFI.\n\nCONTEXT / RULES (important):\n- `c_src/` is the C ground truth. READ IT, NEVER MODIFY IT. The C is ALWAYS correct; if C looks weird, replicate it.\n- The Rust crate is at `translation/`. Run cargo ONLY as: `cd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-iPPPON/translation && cargo test --release --offline --test t05_entropy`. You MUST pass `--offline` (no network). Use `timeout 600`.\n- Both .so files are already built:\n  - C:    `c_src/build/libzstd.so`\n  - Rust: `translation/target/release/libzstd.so`\n  - Rebuild Rust with `cargo build --release --offline` after any src change.\n- NEVER call Rust functions directly. Always load BOTH .so via `libloading` and call exported symbols.\n- A shared harness ALREADY EXISTS at `translation/tests/common/mod.rs`. READ IT FIRST and reuse it. It gives you:\n  - `mod common; use common::*;`\n  - `impls() -> &'static Impls` and `impls().pair::<FnType>(\"symbol_name\") -> (c_sym, rust_sym)` (panics if either .so lacks the symbol)\n  - `Rng::new(seed)` deterministic PRNG with `.next_u64() .next_u32() .below(n) .range(lo,hi) .byte() .bool()`\n  - `Shape`, `ALL_SHAPES`, `gen_shape(shape, len, &mut rng)`, `EDGE_LENS`\n  - `assert_bytes_eq(ctx, c, r)` and `assert_eq_dbg(ctx, c, r)`\n  - zstd/FSE error-code constants\n  Follow the same style as the existing `translation/tests/t01_basic.rs` and `t02_params.rs` (read them for the established pattern).\n\nSCOPE — cover these exported symbols (confirm exact names/signatures by reading the C headers `c_src/src/common/fse.h`, `c_src/src/common/huf.h`, `c_src/src/common/xxhash.h`, `c_src/src/compress/hist.h`, and the implementations in `c_src/src/common/{entropy_common,fse_decompress}.c`, `c_src/src/compress/{fse_compress,huf_compress,hist}.c`, `c_src/src/decompress/huf_decompress.c`, `c_src/src/common/xxhash.c`):\n\nFSE: FSE_compress, FSE_compress2, FSE_decompress, FSE_compressBound, FSE_isError, FSE_getErrorName, FSE_normalizeCount, FSE_writeNCount, FSE_readNCount, FSE_readNCount_bmi2, FSE_optimalTableLog, FSE_optimalTableLog_internal, FSE_buildCTable, FSE_buildCTable_wksp, FSE_buildDTable_wksp (or FSE_buildDTable*), FSE_decompress_wksp, FSE_decompress_wksp_bmi2, FSE_compress_usingCTable, FSE_count* / FSE_NCountWriteBound, FSE_sizeof_CTable, FSE_createCTable/FSE_freeCTable, FSE_createDTable/FSE_freeDTable, FSE_buildCTable_raw, FSE_buildCTable_rle, FSE_buildDTable_raw, FSE_buildDTable_rle, FSE_decompress_usingDTable, FSE_compress_usingCTable_bmi2, FSE_versionNumber.\nHUF: HUF_compress, HUF_compress1X, HUF_compress1X_wksp, HUF_compress1X_usingCTable, HUF_compress2, HUF_compress4X_wksp, HUF_compress4X_repeat, HUF_compress1X_repeat, HUF_compressBound, HUF_isError, HUF_getErrorName, HUF_readStats, HUF_readStats_wksp, HUF_readCTable, HUF_writeCTable_wksp, HUF_buildCTable, HUF_buildCTable_wksp, HUF_optimalTableLog, HUF_estimateCompressedSize, HUF_validateCTable, HUF_getNbBits / HUF_getNbBitsFromCTable, HUF_decompress, HUF_decompress1X1, HUF_decompress1X2, HUF_decompress4X1, HUF_decompress4X2, HUF_decompress1X_DCtx, HUF_decompress4X_hufOnly*, HUF_decompress1X1_DCtx_wksp, HUF_decompress4X_usingDTable*, HUF_readDTableX1*/X2*, HUF_selectDecoder, HUF_decompress*_usingDTable_bmi2 — whatever the .so actually exports (check with `nm -D --defined-only c_src/build/libzstd.so | grep -E '^.* (FSE|HUF|HIST|ZSTD_XXH)'`).\nHIST: HIST_count, HIST_count_simple, HIST_count_wksp, HIST_countFast, HIST_countFast_wksp, HIST_isError.\nXXHASH (namespaced ZSTD_): ZSTD_XXH32, ZSTD_XXH64, ZSTD_XXH32_createState/freeState/reset/update/digest/copyState, ZSTD_XXH64_* equivalents, ZSTD_XXH32_canonicalFromHash/hashFromCanonical, ZSTD_XXH64_canonicalFromHash/hashFromCanonical, ZSTD_XXH_versionNumber, and any ZSTD_XXH3_* if exported.\n\nREQUIREMENTS:\n- Property-style randomized testing with FIXED seeds. Many inputs per function (dozens+), not one hand-picked value.\n- Cover input SHAPES and SIZES: empty (0), 1 byte, 2, 3, 7/8/9, powers of two, sizes around FSE/HUF internal limits, large (>64KB), and all `ALL_SHAPES` distributions. Single-symbol input (RLE), 2-symbol, full 256-symbol alphabet, and highly skewed histograms are important — FSE/HUF special-case these.\n- Cover PARAMETER axes: maxSymbolValue (0, 1, 2, 127, 255, and out-of-range like 256/65535), tableLog (below FSE_MIN_TABLELOG, at min, typical, at FSE_MAX_TABLELOG, above max), and HUF tableLog variants (including HUF_TABLELOG_MAX and above).\n- ERROR PATHS (mandatory): dstCapacity too small (sweep 0..exact), srcSize==0, NULL pointers where the C tolerates/checks them, maxSymbolValue too large, tableLog too large, corrupted/ bit-flipped compressed input to FSE_decompress/HUF_decompress*, workspace too small for the *_wksp variants. Assert the SAME error code (use FSE_isError/HUF_isError + the numeric return), not merely \"both failed\".\n- For xxhash: streaming (reset/update in randomized chunk splits/digest) must equal one-shot, and must match C bit-for-bit; also cover seeds 0/1/max and canonical round trips.\n- For byte-output functions compare the FULL output buffer contents byte-for-byte, and also compare untouched bytes beyond the written length are treated consistently (compare only the written prefix if the C leaves the tail undefined — be careful not to create false failures from genuinely-undefined tail bytes; if you find a case where the C leaves tail bytes untouched, only compare the reported length).\n- Be careful with functions taking opaque table pointers (FSE_CTable*/HUF_CElt*): allocate with the documented size macros, and build the table with the SAME library that will consume it, then ALSO cross-check that C-built tables and Rust-built tables are byte-identical (that is a strong equality check).\n\nIF YOU FIND A DIVERGENCE: fix the RUST source in `translation/src/**` (never c_src). Root-cause it by reading the corresponding C. Rebuild and re-run until green. Report every divergence you fixed with file+what was wrong.\n\nIterate until `timeout 600 cargo test --release --offline --test t05_entropy` passes fully. Keep individual tests fast (whole file well under 300s); if one sweep is too slow, reduce iteration counts rather than dropping coverage areas.\n\nAt the end report: the test file path, number of #[test] functions, the list of symbols actually exercised, the pass/fail status of the final run, and any Rust bugs you fixed."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1802,"cache_read_input_tokens":84785,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1802,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"73cb0b47-bb13-46d2-9cdb-cbadffb29d99","uuid":"be826df2-bc39-42ba-98a5-fa11806beab4","timestamp":"2026-08-31T10:43:33.729Z"}
