- `c_src/` is the C ground truth. READ IT, NEVER MODIFY IT. The C is ALWAYS correct; if C looks weird, replicate it.\n- The Rust crate is at `translation/`. Run cargo ONLY as: `cd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-iPPPON/translation && cargo test --release --offline --test t05_entropy`. You MUST pass `--offline` (no network). Use `timeout 600`.\n- Both .so files are already built:\n  - C:    `c_src/build/libzstd.so`\n  - Rust: `translation/target/release/libzstd.so`\n  - Rebuild Rust with `cargo build --release --offline` after any src change.\n- NEVER call Rust functions directly. Always load BOTH .so via `libloading` and call exported symbols.\n- A shared harness ALREADY EXISTS at `translation/tests/common/mod.rs`. READ IT FIRST and reuse it. It gives you:\n  - `mod common; use common::*;`\n  - `impls() -> &'static Impls` and `impls().pair::<FnType>(\"symbol_name\") -> (c_sym, rust_sym)` (panics if either .so lacks the symbol)\n  - `Rng::new(seed)` deterministic PRNG with `.next_u64() .next_u32() .below(n) .range(lo,hi) .byte() .bool()`\n  - `Shape`, `ALL_SHAPES`, `gen_shape(shape, len, &mut rng)`, `EDGE_LENS`\n  - `assert_bytes_eq(ctx, c, r)` and `assert_eq_dbg(ctx, c, r)`\n  - zstd/FSE error-code constants\n  Follow the same style as the existing `translation/tests/t01_basic.rs` and `t02_params.rs` (read them for the established pattern).\n\nSCOPE — cover these exported symbols (confirm exact names/signatures by reading the C headers `c_src/src/common/fse.h`, `c_src/src/common/huf.h`, `c_src/src/common/xxhash.h`, `c_src/src/compress/hist.h`, and the implementations in `c_src/src/common/{entropy_common,fse_decompress}.c`, `c_src/src/compress/{fse_compress,huf_compress,hist}.c`, `c_src/src/decompress/huf_decompress.c`, `c_src/src/common/xxhash.c`):\n\nFSE: FSE_compress, FSE_compress2, FSE_decompress, FSE_compressBound, FSE_isError, FSE_getErrorName, FSE_normalizeCount, FSE_writeNCount, FSE_readNCount, FSE_readNCount_bmi2, FSE_optimalTableLog, FSE_optimalTableLog_internal, FSE_buildCTable, FSE_buildCTable_wksp, FSE_buildDTable_wksp (or FSE_buildDTable*), FSE_decompress_wksp, FSE_decompress_wksp_bmi2, FSE_compress_usingCTable, FSE_count* / FSE_NCountWriteBound, FSE_sizeof_CTable, FSE_createCTable/FSE_freeCTable, FSE_createDTable/FSE_freeDTable, FSE_buildCTable_raw, FSE_buildCTable_rle, FSE_buildDTable_raw, FSE_buildDTable_rle, FSE_decompress_usingDTable, FSE_compress_usingCTable_bmi2, FSE_versionNumber.\nHUF: HUF_compress, HUF_compress1X, HUF_compress1X_wksp, HUF_compress1X_usingCTable, HUF_compress2, HUF_compress4X_wksp, HUF_compress4X_repeat, HUF_compress1X_repeat, HUF_compressBound, HUF_isError, HUF_getErrorName, HUF_readStats, HUF_readStats_wksp, HUF_readCTable, HUF_writeCTable_wksp, HUF_buildCTable, HUF_buildCTable_wksp, HUF_optimalTableLog, HUF_estimateCompressedSize, HUF_validateCTable, HUF_getNbBits / HUF_getNbBitsFromCTable, HUF_decompress, HUF_decompress1X1, HUF_decompress1X2, HUF_decompress4X1, HUF_decompress4X2, HUF_decompress1X_DCtx, HUF_decompress4X_hufOnly*, HUF_decompress1X1_DCtx_wksp, HUF_decompress4X_usingDTable*, HUF_readDTableX1*/X2*, HUF_selectDecoder, HUF_decompress*_usingDTable_bmi2 — whatever the .so actually exports (check with `nm -D --defined-only c_src/build/libzstd.so | grep -E '^.* (FSE|HUF|HIST|ZSTD_XXH)'`).\nHIST: HIST_count, HIST_count_simple, HIST_count_wksp, HIST_countFast, HIST_countFast_wksp, HIST_isError.\nXXHASH (namespaced ZSTD_): ZSTD_XXH32, ZSTD_XXH64, ZSTD_XXH32_createState/freeState/reset/update/digest/copyState, ZSTD_XXH64_* equivalents, ZSTD_XXH32_canonicalFromHash/hashFromCanonical, ZSTD_XXH64_canonicalFromHash/hashFromCanonical, ZSTD_XXH_versionNumber, and any ZSTD_XXH3_* if exported.\n\nREQUIREMENTS:\n- Property-style randomized testing with FIXED seeds. Many inputs per function (dozens+), not one hand-picked value.\n- Cover input SHAPES and SIZES: empty (0), 1 byte, 2, 3, 7/8/9, powers of two, sizes around FSE/HUF internal limits, large (>64KB), and all `ALL_SHAPES` distributions. Single-symbol input (RLE), 2-symbol, full 256-symbol alphabet, and highly skewed histograms are important — FSE/HUF special-case these.\n- Cover PARAMETER axes: maxSymbolValue (0, 1, 2, 127, 255, and out-of-range like 256/65535), tableLog (below FSE_MIN_TABLELOG, at min, typical, at FSE_MAX_TABLELOG, above max), and HUF tableLog variants (including HUF_TABLELOG_MAX and above).\n- ERROR PATHS (mandatory): dstCapacity too small (sweep 0..exact), srcSize==0, NULL pointers where the C tolerates/checks them, maxSymbolValue too large, tableLog too large, corrupted/ bit-flipped compressed input to FSE_decompress/HUF_decompress*, workspace too small for the *_wksp variants. Assert the SAME error code (use FSE_isError/HUF_isError + the numeric return), not merely \"both failed\".\n- For xxhash: streaming (reset/update in randomized chunk splits/digest) must equal one-shot, and must match C bit-for-bit; also cover seeds 0/1/max and canonical round trips.\n- For byte-output functions compare the FULL output buffer contents byte-for-byte, and also compare untouched bytes beyond the written length are treated consistently (compare only the written prefix if the C leaves the tail undefined — be careful not to create false failures from genuinely-undefined tail bytes; if you find a case where the C leaves tail bytes untouched, only compare the reported length).\n- Be careful with functions taking opaque table pointers (FSE_CTable*/HUF_CElt*): allocate with the documented size macros, and build the table with the SAME library that will consume it, then ALSO cross-check that C-built tables and Rust-built tables are byte-identical (that is a strong equality check).\n\nIF YOU FIND A DIVERGENCE: fix the RUST source in `translation/src/**` (never c_src). Root-cause it by reading the corresponding C. Rebuild and re-run until green. Report every divergence you fixed with file+what was wrong.\n\nIterate until `timeout 600 cargo test --release --offline --test t05_entropy`