oints regardless.\n\nSCOPE t08_legacy — read `c_src/src/legacy/zstd_v0{1..7}.{h,c}` and enumerate exported symbols with:\n`nm -D --defined-only c_src/build/libzstd.so | grep -E ' (ZSTDv0|ZBUFFv0|FSEv0|HUFv0)'`\nFor each version v01..v07 cover its full exported surface, e.g. ZSTDv0X_decompress, ZSTDv0X_getDecompressedSize / ZSTDv0X_findFrameSizeInfoLegacy, ZSTDv0X_isError, ZSTDv0X_getErrorName, ZSTDv0X_createDCtx/freeDCtx, ZSTDv0X_decompressDCtx, ZSTDv0X_decompressBegin/decompressContinue/nextSrcSizeToDecompress, ZSTDv0X_magicNumber / ZSTDv07_isFrame etc. Also the FSEv0X_/HUFv0X_ exports if present.\nKEY CHALLENGE: you cannot easily produce valid v01..v07 frames (this library only *writes* the current format). So drive these functions with: (a) random bytes, (b) buffers starting with each version's magic number followed by random/structured payloads, (c) current-format zstd frames, (d) truncations and bit-flips of all of the above, (e) empty and 1-byte inputs. The REQUIREMENT is that C and Rust agree exactly on the return value/error code for every such input — this is a very effective differential test for the legacy parsers. Use many randomized inputs with fixed seeds. Also fuzz the streaming decompressBegin/nextSrcSizeToDecompress/decompressContinue state machines with randomized chunk feeding, asserting the returned sizes/errors match step by step.\nAlso test `ZSTD_isFrame`, `ZSTD_getFrameContentSize`, `ZSTD_findFrameCompressedSize` and `ZSTD_decompress` on legacy-magic inputs, since zstd_legacy.h dispatches to these decoders from the main API.\n\nSCOPE t09_zbuff — read `c_src/src/deprecated/zbuff.h` and `c_src/src/deprecated/zbuff_{common,compress,decompress}.c`. Cover: ZBUFF_createCCtx(+_advanced), ZBUFF_freeCCtx, ZBUFF_compressInit, ZBUFF_compressInitDictionary, ZBUFF_compressContinue, ZBUFF_compressFlush, ZBUFF_compressEnd, ZBUFF_recommendedCInSize, ZBUFF_recommendedCOutSize, ZBUFF_createDCtx(+_advanced), ZBUFF_freeDCtx, ZBUFF_decompressInit, ZBUFF_decompressInitDictionary, ZBUFF_decompressContinue, ZBUFF_recommendedDInSize, ZBUFF_recommendedDOutSize, ZBUFF_isError, ZBUFF_getErrorName.\nDrive the FULL streaming state machine: init -> repeated compressContinue with randomized input chunk sizes and randomized output buffer sizes (including tiny/1-byte output buffers that force partial flushes) -> compressFlush -> compressEnd. Assert at EVERY step that both libs return the same code AND consume/produce the same number of bytes AND emit identical bytes. Then decompress with ZBUFF_decompressContinue in randomized chunks and assert the same. Cover: all compression levels, dictionaries (incl. empty and large dicts), 0-byte input, input larger than one block, calling functions out of order (e.g. compressContinue before init, decompressContinue before init) which must produce the same error in both, and NULL/zero-size buffers.\n\nREQUIREMENTS for both files:\n- Deterministic FIXED seeds; MANY randomized inputs per scenario (hundreds where cheap).\n- Always compare the numeric return AND the error name/code, not just \"both failed\".\n- Compare produced bytes byte-for-byte over the reported produced length.\n- Keep each file's runtime well under 300s.\n\nIF YOU FIND A DIVERGENCE: fix the RUST source in `translation/src/**` (never c_src), root-caused against the C. Rebuild and re-run until green.\n\nIterate until BOTH `--test t08_legacy` and `--test t09_zbuff` pass. Report: both file paths, #[test] counts, symbols exercised, final pass/fail for each, and every Rust bug you fixed (file + root cause)."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1802,"cache_read_input_tokens":84785,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1802,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"73cb0b47-bb13-46d2-9cdb-cbadffb29d99","uuid":"73d42a91-4ad6-4e60-bfc7-d140de1cc774","tim