TDv07_decompressContinue error on buffered input | forwarded ZSTD_error_* code | legacy/zstd_v07.c:4444-4447`\n`ZBUFFv07_decompressContinue | zbd->stage outside ZBUFFds_* enum | GENERIC (1) | legacy/zstd_v07.c:4472`\n`ZBUFFv07_isError | errorCode > ERROR(maxCode) | 1 else 0 | legacy/zstd_v07.c:2570`\n`ZBUFFv07_getErrorName | any errorCode; never NULL | const char* | legacy/zstd_v07.c:2572`\n`ZBUFFv07_recommendedDInSize | no rejection branch | ZSTDv07_BLOCKSIZE_ABSOLUTEMAX + ZSTDv07_blockHeaderSize | legacy/zstd_v07.c:4489`\n`ZBUFFv07_recommendedDOutSize | no rejection branch | ZSTDv07_BLOCKSIZE_ABSOLUTEMAX | legacy/zstd_v07.c:4490`\n\n---\n\n## Cross-version asymmetries worth flagging for a port\n\n1. **`ZBUFFv05_createDCtx` does not check `ZSTDv05_createDCtx()`** (`zstd_v05.c:3809`), while v06 (`:3922-3925`) and v07 (`:4300`) both check and return NULL. A v05 stream context can be handed back with `zbc->zc == NULL`.\n2. **`ZSTDv07_freeDDict` has no NULL guard** (`zstd_v07.c:4180`) although `ZSTDv07_freeDCtx` (`:2946`), `ZBUFFv05_freeDCtx` (`:3816`), `ZBUFFv06_freeDCtx` (`:3932`), `ZBUFFv07_freeDCtx` (`:4307`) all do.\n3. **v06/v07 collapse many distinct header errors into `corruption_detected` (20)** at `zstd_v06.c:3523` / `zstd_v07.c:3758` (`if (ZSTDv0X_decodeFrameHeader(...)) return ERROR(corruption_detected)`), whereas v05 propagates the real code (`zstd_v05.c:3391`). Notably `dictionary_wrong` (32) from `zstd_v07.c:3186` is invisible through the one-shot API.\n4. **`ZSTDv0X_decompress_usingDict` all three discard `decompressBegin_usingDict`'s return** (`v05:3450`, `v06:3582`, `v07:3825`), so a corrupt dictionary silently proceeds.\n5. **`ZBUFFv06_decompressContinue` computes `toLoad = hSize - zbd->lhSize` before testing `ZSTDv06_isError(hSize)`** (`zstd_v06.c:3990-3991`); v07 tests first (`zstd_v07.c:4364-4365`).\n6. **RLE blocks**: v07's one-shot frame loop supports `bt_rle` via `ZSTDv07_generateNxBytes` (`:3782`), but v07's streaming `decompressContinue` rejects it with `GENERIC` (`:4000`). v05/v06 reject `bt_rle` in both paths.\n7. **`ZSTDv07_copyRawBlock` lacks the `dst==NULL` check** present in `ZSTDv05_copyRawBlock` (`:2801`) and `ZSTDv06_copyRawBlock` (`:2989`).\n8. **`ZSTD_initLegacyStream` returns 0 (success) for unsupported versions 1-4** (`zstd_legacy.h:314-319`) while `ZSTD_decompressLegacyStream` returns `version_unsupported` (12) for the same versions (`:382-387`) — an init that \"succeeds\" leaves `*legacyContext` untouched.","usage":{"total_tokens":145431,"tool_uses":59,"duration_ms":467017},"uuid":"a3961d3e-0358-4848-a63c-8569d0f6752d","session_id":"73cb0b47-bb13-46d2-9cdb-cbadffb29d99"}
