eset` | any valid `statePtr` | `XXH_OK` (0) — unconditional | `common/xxhash.h:3571` | [ ] |\n| 602 | `ZSTD_XXH64_update` | `input == NULL` (any `len`) | `XXH_OK` (0) early return, state untouched; `NULL`+`len>0` silently ignored, not rejected | `common/xxhash.h:3574-3578` | [ ] |\n| 603 | `ZSTD_XXH64_update` | `state == NULL` with `input != NULL` | **no NULL check** — `state->total_len += len` = UB | `common/xxhash.h:3583` | [ ] |\n| 604 | `ZSTD_XXH64_update` | `state` never `reset` | no init/stage check; garbage hash, no error | `common/xxhash.h:3573-3620` | [ ] |\n| 605 | `ZSTD_XXH64_update` | valid arguments (both early-returns and the fall-through) | `XXH_OK` (0) on every path — `XXH_ERROR` unreachable | `common/xxhash.h:3577`, `:3588`, `:3620` | [ ] |\n| 606 | `ZSTD_XXH64_digest` | `state == NULL` | **no NULL check** — `state->total_len` deref = UB | `common/xxhash.h:3624-3641` | [ ] |\n| 607 | `ZSTD_XXH64_digest` | state never `reset`; note the tail length passed on is `(size_t)state->total_len`, masked to `&31` inside `XXH64_finalize` | no error possible (return type is a plain hash) | `common/xxhash.h:3640`, `:3439-3441` | [ ] |\n| 608 | `ZSTD_XXH64_canonicalFromHash` | `dst == NULL` — **no NULL check** | UB (`void` return) | `common/xxhash.h:3647-3652` | [ ] |\n| 609 | `ZSTD_XXH64_canonicalFromHash` | `sizeof(XXH64_canonical_t) != sizeof(XXH64_hash_t)` | compile-time `XXH_STATIC_ASSERT`, not runtime | `common/xxhash.h:3649` | [ ] |\n| 610 | `ZSTD_XXH64_hashFromCanonical` | `src == NULL` — **no NULL check**, `XXH_readBE64(src)` | UB; all 8-byte inputs are valid hashes | `common/xxhash.h:3655-3658` | [ ] |\n| 611 | any `ZSTD_XXH3_*` / `ZSTD_XXH128*` name | called across the FFI boundary | **link error / unresolved symbol** — the entire XXH3 family is excluded by the forced `XXH_NO_XXH3` | `common/xxhash.h:14-16`, `:3664`, `:7089` | [ ] |\nEOF\nwc -l translation/ERRORS.md","description":"Append section M"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_detai