{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_cfcwilsgcqnvd5jwvpt5gucudisnvfxarxaf5e5ihtku2yuxpxfq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01CfDaWk7BRzxB49n73eL5Ug","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-iPPPON/translation/tests/t05_entropy.rs","old_string":"/// 8-byte aligned scratch buffer with a deterministic fill so that \"untouched\"\n/// tail bytes are identical between the two libraries and a full-buffer\n/// comparison stays meaningful.\nfn abuf(bytes: usize, fill: u8) -> Vec<u64> {\n    let n = (bytes + 7) / 8;\n    vec![u64::from_ne_bytes([fill; 8]); n.max(1)]\n}","new_string":"/// 8-byte aligned scratch buffer with a deterministic fill so that \"untouched\"\n/// tail bytes are identical between the two libraries and a full-buffer\n/// comparison stays meaningful.\n///\n/// `ABUF_SLACK` extra bytes are always allocated beyond the requested size: the\n/// C's own `FSE_BUILD_CTABLE_WORKSPACE_SIZE` macro rounds *down* (`(msv+2+\n/// tableSize)/2`) and `FSE_buildCTable_wksp` then `MEM_write64`s up to two bytes\n/// past the advertised size for odd `maxSymbolValue`. The slack keeps the\n/// harness memory-safe while still letting us hand the library the exact\n/// *declared* size, which is what the error paths key off. Comparing the slack\n/// region too means an over-write that differs between the two libraries still\n/// shows up as a failure.\nconst ABUF_SLACK: usize = 64;\n\nfn abuf(bytes: usize, fill: u8) -> Vec<u64> {\n    let n = (bytes + ABUF_SLACK + 7) / 8;\n    vec![u64::from_ne_bytes([fill; 8]); n.max(1)]\n}"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9419,"cache_read_input_tokens":182638,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":9419,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"pare