{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_wruzqxgrnhfg7oeldoihug7cjdzylncapsqdbec4qjzz233y3g4a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Final state: **19 `#[test]` functions, all passing**, ~62 s wall clock.\n\n## File\n`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-iPPPON/translation/tests/t07_dictbuilder.rs` (3196 lines). No file under `c_src/` or `translation/src/` was touched.\n\n## Result\n`timeout 600 cargo test --release --offline --test t07_dictbuilder` → `test result: ok. 19 passed; 0 failed` in **61.6 s**. Run twice back-to-back with byte-identical results.\n\n## Symbols exercised (all 26 dictBuilder exports of both `.so`s)\n`ZDICT_trainFromBuffer`, `_legacy`, `_cover`, `_fastCover`, `ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_cover`, `_fastCover`, `ZDICT_finalizeDictionary`, `ZDICT_addEntropyTablesFromBuffer`, `ZDICT_getDictID`, `ZDICT_getDictHeaderSize`, `ZDICT_isError`, `ZDICT_getErrorName`, `COVER_sum`, `COVER_computeEpochs`, `COVER_warnOnSmallCorpus`, `COVER_checkTotalCompressedSize`, `COVER_selectDict`, `COVER_dictSelectionError/IsError/Free`, `COVER_best_init/start/finish/wait/destroy`. Plus `ZSTD_compress_usingDict` / `ZSTD_decompress_usingDict` / `ZSTD_getDictID_fromDict` for usability checks. (`COVER_buildDictionary` is `static` in cover.c and not exported — confirmed via `nm -D`.)\n\nCoverage includes: 0/1/2/5/7/10/50/200/500-sample corpora; 0-byte, 1-byte, uniform and wildly-varying sample sizes; totals below and above `ZDICT_MIN_SAMPLES_SIZE`/`MAX(d,8)`; all 8 `Shape`s in both shared-substring and independent variants; `dictBufferCapacity` sweeps from 0 through 110 KB; full `k`/`d`/`f`/`steps`/`accel`/`splitPoint`(incl. NaN)/`nbThreads`/`shrinkDict`/`compressionLevel`/`dictID`/`notificationLevel 0..4` axes; every documented error path asserted against the *exact* numeric `ZSTD_ErrorCode` (42/70/72), not just C-vs-Rust parity; plus a 5000-iteration fixed-seed randomized cross-product fuzz. Every produced dictionary is additionally byte-compared and round-tripped cross-library.\n\n## Rust bugs fixed\n**None** — the Rust port matched the C on every one of the ~100k comparisons. No `translation/src/**` change was needed.\n\n## Assertions weakened\n**None.** Every success path asserts full byte equality. Two things are worth flagging:\n\n1. **Determinism was verified empirically, not assumed.** Test 18 `same_library_results_are_deterministic` calls all seven trainers twice *within the same library* (C twice, Rust twice) and requires bit-identical dictionaries and `*parameters` write-backs. It passes, which is the evidence that byte-equality is legitimate. (`dictID` auto mode is `XXH64(dictContent)` at zdict.c:879, not a PRNG; the only `clock()` uses are `DISPLAYUPDATE` stderr throttles; no `ZSTD_MULTITHREAD` so `nbThreads<=1` keeps `optimize*` sequential.)\n\n2. **One real nondeterminism source found and fixed properly, not papered over.** `cover.c:67` / `fastcover.c:54` keep a *file-static* `g_displayLevel` that `optimize*` copies back into the caller's `parameters->zParams.notificationLevel` (cover.c:1264). Because `cargo test` runs `#[test]` fns on parallel threads, a concurrent test's `notificationLevel` leaked into another's output — nondeterministic *within a single library*. Fixed with a process-wide mutex (`display_level_lock()`) held by the 12 tests that reach the COVER/FASTCOVER trainers, so assertions stay at full byte equality.\n\n## Upstream C defect worked around (not tested)\n`ZDICT_trainFromBuffer` with 10 one-byte samples **kills the process with SIGFPE inside `c_src/build/libzstd.so`**. Root cause: `COVER_ctx_init`/`FASTCOVER_ctx_init` validate the *total* sample size against `MAX(d,8)` (cover.c:614, fastcover.c:328) but derive the dmer count from the *training* subset (cover.c:642, fastcover.c:359). When `splitPoint<1` shrinks training to exactly `MAX(d,8)-1` bytes, the count becomes 0 and `COVER_computeEpochs` evaluates `nbDmers / epochs.size` with `epochs.size==0` (cover.c:719). The Rust port reproduces this faithfully. Since the C is ground truth and it aborts, `cover_input_is_safe()` filters these inputs out of the fuzz with the analysis documented in-place."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":169,"cache_read_input_tokens":226953,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":169,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01RUHBTGsvDTu3wkCWYcgZdT","session_id":"73cb0b47-bb13-46d2-9cdb-cbadffb29d99","uuid":"64d2ea91-8bc6-435e-be09-5943628645a8","timestamp":"2026-08-31T11:07:00.979Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"DictBuilder differential tests"}
