{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_5v565pvua6z3saj5vzlym55mngpdhr35ald3xpcm3wl26rbn2hga","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both suites are green. Final verification run passes.\n\n## Files\n\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-iPPPON/translation/tests/t08_legacy.rs` — 2242 lines, **18 `#[test]`s**, PASS (18/18, ~1.0 s)\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-iPPPON/translation/tests/t09_zbuff.rs` — 1530 lines, **10 `#[test]`s**, PASS (10/10, ~3.2 s)\n\nBoth load `c_src/build/libzstd.so` and `translation/target/release/libzstd.so` via `libloading` through the shared `tests/common/mod.rs` harness (`impls().pair::<T>(sym)`, `Rng`, `Shape`/`gen_shape`, `assert_bytes_eq`, `assert_eq_dbg`). No Rust function is called directly.\n\n## Symbol coverage\n\nI enumerated all 227 `ZSTDv0*`/`ZBUFFv0*`/`FSEv0*`/`HUFv0*`/`ZBUFF_*` exports with `nm -D` (the two `.so`s export **identical** sets) and every one of the 227 is exercised. Highlights:\n\n- **t08**: `ZSTDv0{1..7}_{decompress, findFrameSizeInfoLegacy, isError, getErrorName, createDCtx, freeDCtx, decompressDCtx, resetDCtx, decompressBegin, decompressBegin_usingDict, decompress_usingDict, decompress_usingPreparedDCtx, copyDCtx, decompressBlock, decompressContinue, nextSrcSizeToDecompress, getFrameParams, sizeofDCtx, estimateDCtxSize}`, `ZSTDv07_{getDecompressedSize, createDDict, freeDDict, decompress_usingDDict, createDCtx_advanced, insertBlock, isSkipFrame}`, `ZBUFFv0{4..7}_*` (buffered streaming incl. `decompressWithDictionary`/`decompressInitDictionary`, `recommendedD{In,Out}Size`), `FSEv0{5,6,7}_*` (readNCount, create/free/buildDTable, buildDTable_raw/_rle, decompress, decompress_usingDTable), `HUFv0{5,6,7}_*` (readStats, selectDecoder, readDTableX2/X4, all 1X/4X × 2/4 decoders, `_usingDTable`, `_DCtx`, `4X_hufOnly`), plus the main-API dispatch (`ZSTD_isFrame`, `getFrameContentSize`, `getDecompressedSize`, `findDecompressedSize`, `decompressBound`, `findFrameCompressedSize`, `decompress`, `decompressStream`+`initDStream_usingDict`) on legacy-magic input.\n- **t09**: every function listed in the scope, plus `ZBUFF_compressInit_advanced`, `ZBUFF_create{C,D}Ctx_advanced` with real custom allocators, cross-checked against `ZSTD_CStreamInSize`/`CStreamOutSize`/`DStreamInSize`/`DStreamOutSize`.\n\n## Approach notes\n\n- **t08** builds a deterministic ~800-entry corpus: empty/1-byte, truncated magics, random, each version's magic + random payload, *structured* frames (aligned frame header + 3-byte block-header chains), hand-built exactly-aligned raw-block frames, **literal-only `bt_compressed` frames** (`IS_RAW` literals + `nbSeq==0`) that actually decode successfully through v05/v06/v07's compressed-block path, current-format zstd frames, plus truncations and bit-flips of all of it. Streaming tests step `nextSrcSizeToDecompress`/`decompressContinue` in lock step (mostly exact feeds, 20 % deliberately wrong sizes), advancing a shared output offset to exercise the contiguity bookkeeping; a `copyDCtx` test runs the machine on a *copied*, dictionary-primed context.\n- **t09** drives init → many `compressContinue` (randomized in/out sizes incl. 0/1/2-byte outputs) → `compressFlush` to 0 → `compressEnd` to 0, asserting return code + error name + consumed + produced + bytes at every step, then re-feeds the frame through `decompressContinue`. Covers all levels from `ZSTD_minCLevel()` to `ZSTD_maxCLevel()` plus out-of-range, dictionaries (empty/1-byte/8 K/64 K/1 M/fake-dict-magic, plus wrong-dict and no-dict decode), `compressInit_advanced` with `ZSTD_getParams` output and 22 mutated/invalid parameter sets × 6 `pledgedSrcSize` values × dict/no-dict, 0-byte input, multi-block (up to 3×128 KB, one with byte-at-a-time output), NULL/zero buffers, and out-of-order misuse (continue/flush/end before init, decompressContinue before init, double end, continue after end, mid-stream re-init, decompressContinue past frame end).\n- Both files include **anti-vacuity guards** so the assertions can't silently degenerate into comparing `prefix_unknown` forever: per-version counts of inputs that get past the magic check, distinct outcomes, successful decodes, successful literal-only compressed blocks, and productive streaming steps.\n\n## Rust bugs found\n\n**None.** No divergence between the C and Rust `.so` was observed anywhere in the legacy or ZBUFF surface, so `translation/src/**` was not modified (and `c_src/` was never touched).\n\nTwo failures I hit were my own test calling the C **outside its documented preconditions** — i.e. the C original is UB there, not the Rust translation — so the tests now stay in contract and say why:\n\n1. `FSEv0X_buildDTable` with `tableLog < 5`: `FSEv05_tableStep(tableSize)` becomes a multiple of the table size, the spread loop never leaves cell 0 while the `position != 0` check still passes, and the build loop then reads uninitialised `symbolNext[]` — C and Rust legitimately returned different garbage (`0xF5EEFFF8` vs `0xC4EEFFF8`). Restricted to `tableLog >= FSE_MIN_TABLELOG`, with valid normalized-count distributions generated so the invariant holds.\n2. `HUFv07_selectDecoder(dstSize=0, ...)`: SIGFPE — the C divides by `dstSize` and indexes `algoTime[Q]` with no guard, its header stating *\"Assumption : 0 < cSrcSize < dstSize <= 128 KB\"*. Every caller in the library enforces that, so the probe now sweeps only in-contract pairs (exhaustively for small `dstSize`)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":871,"cache_read_input_tokens":318445,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":871,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_0192suTGPFT4vW4VxJLgCxsp","session_id":"73cb0b47-bb13-46d2-9cdb-cbadffb29d99","uuid":"fe4dc3a1-70e3-4822-93c8-9de7ba40c758","timestamp":"2026-08-31T11:16:52.207Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Legacy + ZBUFF differential tests"}
