_refCDict`, `ZSTD_CCtx_refPrefix{,_advanced}`, `ZSTD_CCtx_refThreadPool`, `ZSTD_DCtx_loadDictionary{,_byReference,_advanced}`, `ZSTD_DCtx_refDDict`, `ZSTD_DCtx_refPrefix{,_advanced}`, `ZSTD_DCtx_setMaxWindowSize` — plus `ZSTD_getCParams`, `ZSTD_getCParamsFromCDict`, `ZSTD_compressBegin_usingDict`, `ZSTD_compressBegin_usingCDict{,_advanced}`, `ZSTD_compressContinue/End`, `ZSTD_decompressBegin_using{Dict,DDict}`, `ZSTD_initCStream_using{Dict,CDict,CDict_advanced}`, `ZSTD_initDStream_using{Dict,DDict}`, `ZDICT_trainFromBuffer`, `ZDICT_getDictID`, `ZDICT_getDictHeaderSize`, `ZDICT_isError`. (`ZSTD_createThreadPool` is not exported by either build — no-MT build — so `refThreadPool` is tested with `NULL` and in the wrong stage.)\n\nAxes crossed: a 22-entry dictionary corpus (0-byte, 1–8-byte, raw random 64 B/1 KB/100 KB, raw text 1 KB/100 KB, real `ZDICT_trainFromBuffer` dicts at 8 KB and ~100 KB, an independently trained \"wrong\" dict, a `dictID==0` full dict, a hand-built `ZSTD_MAGIC_DICTIONARY`+garbage dict, a bit-flipped magic, three bit-flipped entropy tables) × `dct_auto/rawContent/fullDict` × `dlm_byCopy/byRef` × levels −131072…22 × all 9 strategies × `forceAttachDict` (all 4) × `enableDedicatedDictSearch` × `prefetchCDictTables` × `deterministicRefPrefix` × `dictIDFlag` × `useRowMatchFinder` × frame flags × input sizes 0…400 KB. Every combination asserts byte-identical frames, identical dictID, identical error codes, and cross-library round trips.\n\nError paths covered: NULL dict/nonzero size, nonzero dict/0 size, `dct_fullDict` refusals, `dictionary_corrupted` for bit-flipped trained dicts, out-of-range `dct`/`dlm` values (`-1000,-1,3,4,7,100,i32::MIN/MAX`) both at the setter and through to `compress2`, `initStaticCDict`/`initStaticDDict` with exact/undersized/zero workspaces, wrong-stage `loadDictionary`/`refPrefix`/`refCDict`/`refThreadPool`/`DCtx_loadDictionary`/`setMaxWindowSize` (asserted `ZSTD_error_stage_wrong`), `setMaxWindowSize` bounds sweep, single-u