{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_x6gt4r6oifpavkyhsqbgfw5iv4r3akevrqvmrvuvihhbdjkqoxea","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01K6mGfYRfiy75AxaQjn824H","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"W=/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-iPPPON; cd $W/translation\nrm -f tests/tp3.rs\npython3 - <<'PY'\np='tests/t14_gaps.rs'; s=open(p).read()\n\n# 1) RLE literal writer requires dstCapacity >= 4 (assert compiled out in C)\nold = \"\"\"                // RLE variant only makes sense for a constant run, but the C\n                // does not check that, so feed it everything.\n                let mut a = vec![0xC3u8; cap.max(1)];\"\"\"\nnew = \"\"\"                // RLE variant: the C only `assert(dstCapacity >= 4)` and then\n                // `(void)dstCapacity` (zstd_compress_literals.c:86) — with\n                // asserts compiled out (DEBUGLEVEL==0) it writes up to 4 bytes\n                // with NO runtime bound check, so `dstCapacity < 4` is undefined\n                // behaviour IN THE C and segfaults both libraries identically.\n                // Only the in-contract domain is compared.\n                if cap < 4 {\n                    continue;\n                }\n                let mut a = vec![0xC3u8; cap.max(1)];\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s = s.replace(old, new)\n\n# 2) LDM estimate needs every LDM param set, else the C divides by zero\nold = \"\"\"        vec![(ZSTD_c_enableLongDistanceMatching, 1), (ZSTD_c_ldmHashLog, 20)],\"\"\"\nnew = \"\"\"        // NOTE: LDM must be FULLY specified here. `ZSTD_estimateCCtxSize_usingCCtxParams`\n        // does not run `ZSTD_ldm_adjustParameters`, so it divides by\n        // `ldmParams.hashRateLog`; with LDM enabled but `ZSTD_c_ldmHashRateLog`\n        // left at its 0 default the C ITSELF takes SIGFPE (verified by probing\n        // the C .so alone: enabling LDM with 0, 1, 2 or 3 of the four LDM\n        // sub-params set all crash; setting all four returns cleanly).\n        vec![\n            (ZSTD_c_enableLongDistanceMatching, 1),\n            (ZSTD_c_ldmHashLog, 20),\n            (ZSTD_c_ldmBucketSizeLog, 3),\n            (ZSTD_c_ldmMinMatch, 32),\n            (ZSTD_c_ldmHashRateLog, 4),\n        ],\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s = s.replace(old, new)\n\n# 3) selectBlockCompressor table is [4][ZSTD_STRATEGY_MAX+1] -> no OOB indices\nold = \"\"\"    // every strategy (incl. out-of-range), every paramSwitch, every dictMode\n    for strat in 0i32..=10 {\n        for rmf in 0i32..=2 {\n            for dm in 0i32..=4 {\"\"\"\nnew = \"\"\"    // The C body is a raw table lookup\n    //   static const ZSTD_BlockCompressor_f blockCompressor[4][ZSTD_STRATEGY_MAX+1]\n    // (zstd_compress.c:3071) indexed directly by `dictMode` and `strat`, guarded\n    // only by an `assert()` that is compiled out in this build. Indices beyond\n    // dictMode 3 / strategy 9 therefore read PAST the array — undefined behaviour\n    // in the C, which is why the sweep stops at the real table bounds. (Strategy\n    // 0 IS in range: the table has an explicit \"default for 0\" entry.)\n    for strat in 0i32..=9 {\n        for rmf in 0i32..=2 {\n            for dm in 0i32..=3 {\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s = s.replace(old, new)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint(\"patched\")\nPY\ntimeout 600 cargo test --release --offline --test t14_gaps 2>&1 | grep -E '^error(\\[|:)|^test |test result|panicked|SIGSEGV' | head -20","description":"Apply three precondition fixes and rerun t14","timeout":600000}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1945,"cache_read_input_tokens":387317,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1945,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"73cb0b47-bb13-46d2-9cdb-cbadffb29d99","uuid":"a5531c03-b84e-4d97-91e8-4545eb956373","timestamp":"202