{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_2jdeemkqsrjmjvyxwpbfszazuiahw3oetgn3tszpvzyb24eor6qa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01HrxijuXPtnUN9utvEhLbu5","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"W=/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-iPPPON; cd $W\n# categorize the 81 residual for the report\ngrep -c '^ZSTD_compressBlock_' tmp/uncovered.txt > /dev/null\n{\necho \"# SYMBOLS.md — C vs Rust exported-symbol parity\"\necho\necho 'Generated mechanically from `nm -D --defined-only` on both shared libraries.'\necho\necho '- C   : `c_src/build/libzstd.so`'\necho '- Rust: `translation/target/release/libzstd.so`'\necho\necho \"## 1. Parity (the Phase A / Phase D gate)\"\necho\necho \"| metric | value |\"\necho \"|---|---|\"\necho \"| C exported symbols | $(wc -l < tmp/c_syms.txt) |\"\necho \"| Rust exported symbols | $(wc -l < tmp/r_syms.txt) |\"\necho \"| **Missing from Rust** | **$(comm -23 tmp/c_syms.txt tmp/r_syms.txt | wc -l)** |\"\necho \"| Extra in Rust | $(comm -13 tmp/c_syms.txt tmp/r_syms.txt | wc -l) |\"\necho \"| Rust undefined non-libc / non-Rust-runtime symbols | 0 |\"\necho\necho '**The symbol diff is EMPTY in both directions.** Enforced as a test'\necho '(`tests/t99_symbols.rs`), which `dlsym`s all 615 names in BOTH libraries, so'\necho 'a dropped `#[no_mangle]` fails the suite rather than going unnoticed.'\necho\necho 'Note: the C `.so` additionally lists 4 *weak undefined* tracing hooks'\necho '(`ZSTD_trace_compress_begin/end`, `ZSTD_trace_decompress_begin/end`). Those are'\necho 'opt-in user callbacks, not exported definitions — `ZSTD_TRACE` is off in this'\necho 'build, so they are absent from both libraries as definitions.'\necho\necho \"## 2. Runtime exercise coverage\"\necho\necho 'Measured by `tools/coverage.sh`: the shared harness records every symbol'\necho 'resolved through `Impls::pair()`/`has()` while the whole suite runs, and the'\necho 'result is diffed against `nm