{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_gqtk3hotcmfnp5tlm5mxvln4omru2ufql33c5mtmfj2sokpi5gla","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. **The Rust translation is byte-identical to the C on every input tested — no Rust bug was found and `translation/src/**` needed no changes.**\n\n## Completion gate\n\n| Gate | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `nm -D`: 0 missing/extra symbols in Rust | **PASS** — 615 vs 615, diff empty both ways; 0 undefined non-libc |\n| Every `CONFIGS.md` row covered | **PASS** — 849 rows: 756 direct, 93 indirect, 0 unmarked |\n| Every `ERRORS.md` row covered | **PASS** — 1227 rows: 817 direct, 409 indirect, 1 n/a, 0 unmarked |\n| Holds under every feature combination | **PASS (vacuous)** — `Cargo.toml` has no `[features]`; one configuration |\n\n**161 tests across 17 files, 0 failures.** All calls go through `dlsym` on both `.so`s, so the `#[no_mangle]` wrappers and struct-by-value ABI are under test.\n\n## What I found\n\n**No divergences.** ~10⁶ comparisons of compressed frames, entropy tables, suffix arrays, sequence arrays, streaming call traces and error codes all matched exactly. `c_src/` untouched (0 files modified).\n\nThe real work was **separating genuine divergences from C-side undefined behaviour**. `DEBUGLEVEL == 0` compiles out zstd's asserts, so 15 functions have unchecked preconditions. Each time a test crashed I probed the C `.so` *alone* first — in every case the C also crashed or returned garbage, so these were my test inputs escaping the contract, not translation bugs. Examples:\n\n- `ZSTD_compressRleLiteralsBlock` only `assert`s `dstCapacity >= 4` then does `(void)dstCapacity` — segfaults in **both** libraries below that.\n- `ZSTD_estimateCCtxSize_usingCCtxParams` divides by `ldmParams.hashRateLog` without running `ZSTD_ldm_adjustParameters`: SIGFPE in the C unless all four `ZSTD_c_ldm*` params are set.\n- `ZSTD_get1BlockSummary` leaves `blockSize`/`litSize` **unassigned** on its error path, so the C returns stack garbage — only `nbSequences` is meaningful there.\n\nEach is documented inline with the `file:line` citation and the probe evidence.\n\nI also caught **three bugs in my own harness** that would have made tests pass vacuously — most notably an undersized output buffer that made both libraries \"agree\" on a *truncated* frame. `t00_meta` and several inline guards now exist specifically to prevent that class of false pass.\n\n## Two caveats worth your attention\n\n1. **534/615 symbols are called directly.** The other 81 take private struct types (`ZSTD_MatchState_t*`, `SeqStore_t*`, `ZSTD_CCtx_params*`, …) with no public layout, so no external caller can construct valid arguments; they're covered only indirectly through the public API. `SYMBOLS.md` §3 justifies this group by group — it's a real limit on directness, not full equivalence.\n2. **The `[i]` checkbox state is mine, not the spec's.** Rows naming `static` helpers or wire-format states have no callable symbol, so I marked them `[i]` (covered indirectly) rather than `[x]`, with a legend in both files. 409 of 1227 `ERRORS.md` rows are `[i]` — a reviewer wanting strict `[x]`-only coverage should read those as weaker evidence than the direct ones.\n\nArtifacts: `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `VERIFICATION.md`, `run_tests.sh`, `tools/coverage.sh`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1055,"cache_read_input_tokens":480288,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1055,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"73cb0b47-bb13-46d2-9cdb-cbadffb29d99","uuid":"2aa7f097-fd77-47ab-882a-5d029979d419","timestamp":"2026-08-31T12:01:45.877Z"}
